_JOBS = json.loads(r"""[{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/billionbody/remote-job/senior-full-stack-developer","title":"Senior Full-Stack Developer","company":"Billion Body","location":"Remote","description":"We're an ultra-premium health performance company serving elite founders and UHNW individuals globally. We install biological operating systems \u2014 combining world-class physicians, functional medicine, precision diagnostics, and direct access to our founder's network.\nWe are building the software infrastructure that powers this model. It does not exist yet. We are building it from scratch, and we need the engineer who can architect it correctly from day one \u2014 because what we are building in stage one has to be compatible with what we are building in stage six.\nThe Product \nThis is not a health dashboard. It is a longitudinal health intelligence system \u2014 a multi-stage platform that tracks, correlates, and predicts health outcomes for UHNW clients. The stages:\nStage 1 (MVP): Mobile-first client app with daily and weekly check-in prompts, API integrations with Whoop, Oura, and Apple Health, progress photo uploads, compliance visualisation, and push notifications.\nStage 2: Client portal with protocol delivery, daily and weekly schedule builder, monthly/yearly calendar view, and calendar integration.\nStage 3: Progress mapping, monthly/weekly scoring, and diagnostic visualisation \u2014 tracking health trajectory against protocol adherence.\nStage 4: Supplement database with biomarker tagging, click-to-purchase automation, automated repurchase triggers, and delivery tracking.\nStage 5+: Correlative health data engine \u2014 isolating variables across biomarkers, supplements, training, and outcomes to identify what is actually driving each client's results.\nThe architecture you build at stage one must be designed with stages four through six already in mind. This is not optional.\nWhat You Will Build First \nMobile app (iOS + Android): Daily/weekly check-in flows, Whoop/Oura/Apple Health integrations, progress photo upload, compliance dashboards, push notifications.\nBackend: Physician and operator dashboard, client onboarding pipelines, protocol delivery logic, auditable data flows.\nWebsite: Public-facing site as a parallel workstream alongside the Growth Operations Manager.\nThe Technical Challenge \nNo vibe coding. ERD-first. Every schema decision must account for the data relationships stages four and five will require. The data model must support longitudinal records with correlative queries. The supplement database needs biomarker tagging from day one. Check-in data feeds into progress scoring feeds into the correlative engine \u2014 one architecture.\nTech Stack \nFull autonomy. Preferences: React Native or Flutter (mobile), Node.js / Python FastAPI (backend), PostgreSQL + Supabase with RLS + pgvector (database), AWS or Vercel + Docker + CI/CD (infrastructure). Figma Pro and GitHub Pro provided. GoDaddy is not acceptable.\nNon-Negotiables \nProven track record shipping mobile apps to the App Store and Play Store \u2014 links required\nStrong backend and database skills \u2014 you start with the ERD, not the feature\nExperience building systems that scale across multiple feature stages without reconstruction\nSelf-directed \u2014 no PM, no hand-holding\nStrong written English \u2014 remote, async, documentation-first\nYears of experience is not the filter. Architecture thinking and shipped mobile products are.\nStrong Preference For \nWearable platform integration (Apple HealthKit, Whoop, Oura)\nHealth, biotech, or data-sensitive application background\nHIPAA or GDPR-regulated environment experience\nLongitudinal data modelling or time-series database experience\nFast-moving startup where you owned the full stack\nWhat We Offer \nFully remote \u2014 anywhere in the world\n$2,500 \u2013 $4,500/month based on experience\n12 days paid time off per year\nDirect line to the founder\nA product that does not exist yet, built correctly from the start\nHow to Apply \nApply here: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc68P3BGYX8dLsXFb-wvsezIXC1k8K45_yxfHVc9IRgAhQ4IQ/viewform \nEvery application is reviewed personally. You will hear from us within 5\u20137 business days if your profile is a match.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Canada","United States","Afghanistan","Armenia","Azerbaijan","Bahrain","Bangladesh","Bhutan","Brunei Darussalam","Cambodia","China","Democratic People's Republic of Korea","Georgia","Hong Kong (China)","India","Indonesia","Iran","Iraq","Israel","Japan","Jordan","Kazakhstan","Kuwait","Kyrgyzstan","Lao People's Democratic Republic","Lebanon","Macao (China)","Malaysia","Maldives","Mongolia","Myanmar","Nepal","Oman","Pakistan","Philippines","Qatar","Russian Federation","Saudi Arabia","Singapore","South Korea","Sri Lanka","State of Palestine","Syrian Arab Republic","Taiwan","Tajikistan","Thailand","Timor-Leste","Turkmenistan","United Arab Emirates","Uzbekistan","Viet Nam","Yemen"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-10T16:09:54.455Z","expires_at":"2026-08-09T16:09:54.455Z","external_id":"billionbody","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/stubgroup/remote-job/senior-email-marketing-specialist-remote-work-from-home","title":"Senior Email Marketing Specialist - Remote (Work from Home)","company":"StubGroup","location":"Remote","description":"Who We Are \nStubGroup is a remote digital marketing agency that has helped SMBs grow for nearly 15 years through strong marketing strategy and execution. We are also a Premier Google Partner, and we work with businesses across local/home services, professional services, lead-generation SMBs, and ecommerce.\nWe care about doing thoughtful, high-quality work that actually helps clients grow. We are not interested in checkbox email marketing or templated deliverables. We want people who take ownership, think clearly, and care about results.\nAbout the Role \nWe're hiring a Senior Email Marketing Specialist to own email and lifecycle marketing across a portfolio of client accounts.\nThis is a senior, hands-on role. You will not just plan campaigns and hand the work off to someone else. You will be expected to think strategically, prioritize well, and directly build, launch, and optimize a meaningful share of the work yourself.\nYou'll own email strategy and execution across campaigns, automated flows, segmentation, list growth, deliverability, and reporting. You'll build in the client's ESP (Klaviyo, Mailchimp, HubSpot, ActiveCampaign, and similar), write and edit copy, set up and test flows, and use data to drive real improvements in open rates, click rates, and conversions.\nWe also want someone who is eager to embrace AI in practical, thoughtful ways: actively experimenting with AI tools, rethinking workflows, and finding ways to do better work more efficiently. Strong email fundamentals matter most, but you should already be using AI to improve parts of your workflow without sacrificing quality or judgment.\nThis is not a role for someone who was great at email five years ago and stopped evolving. If you get genuinely curious when deliverability rules or platform features change, and you've been incorporating AI into your work in meaningful ways, we want to hear from you.\nWhat You'll Do \nOwn email and lifecycle strategy and execution across an assigned portfolio of client accounts\nPlan, build, and launch campaigns and automated flows (welcome, abandoned cart, post-purchase, win-back, nurture, and more)\nDevelop segmentation strategies and manage list growth, hygiene, and re-engagement\nWrite and edit compelling email copy and subject lines, and improve on what already exists\nSet up and manage A/B tests, then act on the results\nMonitor and improve deliverability, sender reputation, and inbox placement\nBuild reporting that clearly connects email performance to revenue and client goals\nDirectly implement the majority of the work inside client ESPs and related tools\nSupport upsell conversations for current clients when your expertise can help uncover or explain opportunities\nStay current on email best practices, platform changes, and useful AI applications for the work\nWhat We're Looking For \n3+ years of hands-on email marketing experience in an agency or multi-client environment\nProven ability to own email strategy and execution across multiple client accounts\nStrong track record of improving email performance (engagement, deliverability, and revenue) through sound strategy and solid execution\nDeep comfort with at least one major ESP (Klaviyo, HubSpot, Mailchimp, ActiveCampaign, or similar), and the ability to learn new platforms quickly\nStrong skills in automation, segmentation, A/B testing, and deliverability\nStrong copywriting and editing ability: you can write email that is clear, on-brand, and converts\nComfort working with analytics and connecting email metrics to business outcomes\nFluent, professional written and verbal English. You will represent client brands and communicate directly with U.S. clients\nAgency-tested judgment: you can prioritize well, work independently, and manage competing account needs without constant oversight\nThoughtful, practical use of AI in your workflow, with the judgment to know when to trust it and when not to\nComfort working remotely and primarily during U.S. business hours (9:00 am - 5:00 pm Central Time)\nWhat We Offer \nFully remote, work-from-home role\nUnlimited PTO\n$3,500 - $5,000 per month, based on experience\nReal ownership over your client work\nA team that values high standards, thoughtful strategy, caring for our clients, and doing work that actually matters\nHow to Apply \nEmail the following to john+email+hiring@stubgroup.com :\nYour resume\nTell us about an email campaign or automated flow you built that didn't perform the way you wanted. What was underperforming, how did you diagnose the problem, what specifically did you change, and what happened to the numbers afterward? Include the actual metrics if you can.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Canada","United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-09T18:29:58.317Z","expires_at":"2026-08-08T18:29:58.317Z","external_id":"stubgroup","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/novantro/remote-job/coo","title":"COO","company":"Novantro","location":"Remote","description":"Novantro is a Reddit marketing agency helping B2B brands get recommended by AI tools like ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini. We've served 70+ US clients across SaaS, home services, and finance. We're currently at $60k/mo and scaling to $100k/mo with a small, lean, fully remote team.\nThe founder built this from zero in 18 months and is now stepping back from day-to-day operations to focus on growth. This role exists so that when he steps back, nothing breaks and everything gets better. \nWhat you'll own \nClient delivery: every campaign ships on time and at quality. You work directly with our Head of Reddit and content team to make that true every single week.\nTeam management: coordinating a remote team of 5+ (delivery, sales, contractors) across time zones. Keeping people accountable without the founder in the loop.\nSystems: running and improving our stack: Close CRM, Make.com automations, Calendly, Slack, Stripe. If a workflow breaks at 2x volume, you catch it before it breaks.\nClient health: spotting problems before clients feel them. Owning escalations end-to-end. Retention is your scoreboard.\nReporting: the founder gets one clean weekly picture of delivery, pipeline, and team performance from you.\nMust-have requirements (we will not consider applications without these) \nMarketing agency experience is a MUST. You've worked at or run operations for a marketing agency: SEO, content, paid media, or similar. You understand client retainers, deliverables, and why clients churn. No exceptions\nReddit, SEO, or GEO/AEO experience is a MUST. You know how organic visibility works: Reddit marketing, search rankings, or AI answer optimization (getting brands cited by ChatGPT/Perplexity). You don't need to be the strategist, but you must understand what our delivery team does well enough to manage it and quality-check it\n3+ years running day-to-day operations (client delivery, team coordination, reporting)\nHands-on with CRMs and automation tools ( Make.com or Zapier experience is a big plus)\nExperience managing remote contractors and keeping output high without micromanaging\nYou write SOPs, build systems, and make decisions without waiting for approval\nYou're NOT a fit if \nYou need daily direction to function\nYou've only worked inside big companies with big support structures\nYou've only done ops for e-commerce, logistics, or non-marketing businesses this role requires understanding how agency delivery actually works\nYou see \"startup chaos\" as a problem instead of raw material\nCompensation \n$5,000\u2013$10,000/month depending on experience and location, plus a performance bonus tied to client retention and delivery metrics. Full-time, remote, contractor structure.\nThe upside \nYou're joining at the inflection point. Run operations well while we scale $60k \u2192 $100k+/mo, and this role grows into a true COO seat with expanded compensation to match. The founder promotes from within our current team leads all started as contractors.\nHow we hire (fast) \nApplication form (~10 minutes, includes a short Loom video)\nTwo 30-minute calls\nPaid trial task (real work, real pay)\nOffer\nCLICK THE \"APPLY NOW\" BUTTON TO SUBMIT YOUR APPLICATION. \n(Applications through the form only we don't review resumes sent any other way.)","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Canada","United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-09T09:26:26.103Z","expires_at":"2026-08-08T09:26:26.103Z","external_id":"novantro","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/pausebreathwork/remote-job/director-of-operations","title":"Director of Operations","company":"Pause Breathwork","location":"Remote","description":"Who We Are \nAt Pause Breathwork , we believe something radical: emotional suffering should be optional.\nOur mission is to spread breathwork and somatic healing across the globe so people can feel alive, liberated, and connected. We\u2019re not just another wellness company \u2014 we\u2019re building a movement.\nOur values run deep:\nEmbodied Wellness \u2013 we practice what we teach.\nMission-Centered \u2013 everything we do points back to healing the world.\nWorld-Class Experience \u2013 only the best for our students, clients, and community.\nResults-Driven \u2013 we track, measure, and optimize for real impact.\nExtreme Ownership \u2013 no finger-pointing, no excuses, we own our results.\nWe\u2019re a remote team sprinkled all over the world. Even though we\u2019re behind different screens, the vibe is pure connection. We laugh hard, create big, and make magic happen together. Working here is the sweet spot between being deeply mission-driven and having a ridiculous amount of fun.\nRole Purpose \nThe Director of Operations is the operational leader responsible for translating the CEO\u2019s vision into consistent execution across the business.\nThis role owns the company\u2019s commercial operating system by ensuring Marketing, Sales, Revenue Operations, Delivery, Finance, and external partners are aligned, accountable, and executing toward the company\u2019s most important goals.\nThe Operational Director does not create the company\u2019s marketing strategy or replace department experts. Instead, they ensure the existing strategy is executed with excellence, bottlenecks are removed, decisions are implemented quickly, and the business consistently achieves its booked call, revenue, and profit goals.\nThis person becomes Samantha\u2019s operational counterpart, allowing Samantha to focus on vision, brand, innovation, partnerships, growth, and motherhood.\nCore Responsibilities \nOwn Commercial Execution \nOwn the execution required to consistently achieve the company\u2019s weekly booked call targets, monthly revenue targets, and profit goals\nEnsure every commercial initiative ultimately supports the company\u2019s North Star metric\nMonitor leading indicators and proactively identify risks before they impact revenue\nDrive cross-functional execution to ensure Marketing, Sales, Revenue Operations, Delivery, and Customer Experience remain aligned\nEnsure every department understands how their work contributes to company revenue\n\u2060Lead Company Execution \nOwn execution of quarterly priorities, annual goals, and strategic initiatives\nFacilitate weekly leadership meetings with clear decisions, accountability, and follow-up\nRun company scorecards and ensure KPIs are reviewed consistently\nEnsure action items are completed on time\nEliminate bottlenecks that slow execution\nMaintain visibility across every major company initiative\nHold Leaders Accountable \nHold department leaders accountable to KPIs, deadlines, and deliverables\n\u2060Ensure projects move forward without CEO intervention\n\u2060Escalate issues quickly when execution falls behind\n\u2060Drive clear ownership across every department\n\u2060Create a culture of accountability, urgency, and follow-through\nOwn the Commercial Rhythm \nOwn the rhythm\u2014not the individual execution\u2014of:\nMarketing campaigns\nSales pipeline health\n\u2060Booked call targets\n\u2060Funnel performance\nLaunch readiness\n\u2060Vendor performance\nCross-functional communication\nWeekly performance reviews\nPost-launch retrospectives\nIf booked calls fall below target, this role brings together the appropriate leaders, identifies root causes, assigns owners, and ensures corrective action is taken immediately.\nMarketing Leadership & Oversight \nPartner closely with Marketing Operations and external marketing partners to ensure flawless execution.\nResponsibilities include:\nEnsure campaigns launch on time\nHold agencies, contractors, and vendors accountable\n\u2060Ensure creative, copy, funnels, and campaigns move efficiently through production\n\u2060Review campaign performance and facilitate optimization discussions\n\u2060Ensure marketing projects remain aligned with revenue priorities\nProtect execution timelines without becoming the bottleneck\nThis role does not replace Marketing Operations or create the CEO\u2019s marketing strategy.\nCross-Functional Leadership \nPartner with:\nMarketing Operations\n\u2060Sales\n\u2060Customer Experience\n\u2060Finance\n\u2060Delivery\n\u2060Paid Ads Agencies\n\u2060Contractors\n\u2060Technology partners\nEnsure every department is aligned toward company objectives and operating from the same priorities.\nCEO Partnership \nServe as Samantha\u2019s operational extension by:\nProtecting CEO time\n\u2060Filtering decisions that do not require CEO involvement\nDriving initiatives from decision to completion\nMaintaining awareness of company risks, opportunities, and priorities\nPreparing leadership discussions with recommendations instead of problems\nEnsuring the business continues operating efficiently during travel, speaking engagements, and maternity leave\nWhat Success Looks Like \nWithin 6\u201312 months \nThe company consistently achieves or exceeds weekly booked call targets\n\u2060Revenue goals are consistently achieved through disciplined execution\n\u2060Marketing, Sales, Revenue Operations, and Delivery operate as one aligned commercial engine\n\u2060Leadership meetings drive decisions rather than discussions\n\u2060Projects launch on schedule without CEO intervention\n\u2060Vendors and agencies are proactively managed and held accountable\n\u2060Bottlenecks are identified and solved before impacting performance\n\u2060Samantha is no longer the central point of coordination for day-to-day execution\nThe business operates effectively whether Samantha is present or not\nKPIs \nCommercial Performance\nAchieve the weekly booked call target\nAchieve 90\u2013100% of monthly revenue goals\nMaintain company profit margin at or above target\nDeliver quarterly priorities on time\nLaunch campaigns on schedule\nLeadership\nLeadership scorecards reviewed weekly\nDepartment accountability maintained\nCross-functional blockers resolved quickly\n\u2060Vendor and agency performance managed proactively\nCEO Leverage\nIncrease CEO Freedom Score\n\u2060Significantly reduce CEO involvement in day-to-day operational decisions\n\u2060Enable Samantha to spend the majority of her time on vision, partnerships, speaking, innovation, content, and brand\nWho You Are \n\u2060Experienced operational leader with a track record of leading cross-functional teams\nDeep understanding of marketing, sales, launches, funnels, and revenue operations\nAble to translate vision into disciplined execution\n\u2060Strong project prioritization and decision-making skills\nNaturally creates accountability without micromanaging\n\u2060Highly organized, proactive, and calm under pressure\nComfortable leading both internal teams and external vendors\nThinks in systems, processes, and measurable outcomes\nCommercially minded with a strong understanding of the metrics that drive business growth\nAble to identify patterns, diagnose bottlenecks, and mobilize teams toward solutions\nTrusted partner who can operate as Samantha\u2019s operational and strategic extension\nWhat This Role Is Not \nThis role is not:\n\u2060A Marketing Director responsible for creating marketing strategy\nA traditional Operations Manager focused primarily on administration\n\u2060A Project Manager coordinating individual tasks\nA Revenue Operations specialist focused on CRM, dashboards, or systems\nA Marketing Operations specialist responsible for building funnels, automations, dashboards, or backend infrastructure\nThose responsibilities remain with the appropriate department leaders. The Operational Director exists to ensure those departments operate together as one high-performing commercial organization, consistently delivering the company\u2019s booked call, revenue, and profit goals.\nWhy You\u2019ll Love Working Here \nA deeply meaningful mission \u2014 everything you do helps reduce suffering and increase aliveness\nA remote-first lifestyle with a team that actually feels like family\nA chance to work with a CEO who\u2019s a creative firecracker and deeply committed to both mission and team\nReal ownership of your role \u2014 your ideas matter here, and you\u2019ll see them come to life\nA culture that values fun as much as impact. Think: belly laughs on Zoom, Slack threads full of gifs, and a team that truly has your back\nApplication Process \nHere is the outline of the whole application process, so you know what to expect:\nFill in and submit the application form\nSeveral video interviews where we try to get to know you better and give you a chance to get to know us, as well as talk about your previous experiences and future goals\nInterview Task\u00a0\nReference checks\u00a0\nIf that goes well, we will make an offer and continue working together!","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Canada","United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-08T22:43:01.758Z","expires_at":"2026-08-07T22:43:01.758Z","external_id":"pausebreathwork","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/accountingwiseinc/remote-job/accounting-ap-ar-payroll-manager-fully-remote","title":"Accounting/AP/AR/Payroll Manager (Fully Remote)","company":"Full Cycle CFO","location":"Remote","description":"Who We Are \nAt Accounting Wise/Full Cycle CFO, our goal is to assist SaaS and online businesses in achieving their financial goals. We do this by offering scalable modular accounting solutions, timely and consistent financial data, thoughtful solutions, and caring support.\nWe offer opportunities at the ground level of a growing accounting firm.\u00a0 We are a global team where everyone\u2019s opinion matters. We support each other and help our clients succeed.\u00a0 Our goal is to become the number one provider of internal accounting services to SaaS companies and online businesses.\u00a0 As we grow, each team member will directly impact building and contributing to the company's success.\u00a0 In addition, we encourage a remote work lifestyle that offers our team members the flexibility to travel and have a good work/life balance.\u00a0\u00a0\nWe are seeking a talented AP, AR, and Payroll Specialist to join our team. This role is a full-time position. If you have the experience and are looking for an exciting job in which every client is different, you will wear multiple hats, grow professionally, and be a part of a supportive and fun team at the ground level - this is a fantastic opportunity for you.\nIf you\u2019re not sure you\u2019re 100% qualified but are up for the challenge - we want you to apply. \nWhat You\u2019ll Do \nManagement of complete AP process for clients such as:\nBill platforms such as Bill.com , Xero, QBO, etc.,\u00a0\nInitiate payments in various financial platforms\nCollect required documentation from vendors\nMiscellaneous correspondence with vendors, contractors, and other payees.\nManagement of complete AR process for clients such as:\nInvoice platforms such as QBO, Xero, Bill.com , etc.,\u00a0\nA complete understanding of invoice preparation,\nCollection of outstanding invoices,\nMiscellaneous correspondence with clients and customers related to the performance of the AR function.\u00a0\nManagement of payroll duties for clients such as:\nProcess periodic payroll, including any adjustments,\nHandle hiring, terminations, bonuses, maternity leave, etc.\nWork with the payroll provider to resolve any issues\nCommunication with the client and external parties\nManagement of expense reimbursements for clients with and without software applications.\nManagement of general accounting and bookkeeping duties for clients such as:\nRecord, categorize, and reconcile daily transactions across bank and credit card accounts\nPerform monthly bank, credit card, and balance sheet reconciliations\nPrepare and post journal entries, including accruals, prepaids, and deferrals\nMaintain the general ledger and chart of accounts for accuracy and consistency\nSupport revenue recognition and deferred revenue schedules for subscription and SaaS clients\nPrepare month-end and year-end close workpapers, including supporting schedules and tie-outs\nAssist in preparing financial statements and reporting packages for client review\nMaintain clean documentation and workpapers to firm standards\nSupport and collaborate with the accounting team to close financial periods\nResponsive communication with assigned clients and the internal team via Slack, Looms, video conference, e-mail, etc.\nWhat You\u2019ll Need \nBachelor's Degree in Accounting or related field\n5+ years of AP/AR/Payroll experience\nHands-on bookkeeping and month-end close experience, including reconciliations and journal entries\nExperience with online platforms such as QBO, Google Suite, Slack, MS365, etc. \nFamiliarity and comfort with technology\nStrong attention to detail and accuracy, with good analytical skills\nExperience in managing and coordinating client concerns and solutions\nHas the ability to prioritize projects, set goals, and schedules\u00a0\nA positive, helpful, and can-do attitude\nHighly responsive communication with clients and the internal team\nComfortable working on US hours\nWhat\u2019s Nice to Have \nHas experience working with software companies, fintech, lead generation, and/or online service-based businesses\nExperience in bootstrapping and start-up companies\nPhysical presence close to US hours\nExperience in managing Accountants / small teams\nWhat You\u2019ll Love \nCompletely remote position\nThe empowered working environment that promotes autonomy\nUnlimited PTO and Company Retreats\nEmployee recognition perks\nBe part of a global team that values living their best remote life\nBeing part of a fun and supportive team\nGrowth and leading opportunities on the ground floor of a startup\nTo show that you have carefully read this job ad, please include the word 'PRECISION' in the \u201cConfirm understanding of job description\u201d line of the application form. \nThank you for taking the time to consider this position. I look forward to hearing from you soon!\nSagar Khant","locations":["Canada","Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-07T23:33:05.177Z","expires_at":"2026-08-06T23:33:05.177Z","external_id":"accountingwiseinc","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/gymdesk/remote-job/ai-first-product-manager","title":"AI-First Product Manager","company":"Gymdesk","location":"Remote","description":"Company Description\nGymdesk is a gym management platform built for fitness gyms and martial arts studios. Our product suite is used by thousands of gyms and covers the full operating stack: membership management, billing, scheduling, attendance tracking, rank and belt progression, a website builder, and communications tools. We're the system of record for gyms of every type and size, from a single-location BJJ academy to multi-site franchise 24/7 gyms.\nWe're scaling our team to keep up with international demand. We hired our first PM a couple months ago and this will be our second, meaning you'll have an outsized opportunity to write the playbook of how Product functions. This is a PM role where your decisions directly shape what thousands of gym owners interact with every day.\nWhat \"AI-First Product Manager\" Means To Us\nWhat's still the same:\nThe fundamentals haven't changed:\nProduct sense. You can look at a feature request, a usage pattern, or a customer complaint and see the actual problem underneath. You know when to dig deeper and when to ship.\nPrioritization under constraints. We have a focused engineering team, a large surface area, and more requests than we can build. You'll need to say no clearly and back it up with evidence, not just gut feel.\nClarity in the spec. Engineers should be able to read your work and build without a follow-up meeting. You write goals, scope, edge cases, and \"what we're not doing\" with precision.\nCustomer empathy. You'll talk to gym owners. You'll read support tickets. You'll watch people use the product. You'll carry that context into every decision. No amount of AI tooling replaces the judgment that comes from knowing your users deeply.\nCross-functional ownership. You'll work with engineering, design, CS, and marketing. You own the problem end-to-end, from discovery through delivery through measuring impact.\nWhat's different:\nWe believe the PM role is changing fast, and we want someone who's already living in that change. Here's what that looks like at Gymdesk:\nAI as your second brain, not a crutch. You use AI tools daily for research synthesis, drafting, competitive analysis, and pattern recognition. You've built systems (prompts, projects, workflows) that make you measurably faster without sacrificing quality. You own your outputs. \"AI wrote it\" is never an excuse.\nCode-adjacent, not code-afraid. You don't need to be an engineer. But you should be comfortable operating with AI assistants that benefits from a codebase. You know how to build prototypes in Claude Code/Cowork, Cursor, or other tools.\nPrototyping as communication. When a spec is ambiguous, you spin up a quick prototype to show what you mean instead of writing three more paragraphs. The artifact is a functioning thing, not a document.\nSystematic about your AI workflow. You don't just chat with an LLM and hope for good output. You've thought about how to give AI context, how to structure your prompts, how to review what comes back, and how to improve the process over time. You have opinions on what works and what doesn't.\nUp to speed on the landscape. You know what's shipping across the AI tooling ecosystem. Not because you chase hype, but because you understand how these tools change what's possible for PMs and for the products we build.\nThings You'll Do\nSynthesize customer feedback, support patterns, and usage data to find the real problems worth solving\nWrite specs grounded in how the product actually works today, using AI-assisted codebase exploration to understand what exists before proposing what should change\nBuild quick prototypes to make ambiguous ideas concrete and get faster feedback from engineering and design\nOwn features from discovery through delivery: customer evidence, spec, working with eng through build, measuring outcomes\nTriage inbound feature requests against strategy and make clear, defensible priority calls\nImprove your own AI workflows over time, building up the systems and prompts that make you faster and sharper with every cycle\nQualifications\nEvidence of using AI tools seriously in your work (show us your setup, your workflow, or something you've built)\nBased between PST and EST timezones\n3+ years in product management, ideally in B2B SaaS\nDemonstrated product sense: you've shipped features that moved metrics, not just features that existed\nStrong written communication. Our team is distributed. Writing is how decisions get made\nComfort with ambiguity. We're building the PM function. You'll help shape how it works, not inherit a playbook\nBonus: experience with SMB customers, international markets, or vertical SaaS\nWhat you'll get\nSalary of $150,000-$175,000 for U.S. Employees (different ranges elsewhere) and benefits\nMedical, dental, and vision coverage, 401k (US only)\nFully-remote culture\nFlexible time off with no annual cap, company-wide holidays\nDirect influence over product strategy and how the PM function operates\nA team that's serious about using AI to work smarter, not just talking about it\nThe chance to build the playbook for what an AI-first product org looks like at scale\nGymdesk asks respectfully to only apply through the application form and not email/apply to them directly. Recruiters and Agencies, please do not contact Gymdesk directly.","locations":["Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Canada","United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-07T00:15:11.266Z","expires_at":"2026-08-06T00:15:11.266Z","external_id":"gymdesk","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/thedgcompany/remote-job/marketing-automation-revenue-systems-builder-hubspot-ai-web-remote","title":"Marketing Automation & Revenue Systems Builder (Hubspot / AI / Web) \u2014 Remote","company":"The DG Company","location":"Remote","description":"The DG Company \u00b7 100% Remote (must overlap US business hours 50%)\nFull-time \u00b7 Comp: 80K - 100K \u2014 base + performance bonus. \u00b7 Paid monthly via Wise / Deel / PayPal\nREAD THIS FIRST \nI'm the founder. We're scaling a portfolio of fast-growing US brands \u2014 Turf Distributors, Interlocking Products, Biltright, and more \u2014 and we're pouring serious money into paid acquisition and additional companies. But traffic isn't the whole game. Right now, too many leads sit in the pipeline and too many existing customers never hear from us again.\nWe operate in old-school industries that still run on manual, disconnected sales processes. Your mission is to automate an old-school business end to end: take a traditional sales motion and turn it into a modern, automated revenue machine that runs at the leading edge of the industry.\nI'm looking for one builder to own everything that happens after the click: the automation, the CRM, and the entire sales process \u2014 with our sales team built into the system as part of the flow, not treated as a separate bolt-on step. You'll design the whole engine so my team just executes their piece and the machine does the rest. You'll work hand-in-glove with our paid media operator \u2014 they bring the traffic, you turn it into closed revenue and repeat buyers.\nJust as important: I want someone with real vision \u2014 who brings their own ideas to the table, spots what will move conversion before I ask, and keeps us ahead of the industry instead of catching up to it. This is a founder-level seat for a creative, technical mind with an ownership mentality who wants to help build a company to $1B with lean resources. If you're a \"set up a couple of email workflows and wait for instructions\" person, close this tab. If you build systems, bring ideas, and ship real things, keep reading.\nHOW THIS SEAT FITS: to start, you'll run as a peer alongside our paid media operator and our creative/web lead \u2014 all of you reporting directly to me while we build. This is a builder seat, not a middle-management one.\u00a0\nWHAT YOU'LL OWN \nHubSpot + our other CRMs \u2014 architect the whole thing: pipelines, lifecycle stages, lead scoring, deal stages, reporting. Make it a machine, not a mess.\nThe entire sales process, end to end \u2014 nurture sequences, follow-ups, routing, and automations that move leads to close. Critically: build the sales team into the system \u2014 the right lead reaches the right rep at the right moment with the right context, so reps sell instead of chasing admin, and every deal flows through one machine rather than a dozen disconnected steps.\nAutomate the old-school way of doing things \u2014 replace the manual, tribal-knowledge parts of the sales motion with systems that scale.\nUpsell & retention \u2014 build the flows that bring existing customers back and increase lifetime value.\nPipeline conversion \u2014 find where deals stall and build the systems that push them to buy.\nWebsites & landing pages \u2014 build and/or code the pages and funnels this all runs on.\nAI sales agents \u2014 deploy and manage AI voice and text agents that support the sale: answering and following up on calls, texting leads, qualifying, booking, and backing up the human reps so no lead goes cold.\nPhone system & lead capture \u2014 own the phone/telephony system and make sure every single lead \u2014 from a call, a form, a text, an ad \u2014 lands cleanly in the machine, routed and tracked. Nothing falls through the cracks.\nAI tooling \u2014 use Claude and other AI to build tools for our customers and internal team, and keep this company at the frontier of what AI can do for us.\nTraining & enablement tools \u2014 build the systems that get everyone up to speed fast: onboarding and training tools for our sales reps, sales leaders, and customers \u2014 playbooks, interactive guides, AI-powered help, and product education. Make our knowledge scale without a person having to repeat it every time.\nPartner with the paid media operator \u2014 your systems and their traffic have to work as one engine.\u00a0\nYou are the person who makes the back half of the funnel run itself.\u00a0\nYOU MUST HAVE \nDeep, hands-on HubSpot expertise \u2014 you've architected automation and CRM systems, not just used them.\nA real technical / coding background \u2014 you can build and code websites, integrations, and tools yourself.\nProven experience building with AI (Claude specifically is a big plus) \u2014 you've actually shipped AI-powered tools, not just talked about them.\nExperience with AI voice/text agents and phone/telephony systems \u2014 you've deployed AI callers/texters or CRM\u2013phone integrations and know how to capture and route every lead (tools like a CCaaS/VoIP platform, conversational AI, call tracking, etc.).\nA creative, systems-thinking mind \u2014 you see the whole funnel and build the connective tissue.\nVision and initiative \u2014 you bring your own ideas, push us toward what's next in the industry, and don't wait to be told what to build.\nUnderstanding of the full revenue motion \u2014 lead to nurture to close to upsell to retain.\nThe ability to turn knowledge into tools \u2014 you can take how our best people sell and package it into training and enablement that scales to reps, leaders, and customers.\nStrong English and comfort working US hours; you'll work closely with me and the paid media operator.\nHOW TO APPLY \u2014 AND HOW I'LL KNOW YOU'RE REA L\nTalkers can't fake this. Builders will breeze it. Send me all four:\nPick one of our brands (Turf Distributors, Interlocking Products, or Biltright). Look at how we currently capture, nurture, close, and follow up. Tell me \u2014 plainly \u2014 what's broken, what you'd build in your first 90 days, and one idea we probably haven't thought of that would move conversion or put us ahead of the industry.\nShow me what you've built. Real proof: HubSpot workflows/automations you architected, a tool you built with AI, a site or funnel you coded. Links, screenshots, or a short demo. It must be real and yours.\nRecord a 3\u20135 minute Loom (screen-share + your voice) walking me through #1 and #2 \u2014 how you think and how you build.\nRead the whole ad? Start your subject line with the word BUILD followed by the single most impactful system or tool you've ever shipped and its result (example: BUILD \u2014 HubSpot upsell engine, +32% LTV). Anything else gets deleted.\nSend everything to natalie.romero@thedgcompany.com \nFirst great applicant wins!\nONE MORE THING: because this seat has a path to leading the team, add a line (in your email or your Loom) about a time you led or coordinated others to ship something real \u2014 or, if you haven't led yet, why you're ready to. I'm looking for a builder first who can grow into leading, not a manager who can't build.\nHOW THIS STARTS: the strongest applicants get a paid 30\u201360 day trial building one real system on one of our brands. Ship something that moves the number, and the full-time seat and bonus structure are yours.\nDON'T BOTHER APPLYING IF... \nYou've only used HubSpot, not architected and automated it.\nYou can't code or build the websites/tools yourself.\nYou've never actually shipped anything with AI \u2014 you've only read about it.\nYou're an agency or freelancer looking for projects \u2014 this is a full-time, in-house seat.\nYou want a management title but can't build the systems yourself \u2014 this seat leads by building first.\nYou skipped the subject-line step.\nIf you're the builder I'm describing, you already know it. Prove it.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-06T20:01:41.509Z","expires_at":"2026-08-05T20:01:41.509Z","external_id":"thedgcompany","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/zentact/remote-job/staff-software-engineer-typescript-distributed-systems-2","title":"Staff Software Engineer (TypeScript / Distributed Systems)","company":"Zentact","location":"Remote","description":"Build the payments infrastructure powering SaaS products at scale! \nZentact is building a white-label payments infrastructure platform that allows SaaS companies to embed payments into their product in weeks, not months.\nBehind that simplicity is a high-throughput, event-driven system handling:\nPayment orchestration\nReal-time + batch analytics\nDistributed workflows\nMission-critical reliability requirements\nWe\u2019re scaling fast \u2014 and we\u2019re hiring a Staff Engineer to help shape the architecture that supports our next stage of growth.\nThe Role \nThis is a hands-on Staff IC role .\nYou\u2019ll:\nLead architecture decisions across core platform systems\nDesign distributed systems that handle high-volume payment and analytics workflows\nRaise engineering standards across reliability, observability, and safe deployments\nMentor engineers and influence technical direction\nPartner closely with product and leadership to ship safely in a mission-critical domain\nYou will not be managing people \u2014 this is deep technical ownership.\nWhat You\u2019ll Work On \nEvent-driven systems processing large data volumes\nReal-time + batch analytics pipelines\nWorkflow orchestration (Temporal-style systems)\nSafe, no-downtime deploy strategies\nBackwards-compatible APIs and data migrations\nObservability systems (tracing, metrics, structured logs)\nScaling systems for reliability under load\nIf you enjoy thinking about:\nFailure modes\nData consistency\nIdempotency and retries\nScaling and partitioning\nSystem correctness in payments-like environments\nYou\u2019ll likely enjoy this role.\nWhat We\u2019re Looking For \nYou likely have:\n8+ years building production systems\nExperience operating distributed or high-scale backend systems\nStrong system design skills\nA production-first mindset (uptime, safe changes, operational awareness)\nExperience mentoring engineers and influencing architecture\nBonus (not required):\nPayments or regulated systems\nEvent-driven architectures\nWorkflow orchestration tools (Temporal or similar)\nAnalytics databases (ClickHouse, BigQuery, Snowflake, etc.)\nWe care far more about your ability to design and run reliable systems than matching our exact stack.\nTech Stack \nTypeScript (Node.js)\nReact\nEvent-driven architecture (Pub/Sub)\nWorkflow orchestration (Temporal)\nGCP infrastructure\nAnalytics + operational data systems\ntRPC\nZod\nYou don\u2019t need experience with every tool \u2014 strong distributed systems experience transfers well.\nWhy This Role Is Interesting \nStaff-level ownership without management overhead\nArchitect systems early in their scaling curve\nReal distributed systems problems (not CRUD apps)\nPayments complexity without building a payments company\nHigh autonomy, low bureaucracy\nDirect influence on product direction\nWhy Zentact \nHigh impact: you\u2019ll shape core architecture as the product scales fast\nRapidly growing and evolving product\nReal systems problems: reliability, throughput, analytics, workflows, and payments complexity\nBuild a platform that helps SaaS companies launch payments quickly with a managed solution\u00a0\nStrong engineering culture: autonomy, ownership, and practical decision-making\nCompensation & Benefits \nCompetitive salary, based on experience and impact\nUnlimited PTO, take time when you need it, we trust adults to manage their schedules\nFully remote-friendly work environment\nHigh ownership and influence in a fast-growing product\nZentact asks respectfully to only apply through the application form and not email/apply to them directly. Recruiters and Agencies please do not contact Zentact directly.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Canada"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-06T06:37:15.602Z","expires_at":"2026-08-05T06:37:15.602Z","external_id":"zentact","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/alyssanobriga/remote-job/integrator-ceo","title":"Integrator/CEO","company":"Alyssa Nobriga","location":"Remote","description":"About Alyssa Nobriga International \nAlyssa Nobriga International (ANI) is a globally recognized coaching education and personal transformation company founded by Alyssa Nobriga.\u00a0\nAt the heart of ANI is the Institute for Coaching Mastery (ICM) \u2014 an internationally recognized and accredited 1 year coach certification program designed to develop exceptionally qualified, deeply embodied coaches who lead with both emotional intelligence and practical mastery. ICM combines psychology, coaching methodology, nervous system work, leadership development, and transformational communication into a powerful learning experience that has attracted thousands of students from around the world.\nAbout the Role \nWe are looking for a world-class leader to take full ownership of this company's operations and execution. In this role, you are not just a manager \u2014 you are the person who makes the company run. You translate Alyssa's vision into clear execution plans, hold the leadership team to a high standard, and drive results across every function of the business.\nThis is not a role for someone who needs a playbook or constant direction. It is for a high-agency operator who thinks like a founder, moves with urgency, and treats every bottleneck as a problem to solve today.\nWhat You Will Own \nCompany Goals and Execution \nSet and drive company priorities across all departments\nOwn the execution calendar and keep initiatives on track\nRemove bottlenecks, make decisions without waiting for direction, and keep the business moving without founder involvement\nLeadership Team \nDirectly manage all department heads, including the Executive Director\nRun weekly leadership meetings, set the agenda, and hold every leader accountable to their results\nYou are the connective tissue across the leadership team.\nFounder Partnership \nConvert Alyssa's ideas and vision into clear, executable plans\nFilter decisions and communications to and from the Founder to keep her out of daily operations\nYou make the visionary's thinking real inside the company.\nRevenue and Growth \nOwn execution across marketing, sales, and product\nYou are 100% accountable for revenue performance and push the company toward its scaling targets\nYou understand funnels, launches, and conversion, and you ensure all revenue-driving teams stay aligned and deliver\nCompany Performance \nOwn company-wide KPIs and scorecards\nLead quarterly and annual planning\nEnsure every team is focused on the highest-impact work, and make all people decisions across the leadership team, including performance reviews, promotions, and exits\nWhat Is Not Your Job \nDetailed financial management, system building, and admin or HR processes are owned by the Executive Director. Your job is to lead the business at the highest level, not to operate at the process level.\nYour First 90 Days \nAlyssa is fully removed from daily operations\nThe leadership team runs effectively without Founder input\nClear company priorities are executed consistently across all departments\n2 to 3 major growth initiatives delivered without Founder involvement\nWho You Are \nYou are a fast-moving, high-agency operator who takes ownership without being asked. You are decisive with incomplete information, comfortable being wrong and correcting fast, and you don\u2019t wait for permission to act. You anticipate problems before they surface and you do not get stuck in analysis.\nNon-Negotiable Experience \nProven multi-year experience as a COO, Integrator, Executive Director, Previous Founder, or equivalent inside a founder-led online coaching, certification, or personal development business\nExperience inside a company doing $3M to $15M per year, ideally having led scaling from 7 to multi-7 or 8 figures\nTrack record of personally managing department heads, not just individual contributors or teams\nOwned execution across marketing, operations, and product with company-wide accountability for results\nOperated the company day-to-day without founder involvement\nExperience in the exact ecosystem is required: 7-figure launches, personal brand-based business, global contractor team, fast pivots, and AI implementation\nLeadership Capability \nManages and develops leaders, not just teams.\nHolds people accountable to outcomes and replaces underperformers when needed.\nRuns performance reviews and enforces KPIs across the leadership team.\nUnderstands funnels, launches, and revenue impact well enough to push teams toward the right results.\nAlyssa Nobriga asks respectfully to only apply through the application form and not email/apply to them directly. Recruiters and Agencies please do not contact Alyssa Nobriga directly.","locations":["Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Canada","United States","Afghanistan","Armenia","Azerbaijan","Bahrain","Bangladesh","Bhutan","Brunei Darussalam","Cambodia","China","Democratic People's Republic of Korea","Georgia","Hong Kong (China)","India","Indonesia","Iran","Iraq","Israel","Japan","Jordan","Kazakhstan","Kuwait","Kyrgyzstan","Lao People's Democratic Republic","Lebanon","Macao (China)","Malaysia","Maldives","Mongolia","Myanmar","Nepal","Oman","Pakistan","Philippines","Qatar","Russian Federation","Saudi Arabia","Singapore","South Korea","Sri Lanka","State of Palestine","Syrian Arab Republic","Taiwan","Tajikistan","Thailand","Timor-Leste","Turkmenistan","United Arab Emirates","Uzbekistan","Viet Nam","Yemen"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-06T06:36:17.139Z","expires_at":"2026-08-05T06:36:17.139Z","external_id":"alyssanobriga","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/netreputation1/remote-job/enterprise-account-executive-orm-seo","title":"Enterprise Account Executive - ORM/SEO","company":"NetReputation","location":"Remote","description":"Online Reputation Management, Crisis Management, Public Relations & Digital Marketing Services\nAbout NetReputation \nNetReputation is the premier online reputation management firm trusted by the world's most recognized Enterprise and SMB brands, influential executives, and discerning private individuals. Through a powerful fusion of advanced content strategy, crisis response, reputation monitoring, review management, digital privacy, and precision SEO, we help our clients take control of their digital narrative, shaping how the world sees you and your brand to ensure you dominate the search results that matter most.\nPosition Overview \nAs an Enterprise Account Executive, you will own the full sales cycle, from qualifying inbound leads to closing, using a consultative approach to solve high stakes reputation and crisis management challenges. You will sell comprehensive ORM and Digital Marketing Services (SEO, content creation, social media, and paid search) to chief executives, marketing directors, business owners, and high net worth individuals, driving the next stage of growth for SMB and enterprise brands. This is not a SaaS selling role and we're looking for someone who has sold enterprise deals within the ORM, SEO, or Digital Marketing Services. \nKey Responsibilities \nGenerate Revenue: Own the full sales process from lead qualification through custom presentations, ROI analysis, fee negotiation, SOW review, and closing new business in the ORM and Digital Marketing space\nConsultative Selling: Conduct deep dive discovery sessions to understand prospect pain points, analyze their digital footprint, and tailor solutions that build trust and protect credibility\nPresentation and Pitching: Deliver compelling presentations to executive level stakeholders and high net worth individuals using tools such as SERP analysis and reputation scorecards\nPipeline Management: Manage a high volume pipeline, maintain accurate CRM records, and ensure a steady flow of qualified leads\nStrategic Collaboration: Partner with internal strategy, SEO, and content teams to develop customized proposals\nNegotiation: Close complex, long term contractual agreements and retainer based services\nAccount Growth: Build post sale relationships and identify upsell opportunities for large enterprise clients\nQualifications \n5 to 7+ years of experience selling ORM, digital marketing, or PR services to SMB and Enterprise brands\nStrategic thinker with strong consultative selling instincts\nExceptional presenter, able to communicate complex ORM, crisis management, and digital strategies to senior stakeholders\nProficient in CRM platforms (Salesforce, Zoho, or HubSpot) and SEO/reputation tools (BrightEdge, SEMrush, Ahrefs, Meltwater)\nBachelor's degree required\nWhy Join Us? \nTop Tier Tools: Comprehensive digital audits and proprietary tools to support your sales process\nStrong Support System: Backed by a world class Strategy and Client Success team so you can focus on closing\nCompensation & Benefits \nOTE: $200,000-$250,000\nHealth Insurance\nDental Insurance\nVision Insurance\n401(k) Matching\nFlexible Paid Time Off\nWork Location \nFully Remote \u2014 with the option to work from our Sarasota, FL headquarters\nNetReputation asks respectfully to only apply through the application form and not email/apply to them directly. Recruiters and Agencies please do not contact NetReputation directly.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-01T23:10:05.001Z","expires_at":"2026-07-31T23:10:05.001Z","external_id":"netreputation1","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/startinwyoming/remote-job/client-operations-coordinator","title":"Client Operations Coordinator","company":"Start in Wyoming","location":"Remote","description":"About Us \nThe business owner is a creative, entrepreneurial lawyer. He started a law firm, which grew. As that firm grew, he created an online course business to sell courses that satisfy legal requirements. We now have a registered agent business, Start in Wyoming , to help international entrepreneurs and digital nomads create and operate Wyoming LLCs that satisfy US banking requirements. We work with an international client base and run a lean, fully remote team.\nAbout the Role \nWe're hiring a detail-oriented Client Operations Coordinator to help keep client engagements running smoothly \u2014 coordinating meetings, supporting clients through the process, handling documents and records, and keeping our systems organized. You'll work closely with firm leadership and be a steady, professional point of contact for clients throughout their engagement.\nThis is a contract (1099-equivalent) engagement paid via Gusto. Fully remote in Latin America.\nResponsibilities \nCoordinate and schedule client meetings across multiple international time zones\nServe as a responsive, professional point of contact for client communications\nPrepare, process, and track client documents and related follow-ups accurately and on time\nKeep internal records, files, and our CRM organized and up to date\nProvide day-to-day operational support to the team and escalate items as appropriate\nWho you are \n2+ years in client operations, executive/administrative support, customer success, or a comparable coordination role\nExcellent written and spoken English; comfortable as a professional, client-facing voice\nStrong working-hours overlap with U.S. Mountain Time, with flexibility to support clients in other regions\nHighly organized and reliable, with strong attention to detail and follow-through\nComfortable learning and working across common business software (CRM, video conferencing, and cloud document tools)\nAbility to work independently in a remote team\nDiscretion and sound judgment handling confidential client and financial information\nFamiliarity with U.S. business formation or registered-agent services\nPlus if you have experience supporting a law firm or CPA\nCore Values \nBias to action\nCooperative\nOwns problems and issues - personal dignity/ownership mentality\nWork Environment & Benefits \nFully remote,\u00a0 contract position\nMonday\u2013Friday, primarily working U.S. Mountain Time\nSalary - $1,500-$2,500/month USD\nSmall supportive team working directly with the founder\nPTO\nStart in Wyoming asks respectfully to only apply through the application form and not email/apply to them directly. Recruiters and Agencies please do not contact Start in Wyoming directly.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-01T04:03:16.334Z","expires_at":"2026-07-31T04:03:16.334Z","external_id":"startinwyoming","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/alyssanobriga/remote-job/organic-marketing-lead","title":"Organic Marketing Lead","company":"Alyssa Nobriga","location":"Remote","description":"About Alyssa Nobriga International \nAlyssa Nobriga International (ANI) is a globally recognized coaching education and personal transformation company founded by Alyssa Nobriga.\u00a0\nAt the heart of ANI is the Institute for Coaching Mastery (ICM) \u2014 an internationally recognized and accredited 1 year coach certification program designed to develop exceptionally qualified, deeply embodied coaches who lead with both emotional intelligence and practical mastery. ICM combines psychology, coaching methodology, nervous system work, leadership development, and transformational communication into a powerful learning experience that has attracted thousands of students from around the world.\nWho This Role Is For \nThis is not a social media manager role. This is not a scheduler, a caption-writer, or someone who needs instructions.\nThis role is for someone who has already taken a personal brand or thought leader from strong visibility to massive organic reach \u2014 and knows exactly how to do it again.\nYou\u2019ve worked with big names in the coaching / personal development / education / spirituality / wellness / influence space.\nYou understand what makes content spread, what platforms reward, and how to engineer momentum across ecosystems.\nIf you\u2019ve ever said, \u201cI know how to make this go viral \u2014 give me the creator and the access\u201d, this role is for you.\nWe\u2019re open to both full-time and part-time team members. We'd love to hear from you - apply and we'll be happy to review! \nThe Mission \nIn 2026, Alyssa Nobriga\u2019s primary focus is organic reach at scale. Not vanity metrics. Actual reach. Actual awareness. Actual influence.\nYour mission as Organic Marketing Lead is to: \nMake Alyssa`s organic content (podcast, social) go viral in 2026\nEngineer million-view moments\nLead the growth of Alyssa`s podcast into Top 10 rankings\nMake Alyssa`s content unavoidable in personal development niche\nBuild a self-reinforcing ecosystem where every platform fuels the others\nThis role owns organic growth, visibility, reach, and cultural relevance.\nPlatforms You Will Own (Holistically, Not in Silos) \nYou are responsible for orchestrating growth across the full ecosystem:\nPodcast (growth, discoverability, rankings, clips, virality)\nInstagram & other social platforms (Reels-first, carousels, stories, positioning)\nNewsletter (growth, open rates, cultural relevance, shareability)\nWebsite & evergreen content (SEO + authority + narrative control)\nFreebies & lead magnets (distribution, not creation)\nPR & organic exposure (earned media, collaborations, visibility moments)\nYou do not treat these as separate channels.You design one integrated content engine where:\nPodcast moments fuel viral clips\nViral clips drive newsletter signups\nNewsletter deepens authority\nAuthority drives PR and collaborations\nPR feeds back into social proof and reach\nWhat You Will Actually Do (Day-to-Day & Strategic) \nViral Content Strategy (Core Responsibility) \nArchitect a clear, repeatable viral content strategy\nIdentify formats that consistently hit 500K\u20131M+ views\nDefine Alyssa\u2019s viral lanes (themes she can dominate)\nDecide what not to post as aggressively as what to post\nBuild a content thesis that platforms reward\nYou are thinking in patterns, formats, hooks, and psychology \u2014 not aesthetics\nPodcast Growth & Ranking Strategy \nTurn the podcast into a growth machine, not just a show\nDesign episode strategies for ranking, not just value\nEngineer clip systems that travel far beyond the audience\nAdvise on guest selection for maximum reach and algorithmic lift\nUnderstand how charts actually work \u2014 and how to influence them\nPlatform-Specific Mastery (Especially Instagram) \nDeep understanding of Reels mechanics, watch time, retention, saves, shares\nAbility to spot early signals of breakout content\nKnow when to double down, pivot, or kill a format\nUnderstand platform shifts before they\u2019re obvious\nYou\u2019re not chasing trends blindly \u2014 you\u2019re anticipating them\nEcosystem Integration & Narrative Control \nEnsure Alyssa\u2019s message is coherent across platforms\nShape her positioning as a category leader, not just a creator\nAlign content with long-term brand authority\nControl the narrative as visibility increases (reputation management mindset)\nLeadership & Execution \nRoll up your sleeves and execute \u2014 this is not a strategy-only role\nDirect editors, social managers, writers, and other contractors\nSet clear creative standards and kill mediocre output fast\nCreate systems that scale without burning the creator out\nWhat Success Looks Like (Non-Negotiable Outcomes) \nWithin 6\u201312 months: \nMultiple pieces of content consistently reaching 500K\u20131M+ views\nMeasurable, sustained growth across all organic platforms\nPodcast rankings moving into Top 10 in its category\nIncreased inbound PR, collaborations, and invitations\nAlyssa clearly perceived as a dominant voice in her space\nIf you cannot visualize how to get there, this role is not for you.\nWho You Must Be \nExperience (Required) \nProven experience scaling personal brands or influencers organically\nWorked with well-known names in personal development niche\nCan speak in specifics: formats, metrics, timelines, decisions\nHas ridden algorithm waves \u2014 and survived platform changes\nMindset \nObsessed with reach, resonance, and momentum\nDirect and data-informed\nComfortable challenging the creator (respectfully)\nNot precious about content \u2014 you kill what doesn\u2019t work\nStyle \nStrategic thinker and operator\nCalm under pressure when content flops\nExcited by big goals, not intimidated by them\nUnderstands creators deeply \u2014 psychologically and creatively\nWhat This Is NOT \nNot a content calendar role\nNot a junior growth experiment\nNot a brand aesthetics position\nNot a role for someone learning on the job\nThis role is for someone who has already won this game \u2014 and wants to do it again at a bigger level.\nWhy This Role Is Rare \nYou will have:\nA creator who wants to go big\nHigh-quality content access\nA team willing and able to execute fast\nA mandate to focus on growth first\nThe only missing piece is you.\nAlyssa Nobriga asks respectfully to only apply through the application form and not email/apply to them directly. Recruiters and Agencies please do not contact Alyssa Nobriga directly.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Canada","United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-22T01:16:27.877Z","expires_at":"2026-07-22T01:16:27.877Z","external_id":"alyssanobriga","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/altaclaro/remote-job/junior-account-executive-saas","title":"Junior Account Executive (SaaS)","company":"AltaClaro","location":"Remote","description":"About AltaClaro \nAltaClaro is the leading provider of experiential, simulation-based legal training. Our proprietary \"Learn-Do-Review\u201d framework combines expert instruction, realistic practice assignments, and detailed feedback from experienced practitioners to build skills that translate directly into practice.\nWe offer comprehensive training across a variety of crucial legal subjects, including litigation, corporate transactions, M&A, finance, legal writing, and GenAI for legal professionals. Each program is grounded in real-world scenarios that build both substantive knowledge and practical judgment. Leading law firms, corporate legal departments, and law schools utilize AltaClaro to develop lawyers who are prepared to contribute from day one.\nDepoSim , our newest product developed in partnership with Verbit, is the world\u2019s first AI-powered deposition simulator. With DepoSim, attorneys can conduct full simulated depositions against dynamic AI witnesses and opposing counsel, adjust scenarios in real time, and receive structured, rubric-based feedback after each session. DepoSim delivers meaningful, repeatable deposition practice at an unprecedented scale.\nAltaClaro received the prestigious 2025 Legalweek Leaders in Tech Law Award for Best Tech Training Provider. DepoSim was also named a finalist for the 2026 Legalweek Leaders in Tech Award in the Best Tech Training Program category.\nOur impressive client roster includes Am Law 200 firms such as Orrick, K&L Gates, McDermott, A&O Shearman, Taft Polsinelli, and other prominent legal organizations.\nWe are a rapidly growing startup dedicated to fundamentally transforming how lawyers develop practical skills. Our mission is to effectively bridge the gap between law school theory and real-world practice, while also providing continuous learning for professional development throughout a lawyer's career.\nAbout the Role \nWe are seeking a driven and entrepreneurial Junior Account Executive to join our growing team. This is a remote, US-based position reporting directly to leadership. You will be responsible for generating qualified meetings with decision-makers at large law firms, and running some demos primarily through outbound prospecting.\nThis role is ideal for someone who thrives in a startup environment, enjoys the hunt, and is excited about building something meaningful with direct access to founders.\nWhat You'll Do \nPipeline Generation & Prospecting \nOutbound Prospecting (90%): Proactively identify, research, and reach out to prospects at Am Law 200 law firms through multi-channel outreach (LinkedIn, email, phone, video)\nInbound Lead Management (10%): Respond to and qualify inbound inquiries from marketing campaigns, webinars, and website traffic\nBook Qualified Meetings: Build relationships with qualified leads and schedule meetings for the Founder and Account Executive.\nRun Product Demos: Lead product demonstrations for some prospective clients while developing the skills and experience needed to take on increasing responsibility and grow within the organization.\nAccount Research: Conduct thorough research on target accounts, understanding firm structure, recent news, strategic initiatives, and key stakeholders\nQualification & Discovery \nConduct Discovery Calls: Run 15-minute discovery calls to gauge interest, understand pain points, and qualify prospects before scheduling demos\nIdentify Decision-Makers: Map out buying committees and identify Professional Development leaders, Practice Group Leaders, and other key stakeholders\nQualify Opportunities: Use qualification frameworks (BANT, MEDDIC, or similar) to ensure prospects are a good fit\nNurturing & Follow-Up \nNurture Prospects: Drip on and follow up with prospects who aren't immediately ready to buy\nMaintain Engagement: Keep prospects warm through relevant content sharing, check-ins, and relationship building\nEvent Follow-Up: Follow up on leads from legal industry conferences, CLEs, and webinars\nCollaboration & Reporting \nCollaborate with Leadership: Work closely with founders and sales leadership on strategy, messaging, and feedback loops\nPartner with Marketing: Provide feedback on campaigns, content effectiveness, and market insights\nManage Pipeline: Track all activity, prospect information, and pipeline metrics in HubSpot\nReport on KPIs: Maintain accurate records and report on activities, conversion rates, and pipeline contribution\nWho You Are \nRequired Experience & Skills \n2+ years of experience as a Junior Account Executive, BDR, SDR, or in a similar sales development role\nExperience with enterprise sales and selling to complex, sophisticated buyers\nProficiency with HubSpot or Salesforce (HubSpot strongly preferred)\nProven multi-channel outreach skills (LinkedIn, email, phone)\nStrong written and verbal communication skills\nExperience with sales engagement tools (e.g., Outreach, SalesLoft, Apollo, LinkedIn Sales Navigator)\nAbility to quickly learn and articulate complex product offerings\nSelf-starter who can work independently in a remote environment\nPreferred Experience \nBackground in SaaS, Legal, LegalTech, FinTech, EdTech or Financial Services\nExperience selling to law firms, professional services, banks, or regulated industries\nExperience with ABM (Account-Based Marketing) strategies\nCore Traits We're Looking For \nHunter Mentality: You don't wait for leads\u2014you go find them\nOwnership & Adaptability: Comfortable working in a smaller team with less process; you figure things out\nCoachable: Receptive to feedback and eager to improve\nHigh Emotional Intelligence: Personable and able to engage busy, senior decision-makers\nEntrepreneurial & Curious: Excited about startups and continuous learning\nNo Ego: Collaborative, humble, and team-oriented\n\"Whatever It Takes\" Attitude: Willing to do what's needed to succeed\nResilience: Thick-skinned and persistent in the face of rejection\nIntellectual Curiosity: Genuine interest in the legal industry and professional development space\nStrong Work Ethic: Disciplined, organized, and committed to hitting goals\nOur Target Market \nYou'll be selling to Partners, Practice Group Leaders, Professional Development (PD) managers, Directors of Attorney Development, and other decision-makers at Am Law 200 law firms\u2014the top law firms in the US by revenue. These are sophisticated, busy buyers who require a consultative, intelligent approach.\nWhat Success Looks Like \nIn Your First 30 Days: \nComplete onboarding and product training\nUnderstand AltaClaro's value proposition, ICP, and competitive landscape\nShadow discovery calls and demos with leadership\nBegin building your target account list\nIn Your First 60 Days: \nExecute outbound campaigns independently\nBook your first qualified meetings\nDevelop your own messaging and sequences based on what's working\nIn Your First 90 Days: \nConsistently hit weekly meeting targets\nContribute insights to improve sales processes and messaging\nBuild strong relationships with prospects in your territory\nCompensation & Benefits \nBase Salary: $75,000\nOTE: $100,000-120,000 (commission based on qualified meetings booked + percentage of closed sales)\nUncapped Commission\nStock Options\nHealth Benefits: Medical, Dental, Vision\nUnlimited PTO\nRemote Work: Fully remote position with flexible working arrangements\nWhy Join AltaClaro? \nDirect Founder Access: Work closely with leadership and have real impact on company direction\nStartup Environment: Build and shape processes, not just follow them\nGrowth Opportunity: Join a company at an exciting stage with clear paths for advancement (Junior Account Executive \u2192 AE and beyond)\nMeaningful Product: Help law firms develop their attorneys' practical skills and make a real difference in professional careers\nSupportive Culture: Collaborative, feedback-driven team that invests in your development\nInterview Process \nInitial Screen: Brief call with hiring team to discuss your background and interest\nSkills Assessment: Role-play/simulation exercise to assess prospecting and discovery skills\nDeep Dive Interview: In-depth conversation on experience, approach, and culture fit\nReferences: We'll speak with previous managers about your performance and coachability\nWe assess candidates on coachability, curiosity, communication skills, and ability to learn our product quickly. \nAltaClaro is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. \nAltaClaro asks respectfully to only apply through the application form and not email/apply to them directly. Recruiters and Agencies please do not contact AltaClaro directly.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-15T04:07:26.913Z","expires_at":"2026-07-15T04:07:26.913Z","external_id":"altaclaro","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/netreputation1/remote-job/account-executive-orm-seo","title":"Account Executive - ORM/SEO","company":"NetReputation","location":"Remote","description":"Online Reputation Management, Crisis Management, Public Relations, SEO & Digital Marketing Services \nAbout NetReputation \nNetReputation is the premier online reputation management firm trusted by the world's most recognized Enterprise and SMB brands, influential executives, and discerning private individuals. Through a powerful fusion of advanced content strategy, crisis response, reputation monitoring, review management, digital privacy, and precision SEO, we help our clients take control of their digital narrative, shaping how the world sees you and your brand to ensure you dominate the search results that matter most.\nPosition Overview \nAs an Account Executive, you will own the full sales cycle, from qualifying inbound leads to closing, using a consultative approach to solve high stakes reputation and crisis management challenges. You will sell comprehensive ORM and Digital Marketing Services (SEO, content creation, social media, and paid search) to chief executives, marketing directors, business owners, and high net worth individuals, driving the next stage of growth for SMB and enterprise brands. This is not a SaaS selling role and we're looking for someone who has sold deals within the ORM, SEO, or Digital Marketing Services. \nKey Responsibilities \nGenerate Revenue: Own the full sales process from lead qualification through custom presentations, ROI analysis, fee negotiation, SOW review, and closing new business in the ORM and Digital Marketing space\nConsultative Selling: Conduct deep dive discovery sessions to understand prospect pain points, analyze their digital footprint, and tailor solutions that build trust and protect credibility\nPresentation and Pitching: Deliver compelling presentations to executive level stakeholders and high net worth individuals using tools such as SERP analysis and reputation scorecards\nPipeline Management: Manage a high volume pipeline, maintain accurate CRM records, and ensure a steady flow of qualified leads\nStrategic Collaboration: Partner with internal strategy, SEO, and content teams to develop customized proposals\nNegotiation: Close complex, long term contractual agreements and retainer based services\nAccount Growth: Build post sale relationships and identify upsell opportunities for clients\nQualifications \n2-3+ years of experience selling ORM, digital marketing, or PR services to SMB and Enterprise brands\nStrategic thinker with strong consultative selling instincts\nExceptional presenter, able to communicate complex ORM, crisis management, and digital strategies to senior stakeholders\nProficient in CRM platforms (Salesforce, Zoho, or HubSpot) and SEO/reputation tools (BrightEdge, SEMrush, Ahrefs, Meltwater)\nBachelor's degree required\nWhy Join Us? \nCompetitive Compensation: Base salary plus uncapped commission\nTop Tier Tools: Comprehensive digital audits and proprietary tools to support your sales process\nStrong Support System: Backed by a world class Strategy and Client Success team so you can focus on closing\nBenefits \nOTE: $150,000-$175,000\nHealth\u00a0Insurance\nDental\u00a0Insurance\nVision\u00a0Insurance\n401(k)\u00a0Matching\nFlexible\u00a0Paid\u00a0Time\u00a0Off\nWork\u00a0Location \nFully\u00a0Remote\u00a0\u2014\u00a0with\u00a0the\u00a0option\u00a0to\u00a0work\u00a0from\u00a0our\u00a0Sarasota,\u00a0FL\u00a0headquarters\nNetReputation asks respectfully to only apply through the application form and not email/apply to them directly. Recruiters and Agencies please do not contact NetReputation directly.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-15T04:05:01.326Z","expires_at":"2026-07-15T04:05:01.326Z","external_id":"netreputation1","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/styledsettings/remote-job/ai-visual-designer-e-commerce-dtc","title":"AI Visual Designer (E-commerce / DTC)","company":"Styled Settings","location":"Remote","description":"Full-time B2B Contract \u00b7 Remote position \u00b7 Remote (Open to candidates across EMEA & LATAM)\u00a0 \u00b7 Fluent written and spoken English required \nAbout Us \nWe're a small, fast-growing premium e-commerce brand in the home goods space, built by a lean team with a big vision. We've already scaled multiple product lines to multi-seven-figure success, and we're not slowing down.\nOur work lives at the intersection of design, storytelling, and technology. Our customers are women 25\u201355 who want elevated design and aspirational storytelling \u2013 not just a product that works. Every image, word, and touchpoint is held to a premium bar, and increasingly, AI is how we hit that bar faster without lowering it.\nIf you want to see your creative vision come to life, on a small team where every voice matters, you'll feel at home here.\nThe Role \nPlease note: This isn't a general graphic design role. It blends creative direction and execution: you look at a new product and instantly see the vision \u2014 moodboard, look, feel \u2014 then bring it to life through AI-generated video and image creative, at a premium, editorial standard.\u00a0\nYou'll set the creative direction, not just execute someone else's brief:\nDefine the visual direction and moodboards for new product launches across sales and marketing channels\nProduce the creative yourself, using AI video (Higgsfield or equivalent) and product photography blended with AI image generation, with genuine brand sensibility \u2013 not just tool proficiency\nGuide our graphic designer on execution, reviewing their work to hold the premium bar\nWork inside a structured brief \u2192 generation \u2192 QA \u2192 live-ad pipeline\nReport to our Creative Ops Manager, with our Creative Director reviewing direction and setting the final quality bar\nOne clarification upfront: you'll drive creative vision day to day \u2013 final sign-off sits with our Creative Director. This is a high-ownership, hands-on contributor role \u2013 not a people-management title.\nRequirements \nMust have:\nAI video generation (Higgsfield or equivalent), used with real creative judgment \u2013 you're actively experimenting and staying current in AI + creative tools, not just running defaults\nAI image generation with brand sensibility \u2013 can work from direction and hold visual consistency across a product line\nStatic creative capability \u2013 you know how content specs and placement requirements work, and you\u2019re comfortable with moving across platforms as the brand expands\nA portfolio showing creative direction you've actually driven \u2013 moodboards, concepts, premium/editorial finished work. Genuine passion for style, fashion, interiors, or high-end lifestyle \u2013 not just the ability to mimic it. Come ready to walk us through specific examples\nStrong communication and collaboration skills \u2013 comfortable balancing speed with premium-quality output in a fast-paced environment\nFluent written and spoken English\nNice to have:\nExperience with Amazon or DTC brand creative specifically\nComfortable using references and prompts to develop examples and visual concepts\nComfortable in Figma, Photoshop, and Premiere for finishing and compositing\nThe Opportunity \nThis is a high-leverage seat. You'd be one of two designers building a creative department close to scratch, on a brand that's already proven it can scale. Your work will directly influence how our products show up, convert, and scale across e-commerce channels - giving you a rare opportunity to see the commercial impact of your creative decisions fast.\nIf you want real ownership over creative direction, fast iteration with AI, and a team that will actually let you set the vision \u2013 we'd love to hear from you\nProcess \nOur process includes a screening and portfolio review and a real brief exercise \u2013 a lightweight version of an actual product brief \u2013 so you can show us how you think and work.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Belarus","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Czechia","Estonia","Georgia","Greece","Hungary","Kosovo","Latvia","Lithuania","Moldova","Montenegro","North Macedonia","Poland","Romania","Serbia","Slovakia","Ukraine"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-08T07:10:55.622Z","expires_at":"2026-08-07T07:10:55.622Z","external_id":"styledsettings","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/levelupleads/remote-job/sales-development-representative-sdr","title":"Sales Development Representative (SDR)","company":"LevelUp Leads","location":"Remote","description":"Must be a native English speaker. You must submit a video or we will not consider your application. \nPosition : Sales Development Representative (SDR)\nLocation : Fully Remote (Preferably based in LATAM)\nWorking Hours : 7-8 hours per day, Monday - Friday\nSalary : $3600 USD per month + commissions. The average full-time SDR earns\n$4500/month. Many in the $5000-$6500+/month range.\nAbout Us: \nLevelUp Leads is an SDR appointment setting agency focused on providing lead generation and sales solutions for our clients. Our mission is to help companies scale by connecting them with high-quality leads and opportunities.\nKey Responsibilities: \nConduct cold calls and cold emails to prospective clients\nQualify leads and set up meetings for your clients sales team\nMaintain accurate and up-to-date records of all sales activities in the dashboard and/or CRMs such as HubSpot or Salesforce\nFollow up on leads and nurture relationships to convert prospects into clients\nCollaborate with the sales team to develop strategies for lead generation and sales\nRequirements: \nNative English speaker\nExperience in sales, with a strong emphasis on cold calling\nFamiliarity with HubSpot or Salesforce\nTech experience is a plus\nExcellent communication and interpersonal skills\nAbility to work independently and manage time effectively\nReliable internet connection and a quiet workspace for remote work\nPreference for candidates based in or looking to relocate to LATAM\nBenefits: \nCompetitive salary of $3600 per month (at full client capacity), you can potentially take on more\nFully remote position with flexible working hours\nOpportunity to work with a dynamic and supportive team\nPotential for growth and advancement within the company","locations":["Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","United States","Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Canada"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-07T12:01:04.262Z","expires_at":"2026-08-06T12:01:04.262Z","external_id":"levelupleads","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/thefuturesocietyllc/remote-job/interim-operations-lead-integrator-4-week-contract-starts-immediately","title":"Interim Operations Lead / Integrator (4-Week Contract \u2014 Starts Immediately)","company":"TheFutureSociety LLC","location":"Remote","description":"\u23f1\ufe0f We are interviewing this week and the role starts within days of posting, July 6, 2026.\nCompany: TheFutureSociety \u2014 a profitable, founder-led startup approaching its one-year anniversary next month. We operate three brands: The Tarot Ship (291K YouTube subscribers), Great Awakener (premium livestream membership platform), and MAX: Your Virtual Oracle Gateway , the world's first predictive AI platform that integrates a user's birth chart \u2014 launched four weeks ago to immediate traction.\nWho we are: A lean, remote team of five \u2014 ops/creative lead, engineer, partnerships manager, writer/researcher, and support. We're not a corporation with layers; we're a fast-moving startup that grew faster than its org chart. This role exists because our permanent fractional Head of Operations starts early August, and we need a senior operator to run the day-to-day between now and then. Your job is to hold the ship steady, tighten the systems, hand off clean \u2014 and protect the founder's time.\nEngagement: Fractional, 20-25 hours/week. Fixed-term from immediate start through August 6, 2026. Hard stop \u2014 your final deliverable is a clean handoff package for our incoming permanent Head of Operations. Remote \u2014 US or Latin America.\nCompensation: $6,000\u2013$8,000 flat for the full engagement, paid weekly, final payment released on handoff delivery. 1099 contractor. NDA + IP assignment signed before any system access.\nReports to: Founder/CEO. The mandate is simple: the Founder steps fully out of operations for four weeks. You run it; he creates.\nResponsibilities: \nTeam oversight: Coordination, accountability across 6-person team; daily async check-ins with our contractors and vendors; overseeing campaigns and launch of membership perks program late July; weekly written status to the Founder; enforce documentation, logged work from everyone, especially any tech bugs/fixes\nPartnerships continuity: Our Partnerships Manager is on reduced availability for three weeks; he's left a live pipeline doc (brand and talent) and sends updates twice weekly \u2014 you keep his active deals warm and moving, prepare and redline any necessary contracts; escalate decisions to the Founder only when needed\nHiring: Recruit and onboard (with our ops/creative lead) one combined Social Media Lead/Video Editor/Livestream Moderator using our established four-step hiring funnel; scope, shortlist a Meta Ads freelancer/agency for Founder decision\nPayroll and contractor payments on schedule (Gusto, ACH \u2014 all already set up)\nProtect recurring revenue operations: Oversee the failed-payment recovery workstream, cancellation saves, and checkout integrity\nHandoff package: SOPs, contractor roster, open items, metrics baseline\nYou're right for this if: You've operated a subscription, membership, creator-economy, or DTC digital business; you've managed small distributed contractor teams; you're fluent in Stripe and email automation; you can start within 2-3 business days; you're OK to hop in on a weekend should anything arise; and you find a four-week \"own everything, leave it better, hand off clean\" sprint energizing rather than daunting.\nProcess: ops/creative lead call \u2192 reference check \u2192 30-minute Founder call \u2192 NDA/IP assignment \u2192 least-privilege access \u2192 start.","locations":["Canada","United States"],"employment_type":"CONTRACTOR","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-06T23:16:29.457Z","expires_at":"2026-08-05T23:16:29.457Z","external_id":"thefuturesocietyllc","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/clickguardinc/remote-job/head-of-operations-2","title":"Head of Operations","company":"ClickGUARD Inc.","location":"Remote","description":"ClickGUARD is a SaaS startup operating in a domain where ad tech meets cybersecurity. Our platform helps Google Ads advertisers protect their investment and maximize their ROI by detecting and removing wasteful ad traffic from their advertising campaigns. We\u2019ve built the absolute best solution for a significant problem for PPC advertisers, and we need your help taking it to the next level of user experience.\nAbout the role \nWe are seeking a high-leverage, systems-driven Head of Operations to own the execution of ClickGuard's business plan and lead our day-to-day operations. This is the classic EOS Integrator role adapted for a high-velocity, \"AI-First\" environment. You will serve as the organizational anchor, financial gatekeeper, and structural tie-breaker for the leadership team, freeing the Visionary (CEO) to focus entirely on macro strategy and long-term vision.\nYour superpower is not just \"managing process,\u201d but rather balancing a vision with deep emotional intelligence. You don\u2019t just build processes, you act as the cultural glue and coach for the distributed team. It\u2019s forcing structure onto chaos, mandating data truth, removing cross-functional barriers, and ruthlessly driving the Leadership Team to achieve our core financial and operational Rocks.\nYou will directly manage the Leadership Team (Sales, Customer Success, Product, Engineering, and Finance) and hold full accountability for the company's execution, P&L performance, and operating leverage.\nKey Responsibilities \nOperations Enablement \nDirect Team Management: Manage, lead, and hold accountable the cross-functional Leadership Team (Sales Lead, Engineering Lead, and interim functional seats).\nThe Cultural Glue: Act as the ultimate bridge between remote, async-first departments, breaking down operational silos and maintaining high team energy, alignment, and psychological safety.\nThe Visionary/Integrator Dynamic: Partner with the CEO (Visionary) to filter macro strategy into executable 90-day Company Rocks, protecting the team from operational drag, scope creep, and non-core initiatives.\nP&L & Business Plan Execution \nFinancial Accountability: Own the execution of the business plan to protect gross margins and scale revenue without proportional headcount growth.\nUnit Economic Optimization: Systematically monitor and optimize cross-functional metrics (specifically targeting customer payback periods) and LTV benchmarks ($7.5k Human Setup standard).\nTie-Breaking: Act as the final operational tie-breaker for all cross-functional disputes, resolving conflicts through data-driven objective \"Truth\" combined with empathetic\nWorkflow & Systems Engineering \nHubSpot Architectural Integrity: Maintain and audit our single source of truth (HubSpot CRM), ensuring all cross-functional lifecycles, handoffs, and outbound outreach cadences are cleanly instrumented and automated.\nAI-First Process Automation: Ruthlessly identify manual bottlenecks across GTM and operations, replacing legacy processes with autonomous AI agents and automated workflows to maintain exceptional operating leverage.\nFriction Elimination: Bridge the gap between Engineering velocity, Product discovery, and Customer Success to minimize product friction and eliminate the Month 3 retention drops.\nRequired Skills & Experience \n5\u201310+ Years as an Integrator/COO: Proven experience operating as a formal Integrator (EOS/Traction framework experience highly preferred) or Operations Role in a B2B SaaS or High-Velocity Agency environment.\nP&L Management: Concrete experience owning or protecting an operating budget, managing margins, and executing a business plan.\nSystems Architecture Mindset: You do not just \"oversee\" software; you architect workflows. You think in inputs, logic gates, and automated outputs.\nHigh-Spine Accountability: Comfortable having difficult, candid conversations. You manage by objective metrics and have a track record of identifying and transitioning underperforming talent.\nCoaching & People Development: A proven track record of mentoring and scaling distributed teams in async-first environments. You know how to develop \"A-Players\" and manage remote team dynamics.\nBias for High Operating Leverage: A deep commitment to scaling software and AI capabilities over human headcount.\nTechnical Proficiency \nClickUp: Expert-level project workflow management, productivity tracking, and AI automation.\nHubSpot CRM Ecosystem: (Expert Level) Absolute mastery of pipeline structures, custom properties, cross-object workflows, and server-side data instrumentation.\nProject Management Suites: Deep familiarity with modern PM frameworks (ClickUp, Linear, or equivalent agile/sprint tracking tools).\nData Visualization & BI: Ability to construct, audit, and read executive dashboards to enforce scorecard visibility.\nAutomation Engineering: Strong conceptual and execution knowledge of automated workflows (Make, Zapier, or native AI-agent integrations).\nLogistics \nRemote, async-first team culture.\nMust have overlapping availability for live syncs between 8 AM and 4 PM EST .\nFull-time, long-term leadership position.\nWho You Are \nAn Architectural Thinker: You look at a business and see an interconnected machine. You naturally classify problems into Target, Machine, or Fuel issues.\nRuthlessly Analytical: You do not make decisions based on \"gut feeling\" or \"team vibes.\" You demand data \"Truth.\"\nComfortable in Ambiguity: You don't need a playbook written for you; your job is to build the definitive playbook for everyone else.\nWhat\u2019s in it for you? \nCompetitive salary - Compensation that reflects your expertise and contributions.\nHigh-impact role \u2013 You\u2019ll be leading product decisions in a company that values speed, innovation, and customer obsession.\nHands-on environment \u2013 We operate lean, so your contributions will be direct and meaningful.\nFast-growing industry \u2013 AdTech / MarTech is a quickly evolving space, making this an exciting space to be in.\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, age, or any other characteristic.\nPLEASE NO RECRUITERS OR AGENCIES","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Canada","Georgia"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-02T19:23:43.653Z","expires_at":"2026-08-01T19:23:43.653Z","external_id":"clickguardinc","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/freightsimple/remote-job/finance-analyst","title":"Finance Analyst","company":"FreightSimple","location":"Remote","description":"\ud83e\uddee The short version \nYou love working with data and you love finance. You\u2019re happiest when you can pull the numbers yourself, write a query to answer a question, and turn a messy spreadsheet into a clear story. You\u2019d rather find the insight than wait for someone else to hand it to you.\nIf that\u2019s you, keep reading.\n\ud83d\ude80 Why this role is different \nAt our core we\u2019re a technology company, and our data is a first-class asset. Our accounts receivable and accounts payable are largely automated, so this isn\u2019t a data-entry job. It\u2019s a data-analysis one.\nYou\u2019ll spend your time asking questions of the data and answering them yourself, then turning those answers into reports leadership actually uses. \nYou\u2019ll support the finance function with analysis, reporting, and reconciliation. You\u2019ll write SQL against our systems, build and improve management reports, and help us understand what\u2019s really happening behind margins, freight bills, and claims.\n\ud83d\udca1 The honest pitch \nModern, automated systems plus AI tools mean you spend your time on analysis and insight, not manual reconciliations. If you like SQL and finance in equal measure, this is a rare combination.\n\u2728 What you\u2019ll actually do \n\ud83d\udcca Build and improve management reports and the numbers leadership relies on\n\ud83d\udd0d Write SQL to answer finance and operations questions directly from the data\n\ud83d\udcc8 Analyse margins, freight costs, and trends , and explain what\u2019s driving them\n\ud83e\uddfe Support accounts receivable and accounts payable with reconciliation and analysis\n\ud83d\udce6 Dig into cargo claims and freight bill data to spot patterns and anomalies\n\u2699\ufe0f Improve the data and processes behind reporting, with engineering when needed\nWe don\u2019t expect experience in everything. We just ask that you\u2019re eager to learn, and we\u2019ll get you up to speed fast.\n\ud83c\udfaf What we\u2019re looking for \n\ud83d\udcca Strong analytical skills and genuine comfort working with data\n\ud83d\uddc4\ufe0f Hands-on SQL and confidence querying data yourself\n\ud83d\udd2c A data science or analytics background is a real plus\n\ud83e\udd16 Experience using AI tools in your work, and eagerness to get more out of them\n\ud83d\udcbb Some coding experience (ideally, not required)\n\ud83e\uddfe Experience with standard finance team functions such as AR, AP, bookkeeping, and reporting\n\ud83d\udcbc Experience with spreadsheets and reporting tools (Xero is easy to pick up, no prior experience needed)\n\ud83d\ude9b Ideally knowledge of the freight or logistics industry \n\u270d\ufe0f Excellent written and verbal English \n\ud83e\udde9 Strong problem-solving and an eye for detail\n\u23f1\ufe0f Sharp time management and comfort with modern software\n\ud83d\udc99 Why you\u2019ll love working here \n\ud83c\udfe1 Fully remote , with a team that genuinely respects work-life balance\n\u2699\ufe0f Modern, automated systems and clean data to work with\n\ud83d\udde3\ufe0f A real voice in how things are measured and how the business understands itself\n\ud83e\udd1d A calm, supportive culture with friendly people who have your back\n\ud83e\udd16 AI tools to help you work smarter and more efficiently\n\ud83d\ude80 Thorough onboarding and ongoing support\n\ud83d\udcb0 Competitive compensation \nIf you want to answer real questions with real data, let\u2019s talk.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-01T23:19:18.899Z","expires_at":"2026-07-31T23:19:18.899Z","external_id":"freightsimple","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/ucmpracticegrowthsystems/remote-job/ads-specialist-1-800-2-000-mo","title":"Ads Specialist ($1,800-$2,000/mo)","company":"UCM Practice Growth Systems","location":"Remote","description":"Ads Specialist (US Time Zone Business Hours) \nNOTE: Applicants MUST read this entire job posting and complete all steps outlined below to be considered for this position.\nOur Mission: \nAt UCM Practice Growth Systems, we're not just a consulting agency; we're a team on a mission. Dedicated to the glory of God, we aim to bring hope and healing to sick and suffering people through our partnership with upper cervical chiropractors.\nYour Role in Our Mission: \nWe're looking for an Ads Specialist who thrives on performance, loves solving marketing challenges, and is passionate about helping local businesses grow through strategic advertising.\nThe ideal candidate is:\nHungry, driven, and committed to continuous learning and professional growth.\nAvailable to work within U.S. business hours (PST, MST, CST, or EST time zone).\nAn exceptional communicator who is reliable, organized, and represents both our agency and our clients professionally.\nExperienced in managing paid advertising campaigns for local businesses within a marketing agency environment.\nData-driven and analytical, with the ability to diagnose whether campaign issues stem from traffic quality, click-through rates, landing page conversion, or follow-up systems\u2014and confidently develop solutions to improve performance.\nHighly skilled in Meta Ads (Facebook, Instagram), Google Search, TikTok, and other paid advertising platforms, with a strong understanding of campaign structure, optimization, and scaling.\nKnowledgeable in the psychology behind Interruption Marketing (Facebook, Instagram, TikTok) versus Intent Marketing (Google Search), and able to structure campaigns appropriately for each platform.\nAble to create thumb-stopping ad campaigns that combine compelling creative, persuasive direct-response copywriting, and strong calls-to-action that generate qualified leads.\nExperienced in building high-performing Google Search campaigns with tightly themed ad groups, keyword relevance, compelling ad copy, and strategic use of ad assets such as Sitelinks, Callouts, and Structured Snippets.\nSkilled in Conversion Rate Optimization (CRO), with the ability to identify landing page weaknesses, improve message match between ads and landing pages, and optimize the user journey for higher conversion rates.\nFamiliar with the StoryBrand SB7 Framework and able to incorporate its principles into ad messaging and creative strategy.\nExperienced in conducting demographic, audience, and market research to develop highly targeted campaigns.\nA strong copywriter who understands consumer psychology, attention-grabbing hooks, persuasive messaging, and conversion-focused offers.\nPassionate about staying ahead of digital marketing trends, emerging advertising platforms, and new opportunities for local business growth.\nComfortable leveraging AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and others to accelerate research, brainstorming, creative development, copywriting, and campaign optimization\u2014not simply generating generic ad copy.\nBonus Skills (Highly Preferred)\nExperience with GoHighLevel (GHL)\nMarketing reporting automation and dashboard creation\nBasic Video editing skills\nGraphic design experience using Canva, Photoshop, or similar tools\nFamiliarity with various AI tools and prompt engineering\nKey Responsibilities \nPlan, launch, manage, and optimize paid advertising campaigns across Meta (Facebook & Instagram), Google Ads, and test other supported platforms.\nDevelop data-driven advertising strategies based on client goals, target audience, demographics, and budget.\nConduct audience, competitor, and market research to improve campaign targeting and performance.\nWrite high-converting ad copy and collaborate on creative development using StoryBrand SB7 and direct-response marketing principles.\nContinuously test and optimize headlines, copy, creative, audiences, offers, landing pages, and campaign structure to improve results.\nMonitor campaign performance daily, analyzing key metrics such as CTR, CPC, CPL, conversion rate, ROAS, and lead quality, while implementing data-driven improvements.\nAudit and suggest landing page optimizations to increase conversion rates by strengthening messaging, user experience, and calls to action.\nLeverage AI tools to accelerate research, copywriting, creative ideation, reporting, and workflow efficiency while maintaining high-quality human oversight.\nCreate clear performance reports and communicate campaign insights, recommendations, and next steps to internal leadership.\nMaintain organized campaign documentation, tracking, naming conventions, and internal processes.\nSchedule and manage client social media content, and optimize YouTube and Facebook video publishing to maximize reach, engagement, and lead generation.\nStay current on advertising platform updates, emerging AI tools, and digital marketing best practices to continually improve client results.\nTake ownership of campaign performance by consistently improving lead quality, lowering acquisition costs, increasing conversions, and maximizing return on ad spend (ROAS).\nCompensation & Benefits: \n$1800 per month base salary\nPerformance Bonuses for hitting CTR and CPL FB Targets ($100 Monthly bonus for each)\nUpper Cervical Chiropractic Care 100% reimbursed after 90 days of employment\u00a0\nMajor Medical Policy Health Insurance. We Pay 50% of a Major Medical Policy's monthly premiums after 90 days of employment.\u00a0\nVarious Professional & Personal Development Training Opportunities immediately available\nPaid time off after a 90-day probationary period\nComplimentary Attendance in Financial Peace University after 90 days of employment\u00a0\nMonthly Profit Sharing Bonuses after 365 Days of Employment\u00a0\nOpportunities for advancement in leadership and management\nWork within a Christ-centered, mission-driven organization\nMeet the UCM Team https://uppercervicalmarketing.com/upper-cervical-marketing-team/ and Explore Our Core Values https://uppercervicalmarketing.com/about-us/ at this link.\nHow to Apply:\nAre you ready to step into a role where your work truly matters? If you share our dedication to bringing hope and healing to sick and suffering people for the glory of God, follow the link below:\nTo apply, click the \u2018Apply Now\u2019 button to submit your application.\nHours: Full-time remotely\nJob Type: Full-time\nExpected hours: 40 per week\nLanguage: English (Required)","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-30T05:54:14.037Z","expires_at":"2026-07-30T05:54:14.037Z","external_id":"ucmpracticegrowthsystems","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/tulsainternetmarketing/remote-job/agency-operations-manager","title":"Agency Operations Manager","company":"Tulsa Internet Marketing","location":"Remote","description":"Agency Operations Manager\nYou become the person the agency runs through \u2014 not a project-management seat. This is a hands-in-the-work seat, every day. You are not supervising a team of doers from above. You are the person clearing the path, so finished work actually ships.\nLocation: Remote \u2014 Latin America (US Central Time overlap)\nType: Full-time\nPay: $2,400 \u2013 $3,200/month USD to start, paid in USD\nCompany: 6-person US digital-marketing agency\nReports to: Founder / CEO, directly\nWhy This Role Exists\nRight now, too much of this business runs through one person: the founder. Work piles up at his desk waiting for a decision, an approval, or someone to route it to the right contractor or team member. We already proved the projects can get managed, and the founder still isn\u2019t free, which tells us something important. The bottleneck was never project management. The bottleneck is operational judgment, and right now it lives in one head.\nYour entire job is to own the space between \u201cdone\u201d and \u201cshipped.\u201d You become the place work flows through instead of the place it waits. When this role is working, the founder stops being the answer to every \u201ccan you check this?\u201d and gets to go back to building the business.\nWhat You Actually Do\nThis is not a \"point and manage\" role. Every week, work is stalled, half-finished, or quietly failing somewhere across our clients and contractors, and clearing it is the job. You make the decision that unblocks the next step, and when the fastest way to move something is to get in yourself, you get in. You know the difference between doing the work to restore momentum and permanently becoming the bottleneck. The first is the job. The second is the failure.\nTake incoming work, route it to the right person, and own the handoff until it is finished. Not fire-and-forget.\nMake the call that unblocks the next step today, instead of scheduling a meeting to discuss it.\nRun and extend our SOP library (roughly 85 documented processes). When a decision keeps coming back to you, capture it once so it never comes back again.\nManage team and contractor capacity, what ships, and ad spend. You become the primary operational reviewer of our work, escalating only the strategic or client-sensitive calls.\nYou produce flow, not output. The moment you become the person personally doing the task every week instead of the person making it move, the role has failed. \nWhat that looks like in practice: \nA team member or contractor goes quiet with a deliverable half-done. You don\u2019t send a reminder and wait. You get a second team member or contractor on it, and the work ships.\nA funnel is 95 percent built. You log in, check it against our standards, find the two things that are off, send them back, and have it live before the day ends.\nAn automation is failing. You reproduce the problem, loop in the right team member or contractor, confirm the fix, document it, and close the task to prevent it from resurfacing.\nNotice the pattern: you didn\u2019t personally build any of it, but you also didn\u2019t just manage someone else building it. You entered the work, restored momentum, and then made sure that particular fire couldn\u2019t start again.\nHow We Operate\nKeep it moving.\u00a0 Momentum is the job. If the fastest way to keep work moving is making a decision, make it. If it is calling a contractor, call them. If it is a two-minute Loom to clarify expectations, record it. Your job is to make sure work never stops because everyone is waiting on someone else.\nExtreme ownership.\u00a0 Mistakes are fine here. Failing to own them is not. We use \u201cI,\u201d not \u201cthey.\u201d This is the one thing we will not flex on. \nTreat the client\u2019s money like it\u2019s your own.\u00a0 This seat controls team and contractor hours, what ships, and ad spend. That makes it real, not a slogan.\nWe don\u2019t micromanage.\u00a0 If you need permission for every decision, you will not enjoy this role. We hire people we can hand consequences to and then get out of their way.\nWho This Is For\nYou are a doer whose instinct is to act, but whose goal is to build a system that needs less acting over time. You read a queue of stalled work and think, \u201cGive me two hours, and I\u2019ll have this moving,\u201d not \u201clet\u2019s review this in tomorrow\u2019s stand-up.\u201d You have run internal operations for a team before, on US business hours, in confident English. \nThis is NOT for you if: you need a written process to exist before you will act; you reach for a meeting instead of a decision; you want client-facing or strategy work and see execution as beneath you; or you are casual with money that isn\u2019t yours.\nWhat Success Looks Like\nBy your third month, work no longer waits on the founder to route or approve it. Nothing falls through the cracks between our client manager and the production team. The founder can step away for a week, and the operation keeps running. The real signal: the operation needs you less over time, because you keep tightening the flow itself instead of just working harder inside it.\nCompensation\n$2,400 to $3,200 per month USD to start, paid in USD. Pay is tied to demonstrated ownership, not a calendar, and it grows as you take on more of the operation. Strong operators have real room to move up from here over time.\nHow to Apply\nClick the Apply Now button to apply.\nIt's a short application with a few questions, not a quick click-to-apply. That's on purpose. We read for ownership, not polish.\nKnow someone who should see this? This role is unusual enough that the right operator usually hears about it from a person, not a board. Please pass it along.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-27T07:43:50.106Z","expires_at":"2026-07-27T07:43:50.106Z","external_id":"tulsainternetmarketing","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/hybrid85/remote-job/operations-manager","title":"Operations Manager","company":"Hybrid85","location":"Remote","description":"About us\nWe\u2019re a small, all-remote team behind three direct-to-farmer seed brands \u2014 Hybrid85 (non-GMO corn), Cover Crop Exchange (cover crop seed), and Override Ag (glyphosate-tolerant corn). We sell straight to farmers, skipping the legacy dealer network. We\u2019re profitable and growing, we invest in automation, and we hire people who take genuine ownership of their work.\nWe\u2019re hiring our first Operations Manager to own post-sale (and some pre-sale) operations end-to-end \u2014 email-first, customer-facing work \u2014 so the team can stay focused on growth, sales, and product. You\u2019re the person customers hear from, and the one who makes sure orders actually get where they\u2019re going.\nWhat you\u2019d own\nIn peak seasons (Feb\u2013April and Aug\u2013Nov), you own front-line customer support and the inbox (\u201cWhere\u2019s my seed?\u201d, order changes, problem resolution); shipping coordination (ship dates, tracking, freight status, lost-shipment follow-up); fulfillment problem-solving with our warehouses when an order is short, mislabeled, or needs redoing; and chasing down the supplier and warehouse paperwork that keeps our records accurate. In the calmer off-season, you track the team\u2019s projects and to-dos so they don\u2019t slip, handle recurring admin and compliance paperwork, coordinate occasional mailings, and help prepare for upcoming seasons.\nWho we\u2019re looking for\nTraits that matter far more than industry experience:\nYou communicate clearly and warmly in writing \u2014 you\u2019re the voice customers hear most, and you write calmly even when the inbox is stacked.\nYou operate independently \u2014 you make defensible calls when the picture is ~70% complete and loop owners in for genuine judgment calls, not every decision.\nYou own loose ends \u2014 when something lands in your lap with no clear owner, you take it, and you follow up on commitments without being reminded.\nYou\u2019re comfortable with new software \u2014 our stack changes and you\u2019ll live in our admin tools all day.\nYou reach for AI and new tools \u2014 we use AI heavily and we\u2019re leaning in harder as we grow. You should already use these tools by choice and be genuinely excited to push them further.\nWe\u2019ll teach you everything industry-specific. This is an email-first role \u2014 we care most about how you write and how you keep things from slipping.\nWhat to expect\nHigh autonomy \u2014 we\u2019re hiring you to own this, not to ask permission. You\u2019ll own our operations, not a team (no direct reports). Seasonal intensity \u2014 peak stretches are high-tempo; the rest of the year is calmer. We automate aggressively, and your job is to do the work and be our partner in deciding what to automate next. We\u2019re remote \u2014 you\u2019d report directly to a founder; the Lincoln, NE office is optional, otherwise work from wherever.\nCompensation & benefits\nBase salary $70,000\u2013$100,000 (depending on experience; we\u2019ll go higher for the right person), plus a performance bonus tied to peak-season outcomes, a $1,000/month healthcare stipend, and unlimited vacation.\nLocation & requirements\nRemote, US only \u2014 any time zone. Must have authorization to work in the US; we do not sponsor visas at this time. Roughly 40 hours/week.\nHow to apply\nClick the Apply Now button to apply.\nWe read every application and respond to everyone, even if it\u2019s a \u201cno.\u201d Hybrid85, Cover Crop Exchange, and Override Ag are equal opportunity employers.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-26T20:26:22.081Z","expires_at":"2026-07-26T20:26:22.081Z","external_id":"hybrid85","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/levelupleads/remote-job/paid-media-analyst","title":"Paid Media Analyst","company":"LevelUp Leads","location":"Remote","description":"About LevelUp Leads \nLevelUp Leads is a sales development and appointment setting agency.\nOur team becomes your sales development engine, providing the people, data, technology, and campaign execution to give you more selling opportunities.\nWe manage everything from data sourcing to copywriting to campaign management, creating more pipeline and revenue for your business.\nWe\u2019re now looking for a Paid Media Analyst who can plan, launch, manage, and optimize paid campaigns across LinkedIn Ads and Google Ads. This is a hands-on role for someone who understands performance marketing, B2B lead generation, testing, reporting, and campaign execution.\nWhat You\u2019ll Be Doing \nPlan, launch, and manage paid media campaigns across LinkedIn Ads and Google Ads\nBuild campaign structures based on audience, intent, funnel stage, and offer\nManage LinkedIn Ads campaigns focused on B2B lead generation, ABM, retargeting, and pipeline growth\nManage Google Ads campaigns, including Search, Display, Performance Max, and remarketing when needed\nConduct keyword research, audience research, competitor research, and campaign audits\nWrite and test ad copy variations for different campaigns and audience segments\nAnalyze campaign performance and recommend optimizations based on CPL, conversion rate, lead quality, and pipeline impact\nReview landing pages and suggest improvements to increase conversion rates\nWork with tracking tools such as GA4, Google Tag Manager, HubSpot, and ad platform pixels\nPrepare performance reports with clear insights, next steps, and optimization priorities\nCollaborate with the internal team on creative, copy, targeting, offers, and campaign strategy\nStay current with paid media trends, platform updates, and B2B advertising best practices\nWhat We\u2019re Looking For \n4+ years of experience in paid media, performance marketing, or digital advertising\nStrong hands-on experience with LinkedIn Ads and Google Ads is required\nExperience managing B2B lead generation campaigns is strongly preferred\nComfortable working with campaign budgets, targeting, bidding, conversion tracking, and reporting\nStrong understanding of funnel strategy, landing pages, audience segmentation, and retargeting\nExperience with GA4, Google Tag Manager, HubSpot, LinkedIn Campaign Manager, and Google Ads\nAble to analyze data and turn performance numbers into clear recommendations\nStrong writing skills for ad copy, campaign messaging, and performance insights\nC1 English level or above is required and will be tested\nAble to work independently, communicate clearly, and manage multiple accounts at once\nMust overlap at least half of your workday with CST/EST\nWhy Join LevelUp Leads? \nWork with a fast-growing, globally distributed team\nManage campaigns with a direct impact on pipeline and revenue\nCollaborate with a team that values ownership, creativity, testing, and results\nGet exposure to B2B growth, outbound strategy, paid acquisition, and sales development\nRemote-first environment with flexible collaboration","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-25T22:14:34.927Z","expires_at":"2026-07-25T22:14:34.927Z","external_id":"levelupleads","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/levelupleads/remote-job/mid-level-seo-analyst","title":"Mid-Level SEO Analyst","company":"LevelUp Leads","location":"Remote","description":"About LevelUp Leads \nLevelUp Leads is a sales development and appointment setting agency.\nOur team becomes your sales development engine, providing the people, data, technology, and campaign execution to give you more selling opportunities.\nWe manage everything from data sourcing to copywriting to campaign management, creating more pipeline and revenue for your business.\nWe\u2019re now looking for a Mid-Level SEO Analyst who can support and execute SEO strategies for B2B websites, with a strong understanding of technical SEO, content optimization, reporting, and the growing impact of AI search and LLMs.\nThis is a hands-on role for someone who can turn SEO strategy into real implementation, track performance, and help improve organic visibility across traditional search and AI-driven discovery.\nWhat You\u2019ll Be Doing \nExecute SEO strategies across multiple B2B/B2C websites\nConduct keyword research, competitor analysis, search intent analysis, and content gap research\nOptimize website pages for rankings, conversions, internal linking, metadata, structure, and topical relevance\nSupport SEO content planning, including briefs, outlines, article optimization, and content QA\nReview and improve technical SEO elements, including indexation, crawlability, site structure, schema markup, redirects, canonicals, and Core Web Vitals\nMonitor performance in Google Search Console, GA4, Ahrefs, SEMrush, Screaming Frog, and similar tools\nTrack rankings, traffic, conversions, and visibility trends across priority keywords and pages\nSupport AEO and AI search optimization for platforms such as Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Perplexity, and other LLM-driven search experiences\nHelp improve brand/entity visibility across search engines and AI platforms\nPrepare SEO reports with clear insights, completed work, opportunities, and next steps\nCollaborate with other teams to align SEO work with business goals\nStay current with algorithm updates, AI search changes, technical SEO best practices, and B2B content trends\nWhat We\u2019re Looking For \n4+ years of experience in SEO, preferably in a B2B, lead generation, SaaS, or agency environment\nStrong hands-on experience with on-page SEO, technical SEO, content optimization, and SEO reporting\nKnowledge of LLMs, AI search, AEO, Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Perplexity, and how AI platforms discover and surface brands\nComfortable using tools such as Google Search Console, GA4, Ahrefs, SEMrush, Screaming Frog, Google Tag Manager, and WordPress or similar CMS platforms\nAble to identify SEO issues, prioritize opportunities, and explain recommendations clearly\nStrong understanding of search intent, content structure, internal linking, schema markup, and topical authority\nComfortable working with multiple clients, deadlines, and SEO roadmaps\nStrong writing and editing skills for SEO recommendations, content briefs, metadata, and reporting\nC1 English level or above is required and will be tested\nAble to work independently, communicate clearly, and manage recurring SEO tasks with ownership\nMust overlap at least half of your workday with CST/EST\nWhy Join LevelUp Leads? \nWork with a fast-growing, globally distributed team\nManage campaigns with a direct impact on pipeline and revenue\nCollaborate with a team that values ownership, creativity, testing, and results\nGet exposure to B2B growth, outbound strategy, paid acquisition, and sales development\nRemote-first environment with flexible collaboration","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-25T22:10:18.605Z","expires_at":"2026-07-25T22:10:18.605Z","external_id":"levelupleads","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/ucmpracticegrowthsystems/remote-job/client-success-manager-4-000-5-000-mo-potential","title":"Client Success Manager ($4,000-$5,000/mo Potential)","company":"UCM Practice Growth Systems","location":"Remote","description":"Client Success Manager (Central or Eastern Time Zone) \nNOTE: Applicants MUST read this entire job posting and complete all steps outlined below to be considered for this position.\nOur Mission: \nAt UCM Practice Growth Systems, we're not just a consulting agency; we're a team on a mission. Dedicated to the glory of God, we aim to bring hope and healing to sick and suffering people through our partnership with upper cervical chiropractors.\nYour Role in Our Mission: \nWe are looking for a passionate, energetic, people-oriented leader to serve as a Client Success Manager. This role combines relationship-building, client success support, and management responsibilities. You will work closely with our Director of Client Success, the client success team, and the UCM leadership team to coach clients in our success principles, support their teams, perform review calls via zoom, capture happy client video testimonials, and encourage upgrades and referrals. If you love connecting with people and seeing them grow\u2014this role may be perfect for you.\nWho We Are Looking For: \nHigh energy personality (energetic, relational, outgoing, warm)\nHungry, driven, and eager to grow within a results oriented & impactful team\nUS-based, preferably in the Midwest or Southern US\nExperience in client success, account management, or sales\nPositive experience with Chiropractic (UC experience is a strong plus)\nStrong communication skills, reliability, and ability to represent our brand professionally\nExperience leading, managing and holding team members accountable to results\nKey Responsibilities \nLead client review calls daily (also preparation and data gathering for calls)\nManage the client success team and get great results\nBring energy, enthusiasm, and relational strength to every interaction\nCompensation & Benefits: \n$40,000 base annual starting salary\n25% commission on all upgrades ($1000-$2000/month potential)\nUpper Cervical Chiropractic Care 100% reimbursed immediately\nMajor Medical Policy Health Insurance. We Pay 50% of a Major Medical Policy Monthly Premiums immediately.\u00a0\nVarious Professional & Personal Development Training Opportunities immediately\nPaid time off after 90 day probationary period\nComplimentary Attendance in Financial Peace University after 180 days of employment\u00a0\nMonthly Profit Sharing Bonuses after 365 Days of Employment\u00a0\n401k with 4% match after 365 Days of Employment\u00a0\nOpportunities for advancement in leadership and management\nWork within a Christ-centered, mission-driven organization\nFlexible Hours: \nMonday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday 8 AM to 5 PM Eastern time or 9 AM to 6 PM Eastern time & Tuesdays\u00a0 11 AM to 8 PM Eastern time. 60 minute lunch each day.\nMeet the UCM Team https://uppercervicalmarketing.com/upper-cervical-marketing-team/ and Explore Our Core Values https://uppercervicalmarketing.com/about-us/ at this link.\nHow to Apply: \nAre you ready to step into a role where your work truly matters? If you share our dedication to bringing hope and healing to sick and suffering people for the glory of God, follow the link below:\nTo apply, c lick the \u2018Apply Now\u2019 button to submit your application. \nHours: Full-time remotely\nJob Type: Full-time\nExpected hours: 40 per week\nLanguage: English (Required)","locations":["Canada","United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-24T03:16:04.784Z","expires_at":"2026-07-24T03:16:04.784Z","external_id":"ucmpracticegrowthsystems","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/ignitvio/remote-job/sales-development-representative-cold-caller-appointment-setter-for-us-home-professional-services-remote","title":"Sales Development Representative (Cold Caller / Appointment Setter for US Home & Professional Services - Remote","company":"Ignitvio","location":"Remote","description":"About Ignitvio \nIgnitvio helps home and professional services businesses in the US stop losing money to missed calls and slow follow up. We build AI receptionists, lead response systems, and outbound engines for roofing, HVAC, dental, veterinary, insurance, and other home and professional services companies. We are a small, fast moving team and you will work directly with the founder.\nThe role \nThis is a phone first role. You will call home and professional services businesses in the US, get owners and decision makers on the phone, handle the \"I'm not interested,\" and book them into qualified meetings with our team. We hand you researched leads from our own systems, so you are not dialing random lists. You are calling businesses we already know are a good fit. We close the deals. You fill the calendar.\nYou will do well here if you have done real outbound before, you can take 30 nos and keep your energy on dial 31, and you can hold a conversation with a busy business owner without sounding like a script.\nWhat you will do \nCall US home and professional services businesses from our researched lead lists\nGet owners and decision makers on the phone\nHandle objections, hold the line, and book qualified meetings\nConfirm and remind so booked meetings actually happen\nLog all calls and outcomes in our CRM\nHit your daily dial and booking targets\nWhat we need from you \nReal cold calling or phone sales experience, US prospects preferred\nNear native spoken English that is clear and easy to understand on a phone\nA quiet place to make calls with reliable internet and backup power\nAbility to work US business hours\nWorld class objection handling skills (I will test this in your interview)\nMust know how to handle gate keepers\nSomeone who manages their own day and hits their numbers without anyone watching\nWhat you get \nA strong monthly base salary plus uncapped bonuses. I personally wrote the compensation plan so you can hit $10k plus in a month if you deliver enough qualified meetings\nPay for every qualified meeting you book, every meeting that shows, and every deal that closes from your meetings\nTop performers earn well above the local market for this kind of work, with no ceiling\nWorld class training on the offer and the script (I am former top 1% sales rep at 4 separate companies and a sales manager for Oracle - one the biggest software companies in the world). You bring the energy and the consistency\nHow to apply \nA short video is required\nFollow the application instructions carefully\nApplications without a video will not be reviewed","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-24T05:53:53.796Z","expires_at":"2026-07-24T05:53:53.796Z","external_id":"ignitvio","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/starlightmarketing/remote-job/remote-hybrid-brand-marketing-graphic-designer-agency","title":"Remote Hybrid Brand & Marketing Graphic Designer (Agency)","company":"Starlight Marketing","location":"Remote","description":"The Role \nWe don't need a narrow specialist; we need an agile, visually elite generalist who loves variety. One day you will be drafting a corporate logo, the next you will be layout out a multi-page restaurant menu, and the next you might be mapping out a vehicle wrap blueprint. You will report directly to the founder, taking client briefs and translating them into pixel-perfect, on-brand assets.\nCore Responsibilities \nBrand Systems: Design logos and comprehensive branding profiles from scratch, keeping typography, hierarchy, and color theory razor-sharp.\nDigital & Print Collateral: Edit, format, and prepare flawless print-ready files using Adobe InDesign, Illustrator, and Photoshop (e.g., flyers, multi-page layout documents, business cards, menus, digital banner ads).\nSocial Production: Design engaging daily social media graphics and templates directly in Canva, ensuring ease of delivery for our content scheduling assistant. Comfortable conceptualizing and editing short-form video content (Reels/TikToks/Shorts).\nThe Unconventional Challenge: Enthusiastically step up to non-standard design briefs when they come through the agency\u2014such as product packaging, vehicle wraps, and large-scale window/signage graphics. (No previous wrap experience required, but an enthusiastic, structural \"figure-it-out\" attitude is non-negotiable!).\nRequirements \n3\u20135+ years of design experience, ideally within a multi-client agency environment. An elite portfolio showing a balance of digital marketing assets and strong print typography/layout work.\nMastery of the Adobe Creative Suite (InDesign, Illustrator, Photoshop) AND advanced fluency in Canva. Strong organizational skills\u2014you must be comfortable working out of project management systems (like ClickUp) and meeting strict client deadlines.\nReliable high-speed internet and availability to overlap with US business hours for asset reviews.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-24T04:01:14.845Z","expires_at":"2026-07-24T04:01:14.845Z","external_id":"starlightmarketing","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/freightsimple/remote-job/motion-graphic-designer","title":"Motion/Graphic Designer","company":"FreightSimple","location":"Remote","description":"\ud83c\udfac The short version \nYou tell stories through motion and visuals, you sweat the timing and the typography, and you want your work seen by a fast-growing audience. You can take a concept and run with it.\nIf that\u2019s you, keep reading.\n\ud83d\ude80 Why this role is different \nYou\u2019ll create the video, animation, and graphic content that brings the FreightSimple brand to life, from product explainers and social clips to feature demos and campaigns. You\u2019ll turn complex logistics ideas into content that\u2019s clear, engaging, and on-brand.\nThis is a ground-floor role. You won\u2019t be following someone else\u2019s style guide. You\u2019ll be building it. \nAt our core we\u2019re a technology company, and we use data, automation, and AI tools to work smarter, including for generating and editing content.\n\ud83d\udca1 The honest pitch \nCreative ownership of how a fast-growing company shows up to the world, the best creative and AI tools available, and a team that actually ships your work instead of sitting on it.\n\u2728 What you\u2019ll actually do \n\ud83c\udf9e\ufe0f Motion design , animations, explainers, and product demos that make complex ideas simple\n\u2702\ufe0f Video production , editing and assembling content for marketing, social, and the website\n\ud83c\udfa8 Graphic design , for landing pages, social media, ads, and presentations\n\ud83e\udded Brand consistency , a cohesive visual style across everything\n\ud83e\udd1d Content collaboration , working with marketing and product to plan and produce content that drives results\n\ud83d\uddc2\ufe0f Asset library , building reusable templates, graphics, and motion assets\n\ud83c\udfaf What we\u2019re looking for \n\ud83c\udfa5 A strong portfolio or reel demonstrating motion and graphic design work\n\ud83c\udf9e\ufe0f Proficiency with motion/video tools such as After Effects and Premiere Pro\n\ud83c\udfa8 Proficiency with graphic tools such as Figma, Illustrator, or Photoshop\n\ud83d\udc41\ufe0f A strong sense of layout, typography, color, and timing \n\ud83e\udd16 Experience using AI tools to generate and edit video, image, and motion content\n\ud83e\udde9 The ability to take a concept and run with it independently\n\u270d\ufe0f Excellent written and verbal English \n\u2764\ufe0f Why you\u2019ll love working here \n\ud83c\udfe1 Fully remote , with a team that genuinely respects work-life balance\n\ud83c\udfa8 Creative ownership of how a fast-growing company shows up to the world\n\ud83e\uddf0 The best tools available , modern creative and AI tools\n\ud83d\udde3\ufe0f A real voice in strategy , we listen to our team and value your ideas\n\ud83e\udd1d A calm, supportive culture with friendly people who have your back\n\ud83d\ude80 Thorough onboarding and ongoing support\n\ud83d\udcb0 Competitive compensation \nIf you want to build a brand\u2019s visual voice from the ground up, let\u2019s talk.","locations":["Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-23T07:24:15.368Z","expires_at":"2026-07-23T07:24:15.368Z","external_id":"freightsimple","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/freightsimple/remote-job/finance-manager","title":"Finance Manager","company":"FreightSimple","location":"Remote","description":"\ud83e\uddee The short version \nYou\u2019re a finance leader who loves getting the details right and the systems even better. You want to own the whole finance function, not just a slice of it, and you\u2019d rather design a better process than grind through a broken one.\nIf that\u2019s you, keep reading.\n\ud83d\ude80 Why this role is different \nAt our core we\u2019re a technology company, and our first instinct is to automate. Our accounts receivable and accounts payable are largely automated already, so this isn\u2019t a data-entry job.\nYou\u2019ll own the finance function end to end, the day-to-day and the strategy, and you\u2019ll have real influence over how the business runs. \nYou\u2019ll lead accounts receivable, accounts payable, bookkeeping, cargo and insurance claims, and management reporting. Just as importantly, you\u2019ll improve the systems and processes behind them and give leadership the numbers they need to make decisions.\n\ud83d\udca1 The honest pitch \nModern, automated systems plus AI tools mean you spend your time on judgement and improvement, not reconciliations. You'll have the autonomy to shape how finance works here.\n\u2728 What you\u2019ll actually do \n\ud83d\udcca Own financial reporting , management reports and the numbers leadership relies on\n\ud83d\udce5 Lead accounts receivable , customer setup and invoice changes\n\ud83d\udce4 Lead accounts payable , carrier accounts, freight bill auditing and corrections\n\ud83d\udcda Own the books , bookkeeping and month-end\n\ud83d\udce6 Oversee cargo claims and insurance , on behalf of customers\n\u2699\ufe0f Improve the systems and processes behind all of it, with engineering when needed\nWe don\u2019t expect experience in everything. We just ask that you\u2019re eager to learn, and we\u2019ll get you up to speed fast.\n\ud83c\udfaf What we\u2019re looking for \n\ud83c\udf93 An accounting qualification (CPA or equivalent) or strong equivalent experience\n\ud83e\udded Experience owning or managing a finance/accounting function \n\ud83d\udcbc Experience with Xero and financial reporting\n\ud83d\ude9b Ideally knowledge of the freight or logistics industry \n\u270d\ufe0f Excellent written and verbal English \n\ud83e\udde9 Strong problem-solving and confidence in challenging situations\n\u2764\ufe0f High emotional intelligence , genuine curiosity about people, and a desire to help\n\u23f1\ufe0f Sharp time management and comfort with modern software\n\ud83d\udc9b Why you\u2019ll love working here \n\ud83c\udfe1 Fully remote , with a team that genuinely respects work-life balance\n\u2699\ufe0f Modern, automated systems that eliminate busywork so you can focus on judgement and strategy\n\ud83d\udde3\ufe0f Real ownership of the finance function and a voice in how the business runs\n\ud83e\udd1d A calm, supportive culture with friendly people who have your back\n\ud83e\udd16 AI tools to help you work smarter and more efficiently\n\ud83d\ude80 Thorough onboarding and ongoing support\n\ud83d\udcb0 Competitive compensation \nIf you want to own finance, not just do finance, let\u2019s talk.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-23T07:31:57.616Z","expires_at":"2026-07-23T07:31:57.616Z","external_id":"freightsimple","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/mcdnllc/remote-job/short-form-video-editor-for-dtc-beauty-ads","title":"Short-Form Video Editor for DTC Beauty Ads","company":"MCDN LLC","location":"Remote","description":"Join Our Team as a Short-Form Video Editor (Full-Time, Remote)\nWant to be the creative engine behind a fast-scaling beauty brand?\nWe've already launched a profitable DTC beauty brand in the US, and we're scaling hard on paid social. Your job: take a written script and turn it into a finished video ad that sells. You build the whole thing, working side by side with the founder and media buyer. Not a corporate content team. A lean, fast creative crew.\nOur 100% learning guarantee: \nThe pace is fast and the bar is high. We ship volume, test constantly, and put real money behind what works.\nIf you live and breathe video, obsess over the first 3 seconds, and love turning a script into something people can't scroll past, you'll feel at home here.\nYour Mission \nTurn written scripts into finished video ads. You take a text script and build the whole thing: source and dress the b-roll, set the rhythm, add the voiceover, and use your cuts and pacing to carry the emotion each line needs to land. This is the heart of the role.\nDay to day:\nTurn a script into a complete video: b-roll, voiceover, pacing, and emotion through the edit\nGenerate and dress b-roll, images, and voiceovers, and keep them consistent with our products and characters across every shot\nEngineer strong hooks and pattern interrupts in the first 3 seconds\nAdd captions, subtitles, sound design, music, and on-screen text\nControl pacing and retention so viewers watch to the CTA\nProduce variations and angles from the same script, and re-cut winners into fresh hooks\nBuild the workflows that let you produce fast without losing quality\nSecondary:\nSome static ad creation\nPulling b-roll from our UGC creator footage as raw material (you won't be editing the UGC creator ads themselves)\nWho You Are \nExpert in at least one editing suite: Premiere, After Effects, CapCut, or DaVinci Resolve\nA portfolio of video ads you've built (VSL or short-form), required\nFast and high-volume: you ship a lot without dropping quality\nRetention-obsessed: you think in hooks, pacing, and watch-time\nFluent with AI tools for b-roll, images, and voiceovers, and you understand the workflows behind them\nDetail-focused: clean cuts, synced captions, consistent products and characters\nResponsive on our Asia hours (Bangkok / ICT). We want someone we can reach and move fast with during our day, not just a couple hours of overlap\nFluent in English (written and spoken)\nWhy Join Our Team \nWork directly with the founder, with the option to be based in Thailand and build alongside us in person\nHigh autonomy and full ownership of the creative\nA profitable brand scaling fast, with lots of upside\nClear path to more pay and a bigger creative role\nPerformance bonus: when your ads win and scale, you earn on top of base pay","locations":["Afghanistan","Armenia","Azerbaijan","Bahrain","Bangladesh","Bhutan","Brunei Darussalam","Cambodia","China","Democratic People's Republic of Korea","Georgia","Hong Kong (China)","India","Indonesia","Iran","Iraq","Israel","Japan","Jordan","Kazakhstan","Kuwait","Kyrgyzstan","Lao People's Democratic Republic","Lebanon","Macao (China)","Malaysia","Maldives","Mongolia","Myanmar","Nepal","Oman","Pakistan","Philippines","Qatar","Russian Federation","Saudi Arabia","Singapore","South Korea","Sri Lanka","State of Palestine","Syrian Arab Republic","Taiwan","Tajikistan","Thailand","Timor-Leste","Turkmenistan","United Arab Emirates","Uzbekistan","Viet Nam","Yemen","Albania","Belarus","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Czechia","Estonia","Greece","Hungary","Kosovo","Latvia","Lithuania","Moldova","Montenegro","North Macedonia","Poland","Romania","Serbia","Slovakia","Ukraine","Algeria","Angola","Benin","Botswana","British Indian Ocean Territory","Burkina Faso","Burundi","Cabo Verde","Cameroon","Central African Republic","Chad","Comoros","Congo","C\u00f4te d\u2019Ivoire","Djibouti","Egypt","Equatorial Guinea","Eritrea","Eswatini","Ethiopia","French Southern Territories","Gabon","Gambia","Ghana","Guinea","Guinea-Bissau","Kenya","Lesotho","Liberia","Libya","Madagascar","Malawi","Mali","Mauritania","Mauritius","Mayotte","Morocco","Mozambique","Namibia","Niger","Nigeria","Rwanda","R\u00e9union","Saint Helena","Sao Tome and Principe","Senegal","Seychelles","Sierra Leone","Somalia","South Africa","South Sudan","Sudan","Tanzania","Togo","Tunisia","Uganda","Western Sahara","Zambia","Zimbabwe"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-19T17:08:41.263Z","expires_at":"2026-07-19T17:08:41.263Z","external_id":"mcdnllc","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/billionbody/remote-job/financial-manager","title":"Financial Manager","company":"Billion Body","location":"Remote","description":"Financial Manager\n\ud83d\udccd Remote | \ud83d\udcbc Full-Time | \ud83d\udcb0 Competitive \u2014 Based on Experience | \ud83d\udcc8 Path to CFO\nAbout Us\nWe're an ultra-premium health performance company serving elite founders and UHNW individuals globally. We install biological operating systems - combining world-class physicians, functional medicine, biohacking, and direct access to our founder's network.\nWe are scaling rapidly and we need someone who can build and own the financial infrastructure of a high-growth company operating out of a UAE Free Zone. This is not a junior role. We need a finance professional who has done this before \u2014 end-to-end, in the UAE, with the compliance and complexity that comes with it.\nThe Role\nYou will own the entire finance function and build it out from the ground up. That means hiring, structuring the accounting team, implementing the right systems, establishing financial controls, and ensuring every department is operating within clear financial guidelines.\nYou report directly to the founder. Your work influences every major business decision. If you want a role where finance sits at the center of strategy - not in the back office - this is it.\nWhat You'll Own\nUAE Compliance & Tax \nFull ownership of UAE VAT compliance - filing, reporting, and ensuring company-wide adherence\nMaintain compliance with Meydan Free Zone financial regulations and all applicable UAE financial law\nLiaise with external auditors, consultants, and regulatory bodies as needed\nEnsure audit-ready financial documentation at all times\nAccounting & Financial Controls \nOversee and manage the full accounting function - AP, AR, reconciliation, payroll, and reporting\nBuild and enforce accounting policies and financial controls across the company\nEnsure every team member and department is adhering to established financial procedures\nManage multi-currency transactions across Wio Bank, Mercury, and Wise\nReview and approve invoices, contractor payments, and client billing\nTeam Building \nIdentify gaps in the finance function and hire accordingly - accountants, bookkeepers, or financial analysts as the company scales\nTrain and manage the finance team, setting clear KPIs and standards\nBuild a finance department that operates independently and to a world-class standard\nFinancial Planning & Reporting \nProduce monthly P&L statements, cash flow reports, and financial summaries for the founder\nBuild and maintain a rolling 3\u201312 month financial forecast\nDevelop financial models for new service lines, pricing strategies, and growth scenarios\nIdentify cost inefficiencies proactively and surface savings opportunities\nSystems & Infrastructure \nSelect, implement, and manage the right accounting software for the business (QuickBooks, Xero, Zoho Books, or equivalent)\nBuild scalable financial infrastructure that can support 10x growth\nEnsure clean, structured data that enables fast, accurate reporting at any time\nWhat We're Looking For\nNon-Negotiables \n3\u20135 years of experience in financial management, senior accounting, or as a financial specialist\nMandatory: proven, hands-on experience with UAE VAT compliance and filing \nKnowledge of UAE Free Zone financial regulations\nExperience owning or significantly contributing to a full finance function\nTrack record of building or managing a finance/accounting team\nProficiency in accounting software (QuickBooks, Xero, Zoho Books, or equivalent ERP)\nMulti-currency account management experience\nZero-error standard - numbers are either right or wrong\nExcellent written English - all reports must be founder-ready\nStrong Preference For \nCPA, ACCA, CMA, CA, or equivalent professional qualification\nExperience working in a UAE Free Zone company (Meydan, DIFC, DMCC, or similar)\nDirect reporting to a founder or C-suite\nExperience in a fast-scaling startup or premium services company\nFamiliarity with Wio Bank, Mercury, or Wise for business payments\nWhat Success Looks Like\nMonth 1\u20132: Audit & Foundation \nFull audit of existing financial records completed\nUAE VAT position assessed and any outstanding filings resolved\nAccounting software selected and implemented\nFinancial controls documented and communicated to all departments\nMonth 3\u20136: Ownership \nFull AP/AR cycle running independently\nMonthly P&L and cash flow reports delivered consistently\nRolling 3-month cash flow forecast live\nFinance team hiring plan proposed and initiated\nMonth 7\u201312: Scale \nFinance team hired and operational\n12-month financial model built and maintained\nAll departments operating within financial guidelines\nScalable financial infrastructure in place for growth\nClear CFO candidate as company enters next phase\nThis Role Is Not For You If\nYou have never dealt with UAE VAT compliance first-hand\nYou've only worked in one part of the finance function, not owned it end-to-end\nYou're not comfortable building systems and teams from scratch\nYou need detailed instructions to do your job\nYou treat finance as a back-office function rather than a strategic one\nWhy Join Us\nOwn the entire finance function with a direct line to the founder\nBuild a finance team from the ground up \u2014 real ownership, real impact\nClear and fast path to CFO as the company scales\nRemote with full flexibility\nCompetitive compensation based on experience\nWork at the intersection of elite health, premium service, and high-growth business\nHow to Apply\n\u2192 Apply Now\nEvery application is reviewed personally. You will hear from us within 5\u20137 business days if your profile is a match.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","United States","Canada","Armenia","Azerbaijan","Bahrain","Iraq","Israel","Jordan","Kuwait","Lebanon","Oman","Qatar","Saudi Arabia","State of Palestine","Syrian Arab Republic","United Arab Emirates","Yemen","Afghanistan","Bangladesh","Bhutan","Brunei Darussalam","Cambodia","China","Democratic People's Republic of Korea","Georgia","Hong Kong (China)","India","Indonesia","Iran","Japan","Kazakhstan","Kyrgyzstan","Lao People's Democratic Republic","Macao (China)","Malaysia","Maldives","Mongolia","Myanmar","Nepal","Pakistan","Philippines","Russian Federation","Singapore","South Korea","Sri Lanka","Taiwan","Tajikistan","Thailand","Timor-Leste","Turkmenistan","Uzbekistan","Viet Nam"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-19T16:55:43.568Z","expires_at":"2026-07-19T16:55:43.568Z","external_id":"billionbody","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/stubgroup/remote-job/senior-google-ads-account-manager-remote-work-from-home","title":"Senior Google Ads Account Manager - Remote (Work From Home)","company":"StubGroup","location":"Remote","description":"Who we are \nWe are a team of hard-working marketers running a Premier Google Partner ad agency.\nWe help businesses large and small. Most of our clients are located in the United States, and our team members are located throughout the United States and around the world.\nCheck out our website: stubgroup.com \nWhat we're looking for \nWe need a Senior Google Ads Account Manager! This is a remote (work-from-home) position.\nSenior Google Ads Account Managers should possess:\nAdvanced knowledge of Google Ads and how to create and manage profitable campaigns for ecommerce and lead-generation businesses.\nStrong client communication skills.\nYou will work directly with high-value clients as their primary point of contact and will be responsible for managing client relationships and creating and managing Google Ads campaigns for them.\nCompensation & growth opportunities \nAt StubGroup, we have a milestone-based compensation structure that rewards our team members with increasing compensation as they generate more value for the company.\nStarting Compensation: New Senior Google Ads Account Managers begin with a competitive monthly salary range of $4,000 - $5,000 .\nBonuses and Incentives: Senior Google Ads Account Managers who go above and beyond may also earn additional bonuses and incentives aligned with the exceptional value they create for StubGroup.\nWe believe teamwork is the foundation of success, and we\u2019re committed to recognizing and rewarding the outstanding contributions of our team members. Together, we grow and thrive!\nThe ideal candidate \nGoogle Ads Knowledge: Proficiency in Google Ads is essential. You will be directly managing and overseeing high-value Google Ads campaigns for lead generation and ecommerce websites. You must be expert at using the Google Ads interface and Google Ads Editor, and have an advanced understanding of campaign structures, bidding strategies, conversion tracking, etc.\nMarketing Strategy: Your responsibility is to learn about each client's business, including their products, target audience, and more. Your goal is to guide clients toward strategies that maximize the profitability of their ad campaigns. Whether it's recommending website changes or addressing a client's fixation on low click-through rates at the expense of website traffic quality and conversion rates, it's your job to educate them on more effective metrics for evaluating campaign success.\nProblem-Solving: Our company values self-sufficiency and resourcefulness. We expect team members to \"figure it out\" and take initiative, rather than asking questions that could have been answered independently. Of course, we're here to provide support when you genuinely cannot solve a problem on your own. The expectation is that you will consistently go above and beyond, overcoming obstacles instead of letting them hinder your progress.\nMake sure you\u2019re comfortable with: \nRemote working. This is a remote (work-from-home) position.\nAll job offers start with a 60-day trial to make sure that we\u2019re the right fit for each other.\nCommunicating with business owners who don't understand how Google Ads works\nJuggling a large number of tasks at a time and properly prioritizing how to handle them.\nWorking from 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Central Time (United States business hours)\nOur values \nIntegrity : Honesty is vital. We must be honest with ourselves, with our colleagues, and with our clients. We tell clients exactly what we are doing for them, and what we can or can't do to help them. If we make a mistake, we own it.\nResponsibility : We are here to solve problems for clients. We are constantly looking for ways to provide more value to our clients. How do we help them succeed? How do we help our colleagues succeed? We don't shirk work. We look for more of it. By being proactive, we stand out from the crowd and win our clients' trust.\nCare : We're not just in this for the money. We genuinely want our clients to be successful. We understand that we're making an impact, that we are helping businesses create jobs and put food on the table for their families. We value that trust and do not abuse it.\nTo apply \nIf you're interested, please submit the following:\nA link to your resume in PDF format with the following naming convention: [Lastname.Firstname.Senior-Manager.pdf]\nDetails of your experience\nYour answer to this question: If you were an animal, what animal would you be and why?\nYour answer to this question: I get up in the morning because . . .\nSubmissions should go to: john+senior+manager+dynamite@stubgroup.com \nI am looking for people who can format their submissions in a way that makes it easy for us to review. Remember, in client management, you want to help make it as easy on the client as possible! I\u2019m happy to answer any questions you may include in your application.\nThank you for your consideration and best of luck with your job search!","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Canada","South Africa"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-19T14:48:10.222Z","expires_at":"2026-07-19T14:48:10.222Z","external_id":"stubgroup","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/intentsignal/remote-job/account-manager","title":"Account Manager","company":"IntentSignal","location":"Remote","description":"About the role \nWe\u2019re a fast-moving lead generation agency, and we\u2019re looking for an Account Manager to own client relationships. You\u2019ll be the face our clients see most, guiding them through onboarding, running their recurring check-ins, and making sure everything they\u2019re owed actually gets done by the rest of our team.\nThis is a high-trust, high-freedom role. We don\u2019t micromanage. You\u2019ll have a lot of flexibility in how you run your day and your accounts. We need someone who is responsive, organized, and takes ownership.\nWhat you\u2019ll do \nOnboard new clients: run kickoff calls, gather everything we need to launch, set clear expectations, and get them off to a smooth start. (This is the most important part of the job and where we need the most help)\nRun client syncs: weekly or biweekly calls to review performance, talk through ideas, and keep the relationship strong.\nTurn ideas into todos: capture client ideas and requests, translate them into clear tasks, and hand them off to our campaign managers so the work gets done.\nStay on top of delivery: track what\u2019s owed to each client and make sure nothing slips through the cracks.\nWhat we\u2019re looking for \nStrong, clear communicator: comfortable and confident on live client calls\nHighly organized and detail-oriented; you keep your own systems tidy (for most systems we use Google Sheets and Clickup)\nResponsive and reliable: clients and teammates can count on you\nBonus: experience in agencies, marketing, or client-facing account management\nWhat you\u2019ll get \nA lot of flexibility and freedom in how you work\nA role you can fully own and shape\nA collaborative team that trusts you to do great work","locations":["Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Canada","United States","South Africa","Australia"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-18T04:57:39.826Z","expires_at":"2026-07-18T04:57:39.826Z","external_id":"intentsignal","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/scalers/remote-job/head-of-finance","title":"Head of Finance","company":"Scalers","location":"Remote","description":"Location: Remote\nType: Part-Time / Fractional\nCompensation: $3,500\u2013$5,000 USD per month.\nAbout the Role\nWe're looking for a commercially minded Head of Finance to build and own the financial operating system across three fast-growing businesses:\nScalers \u2013 Marketing and growth company\nAffiliate Takeover (ATO) \u2013 Global events and media brand\nCircle \u2013 New membership and mastermind business\nThis is not a traditional bookkeeping role.\nWe're looking for someone who can create clarity from complexity, build systems that scale, and give leadership instant visibility into the financial health of the business.\nInitially, you'll spend time building processes and infrastructure. Over time, the goal is to leverage automation, AI, and efficient systems so the finance function becomes increasingly streamlined and proactive.\nExpected workload:\nInitial: 20\u201330 hours per week\nLong-term target: 10\u201320 hours per week through automation and process optimisation\nYour Mission\nWithin your first 60 days, build a finance function that gives leadership reliable, real-time visibility across all entities.\nLeadership should be able to instantly access:\nCash position by entity\nTotal consolidated cash\nReceivables\nPayables\nProject profitability\n13-week cash forecast\nRunway\nKey financial risks\nRequired financial decisions\nWhat You'll Own\nWeekly Reporting \nCash position by entity\nConsolidated cash position\nAccounts receivable report\nAccounts payable report\n13-week rolling cash forecast\nRunway analysis\nFinancial risk report\nWeekly finance summary for leadership\nMonthly Reporting \nProject-level P&L reporting\nConsolidated P&L reporting\nCash flow reporting\nExpense reconciliation\nCost allocation across entities\nManagement reporting package\nForecasting & Strategic Finance \nYou'll own:\nBest-case, base-case and worst-case forecasts\nCash planning and liquidity management\nCapital allocation recommendations\nFinancial modelling for growth initiatives\nScenario planning and risk analysis\nFinancial Controls \nYou'll ensure:\nAll expenses are accurately categorised\nAll transactions are reconciled\nFinancial records remain clean and audit-ready\nReporting is reliable and accurate\nFinancial processes improve continuously as the business grows\nInternational Finance & Tax \nOur businesses operate across multiple countries, currencies and legal entities. We're looking for someone who understands the complexities that come with international operations and can help leadership make informed decisions.\nYou should have experience with:\nManaging finances across multiple countries and entities\nUnderstanding the tax implications of cross-border transactions\nWorking with international contractors, suppliers and customers\nMulti-currency cash management and forecasting\nVAT, sales tax and indirect tax considerations across different jurisdictions\nCollaborating with local accountants and tax advisors where required\nIdentifying tax risks and opportunities as the businesses scale\nYou don't need to be a tax specialist in every jurisdiction, but you should know the right questions to ask, recognise potential risks early, and ensure the businesses remain financially and operationally efficient internationally.\nAI & Automation \nWe're building a modern finance function.\nYou must actively use AI and automation tools to:\nReduce manual work\nImprove reporting speed\nIncrease forecasting accuracy\nBuild efficient workflows\nMinimise hours required while maximising output\nWe're looking for someone excited by technology and eager to rethink how finance is run.\nWhat We're Looking For\nEssential Experience \nYou have experience owning finance for one or more of the following:\nMarketing agencies\nMedia businesses\nInformation businesses\nEvents companies\nSaaS businesses\nE-commerce companies\nYou also have:\nExperience managing finances across multiple entities, countries and currencies\nStrong understanding of international tax considerations and cross-border transactions\nStrong cash flow management skills\nStrong reporting and forecasting capabilities\nExperience with multi-currency reporting and cash management\nExcellent English communication skills\nExperience working directly with founders and operators\nA systems and process mindset\nComfort using AI and automation tools\nPreferred Locations\nWe are particularly interested in candidates based in:\nSouth Africa\nSerbia\nRomania\nPoland\nCroatia\nBulgaria\nHungary\nArgentina\nColombia\nMexico\nExceptional candidates from other locations are also encouraged to apply.\nWhat Success Looks Like\nAfter 60 days:\n\u2705 Leadership trusts the numbers\n\u2705 Cash flow is visible and predictable\n\u2705 Reporting is accurate and delivered on time\n\u2705 Financial risks are identified early\n\u2705 Key decisions are supported by real data\n\u2705 Finance operates efficiently through systems, AI and automation\nIf you enjoy bringing order to complexity, building systems that last, and using technology to create leverage, we'd love to hear from you.\nClick the \"Apply Now\" button to submit your application.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Canada","United States"],"employment_type":"PART_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-16T14:26:34.371Z","expires_at":"2026-07-16T14:26:34.371Z","external_id":"scalers","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/mailerlite/remote-job/performance-copywriter","title":"Performance Copywriter","company":"MailerLite","location":"Remote","description":"MailerLite is one of the fastest-growing email marketing services. We help more than 1 million businesses around the world stay in touch with their customers. Today, we are a team of more than 170 dreamers, adventurers, and world travelers passionate about what we do and what we believe in. And we are ready for another talented person to join the party.\nWe\u2019re looking for a Performance Copywriter who thinks in terms of ROI and conversion rates, but can still communicate a strong brand personality. Your primary goal is to drive new sign-ups by crafting high-converting digital ads and landing pages, while maintaining our brand voice across all conversion channels including video, email, and website.\nWhy MailerLite? \nWondering why we think you\u2019ll love working for MailerLite? Here are our favorite 6 reasons!\nYou'll see your words drive real results \nYour copy won't sit in a backlog \u2013 it'll run against real audiences, generate real data, and directly move conversion metrics.\nYou'll grow, develop and evolve \nAs part of a team that's always looking for new, innovative ways to offer value for our customers, you'll constantly be experimenting, learning, and trying out new things.\nYou'll take ownership \nWe expect you to take full responsibility and ownership of your tasks. Team leads avoid micromanaging and minimize interruptions so you can stay focused on your assignments.\nYou'll have experts at hand \nWhenever you\u2019re stuck, your teammates with a wide range of different expertise are ready to help you grow. And they\u2019d love for you to share your knowledge too!\nYou'll pick where you work, every day \nWe embrace the remote culture. Every day you get to choose what environment makes you most productive.\nYou'll have stability \nWe value a stable workplace! MailerLite has been thriving for over 10 years and our year-over-year growth continues to increase.\nWhat you will work on \nConversion-driven Search & Social Ad Copywriting: Write high-intent headlines and descriptions for Google Ads (RSA) that improve Quality Score and lower CPA. Craft compelling ad copy for Meta, LinkedIn, and other social platforms\nHigh-Conversion Landing Pages: Design the narrative flow and write the copy for landing pages that maintain \u201cmessage match\u201d from the ad and convert traffic at each stage of the funnel\nConversion Rate Optimization (CRO): Constantly A/B test headlines, CTAs, and hooks. You\u2019ll analyze performance data to iterate on winning copy and phase out underperforming assets\nMulti-Channel Scripting: Write high-impact scripts for both short-form and longer-form video ads\nCollaborative Strategy: Work closely with Ads managers and designers to ensure the creative vision aligns with the technical targeting and visual elements\nWhat we expect from you \n3\u20135 Years of Experience: Proven track record in a performance marketing agency or a fast-growing B2B brand\nNative English Proficiency: Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English\nUS Market Competency: Proven experience and deep understanding of the US market\nA \"Conversion-First\" Mindset: You know the difference between \"clever\" copy and \"converting\" copy and understand consumer psychology and triggers\nTechnical Literacy: Familiarity with Google Ads interfaces, landing page builders, and basic SEO principles\nData Fluency: You aren't afraid of the numbers. You can look at a dashboard, see a high bounce rate, and know exactly how to rewrite the hero section to fix it\nPortfolio of Wins: A proven track record of success, demonstrated through campaign metrics, before-and-after copy examples, or case studies showing a direct lift in conversions\nWorking hours overlap: At least 4 hours of daily overlap with the CET timezone\nWhat we offer \nYearly gross salary: From $50,000 per year, with final compensation based on experience and qualifications\nRemote-first culture: Our team works remotely from around the world\nInternational health insurance: Provided with coverage in most countries, with a monthly payout available in select countries where coverage is limited\nCompany-paid retreats: Once a year, we gather for a week in a beautiful location to work, learn, and have fun together\n31 days of vacation (including public holidays): We encourage you to unplug and recharge!\n12 paid sick days: For your physical and mental well-being, no doctor's note required. Parents can use them to care for their sick children\n4 creative days: One paid day off per quarter to do something creative and fun\n12 parental days: Enjoy one paid day off each month to treasure time with your children\nParental leave: 100% paid leave when welcoming a new child through birth (3 months maternity, 1 month paternity) or adoption\nParenting budget of $1000: A $1000 special gift to celebrate the arrival of your little one, whether through childbirth or adoption\nJoy Budget: Annual allowance to spend on what brings you joy, starting at $1,000 per year and increasing over time\nMacBook and other tools: That\u00a0help you to do your job efficiently","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Afghanistan","Armenia","Azerbaijan","Bahrain","Bangladesh","Bhutan","Brunei Darussalam","Cambodia","China","Democratic People's Republic of Korea","Georgia","Hong Kong (China)","India","Indonesia","Iran","Iraq","Israel","Japan","Jordan","Kazakhstan","Kuwait","Kyrgyzstan","Lao People's Democratic Republic","Lebanon","Macao (China)","Malaysia","Maldives","Mongolia","Myanmar","Nepal","Oman","Pakistan","Philippines","Qatar","Russian Federation","Saudi Arabia","Singapore","South Korea","Sri Lanka","State of Palestine","Syrian Arab Republic","Taiwan","Tajikistan","Thailand","Timor-Leste","Turkmenistan","United Arab Emirates","Uzbekistan","Viet Nam","Yemen","Algeria","Angola","Benin","Botswana","British Indian Ocean Territory","Burkina Faso","Burundi","Cabo Verde","Cameroon","Central African Republic","Chad","Comoros","Congo","C\u00f4te d\u2019Ivoire","Djibouti","Egypt","Equatorial Guinea","Eritrea","Eswatini","Ethiopia","French Southern Territories","Gabon","Gambia","Ghana","Guinea","Guinea-Bissau","Kenya","Lesotho","Liberia","Libya","Madagascar","Malawi","Mali","Mauritania","Mauritius","Mayotte","Morocco","Mozambique","Namibia","Niger","Nigeria","Rwanda","R\u00e9union","Saint Helena","Sao Tome and Principe","Senegal","Seychelles","Sierra Leone","Somalia","South Africa","South Sudan","Sudan","Tanzania","Togo","Tunisia","Uganda","Western Sahara","Zambia","Zimbabwe"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-15T15:56:31.014Z","expires_at":"2026-07-15T15:56:31.014Z","external_id":"mailerlite","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/accommercelp/remote-job/senior-creative-strategist-8-figure-dtc-brand","title":"Senior Creative Strategist - 8 Figure DTC Brand","company":"Ac Commerce L.P.","location":"Remote","description":"Who we are \nWe're an 8-figure DTC pet brand on a mission to become the number one player in our space. We help dog owners take care of their dog's teeth. Fresher breath, cleaner teeth, and fewer expensive vet bills down the line. We went from zero to eight figures in two years. We are nowhere near done.\nWhat's in it for you \nManage and lead our creative department, with the freedom to bring your own ideas and leadership to life.\nWork closely with the founder.\nAccess to our library of top copywriting and DTC marketing courses.\nA clear path to grow with us, all the way up to CMO.\nA bonus system for every ad that scales.\nWhat you'll do \nYou will own the creative department. You will lead a team of video editors and media buyers, and you will write the scripts for our VSLs, advertorials, and native ads.\nYou will also work closely with the founder. Together you will strategize, analyze market trends, and dig deep into our core avatar and sub avatars.\nRequirements \nAt least 2 years of experience in direct response marketing for 7+ figure DTC ecommerce brands.\nAI native. You are a systems builder. You don't rely on AI, you use it to amplify your knowledge.\nOur 4 core values \nObsession.\nTake accountability and ownership. Own what you build, and own it when it fails.\nCommunicate, communicate, communicate.\nSelf starter mentality. You don't wait on anyone to give you instructions. You act.\nHow to apply \nSend us 2 things:\nA one minute Loom. You, your experience, the brands you've worked with, and what exactly you did.\n3 to 5 of your best ads with the numbers (spend, ROAS or CPA, how long they ran) and your hypothesis behind it.\nCompensation \n$4,000 to $6,000 per month base, plus performance bonuses (can easily reach $10,000 per month). Full-time remote.","locations":["Canada","Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","United States","Afghanistan","Armenia","Azerbaijan","Bahrain","Bangladesh","Bhutan","Brunei Darussalam","Cambodia","China","Democratic People's Republic of Korea","Georgia","Hong Kong (China)","India","Indonesia","Iran","Iraq","Israel","Japan","Jordan","Kazakhstan","Kuwait","Kyrgyzstan","Lao People's Democratic Republic","Lebanon","Macao (China)","Malaysia","Maldives","Mongolia","Myanmar","Nepal","Oman","Pakistan","Philippines","Qatar","Russian Federation","Saudi Arabia","Singapore","South Korea","Sri Lanka","State of Palestine","Syrian Arab Republic","Taiwan","Tajikistan","Thailand","Timor-Leste","Turkmenistan","United Arab Emirates","Uzbekistan","Viet Nam","Yemen"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-14T23:22:08.849Z","expires_at":"2026-07-14T23:22:08.849Z","external_id":"accommercelp","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/destinationasset/remote-job/executive-assistant-personal-assistant","title":"Executive Assistant / Personal Assistant","company":"Destination Asset","location":"Remote","description":"Summary \nAre you looking to work in the vacation rental (Airbnb, etc) space and to join a fast-growing, agile company? The founder of Destination Asset is seeking an Executive Assistant (min 1-year experience) to make their lives easier and help the company grow. If you\u2019re passionate, take pride in your work, and have some related experience, we want to hear from you!\nAbout Destination Asset \nDestination Asset serves vacation rental management companies and owners with portfolios ranging from 1 to 100+ units with proven revenue management and optimization processes.\u00a0\nDestination Asset has grown to be the top reviewed and top rated company in the PriceLabs Expert Directory by fulfilling our mission: for every host to be optimistic about every STR season and property launch.\nThe company is run by the founder, Jacob Murphy, who is based in the United States. The company has 4 team members who are based around the world who assist to maintain reporting systems, optimize calendars, and monitor the pricing algorithms. Everyone on the team is very authentic with their interactions and enjoys a light level of humor. Everyone shows up to their work excited about the industry, and they work efficiently to get things done and provide an exceptional experience to all of our partners. At the end of the day, owners trust us to manage millions in bookings every month, which we take very seriously.\nAbout the Portfolio Management & Executive Assistant Role \nDestination Asset is hiring an Executive Assistant to work directly with the founder. This is a role that was created to support the founder with business and personal tasks. Overall, the EA will be helping the founder save time and streamline specific tasks as well as handle client support questions by answering or delegating as needed.\nJacob has prepared some training materials to make the transition into the role as smooth as possible, but this role will throw you into some tasks that will need you to create systems, take notes, and keep track of how things are done yourself. This role will be flexible at the beginning while you learn the systems, and be flexible with how you keep things organized. You can pitch in ideas to improve things. The new EA will have the support they need to learn the company, the role, and be positioned for success. The first week or two on the job will be training with the founder. The first two months in general will be training-focused, and spent getting you up to speed answering emails. You\u2019ll be at the front edge of the Airbnb industry and what it takes to be successful in it.\u00a0\nAfter training, the new hire will be communicating with the founder regularly and will be more autonomous with the responsibilities.\u00a0\nResponsibilities of the Job: \nAnswering or directing client/partner email, slack, whatsapp, etc support requests\nResponding to each client while knowing (or knowing how to reference) their preferred tone, strategy, philosophy, knowing promises made, what not to say, sensitivity level, risk tolerance, their main concern, etc\nOversee and communicate with the team leader to ensure certain task completion\nSetting deadlines and timelines for tasks and managing their completion\nHandle the administrative tasks currently on the desk of the founder\nHelping out with operational tasks related to the business\nTake ownership of keeping the founder organized in business and life\nKeep track of the simple sales cycle to ensure follow up with prime prospects\nFollowing SOP steps to create needed reports, use Claude projects, etc\nProactively identifying areas of disorganization and building systems from the ground up to solve them.\nCreating, documenting, and implementing Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) where none currently exist.\nActing as a proactive problem-solver who anticipates the founder's needs rather than waiting for direction.\nPotentially lead future OTA listing optimization processes\nAs the EA becomes more comfortable in the role, there\u2019ll be opportunities for more responsibilities and projects. In addition to helping the founder manage their work, they\u2019ll also be helping the rest of the team in specific capacities, acting as the glue of the team.\nDetails \nThis is a remote role. The hours are flexible, but the new hire needs to only have their workday overlap somewhere with Jacob\u2019s. The team currently operates mostly within a 7a-3p Eastern US time.\nThis is a part-time, long-term, contractor role, salaried through Wise, paid weekly. As the business grows, or as skills are developed, it could easily become full time.\nWho We\u2019re Looking For \nWe\u2019re looking for someone with at least 1 year of experience as an EA, VA, or in a related field. What\u2019s most important for our new hire is to be driven, have passion for the industry, and have a can-do attitude.\u00a0\nOur ideal candidate sees the opportunity with this job and company, is excited about the industry, and is willing to give it their all to excel.\u00a0\nRequirements \nMinimum 1 year of experience\nLocated anywhere in North or South America (or can operate in those hours)\nTop level, strong written and spoken communication\nStrong understanding of data, spreadsheets, and numbers\nExperience working remotely during set hours\nNative English level\nUse the word racecar in your app\nPassion or interest in the real estate industry\u00a0\nStrong EQ / emotional intelligence to manage client relationships\nAttention to detail and pride in your work\nProject management and scheduling experience\nNice to Haves \nExperience as an Executive Assistant\nExperience in short term rentals, vacation rentals, Airbnb, etc\nExperience with answering emails and messages on behalf of an executive\nCustomer support experience\nWhat\u2019s in it for you? \nThis is an opportunity for a passionate and driven professional to join a fast-growing team. You\u2019ll be paid well, respected, and trained. Destination Asset believes in supporting its team members to help them reach the professional success they seek.\nBenefits and Perks \nPaid time off\u00a0\nWork directly with the founder\nCompetitive pay with raise opportunities\nFully remote\nAs the company grows, so will the roles of each team member. When the company needs to hire, you\u2019ll be involved in this process.\nDirect access to STR and data expertise from Jacob.","locations":["Canada","United States","Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Belarus","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Czechia","Estonia","Georgia","Greece","Hungary","Kosovo","Latvia","Lithuania","Moldova","Montenegro","North Macedonia","Poland","Romania","Serbia","Slovakia","Ukraine"],"employment_type":"PART_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-12T16:25:42.894Z","expires_at":"2026-07-12T16:25:42.894Z","external_id":"destinationasset","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/teamup/remote-job/client-success-associate","title":"Client Success Associate","company":"TeamUp","location":"Remote","description":"Are you a relationship-driven professional who enjoys working closely with clients and ensuring they feel fully supported every step of the way?\nIf so, this opportunity might be a great fit for you!\nJoin a fast-growing, relationship-focused company that values strong partnerships, clear communication, and delivering a high-quality client experience.\nIn this role, you\u2019ll be the key point of contact for clients - building trust, maintaining consistent check-ins, and ensuring both clients and talent are set up for long-term success. You don\u2019t just care about our company; you also genuinely care about the businesses and teams you support. You take pride in understanding your clients\u2019 challenges, approaching situations with a calm, solutions-focused mindset, and helping them navigate issues with confidence and ease.\nWHAT\u2019S IN IT FOR YOU? \nCompetitive salary based on skills and experience;\nFull-time, long-term remote opportunity with stability and growth;\nIndependent contractor arrangement;\nWork directly with clients and play a key role in relationship building and retention;\nBe part of a collaborative, fast-paced, and people-first environment;\nWork alongside and grow with a dynamic global team;\nJoin team retreats, and company engagement activities;\nOpportunity for professional growth, development, and career progression;\nWork-from-home setup\nCOMPANY BACKGROUND \nTeamUp is a specialized recruiting partner for accounting, finance, and administrative roles. We support small to mid-sized firms across the US, Australia, and Canada by connecting them with top-tier remote talent - primarily from the Philippines and expanding into Latin America.\nWe focus on building long-term partnerships by ensuring strong alignment between clients and talent. Our goal is not just to fill roles, but to create lasting, successful working relationships that help businesses grow.\nJOB SUMMARY \nWe are seeking a proactive and client-focused Client Success Specialist to serve as the main point of contact for clients and help create a seamless, high-quality experience throughout the partnership. In this role, you will manage client relationships through structured onboarding, regular check-ins, and clear, timely communication across all touchpoints. Your main goal is to drive high client satisfaction, successful placements, and long-term engagement between clients and their hires. You\u2019ll also support the success of hires through onboarding guidance, performance coaching, and client\u2013talent alignment, while assisting in resolving client concerns and identifying potential risks early. Working closely with internal teams, you\u2019ll help ensure smooth coordination and continuously contribute to improving processes, outcomes, and the overall client experience.\nDUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \nServe as the primary point of contact for clients.\nBuild and maintain strong, long-term client relationships while liaising with clients, partners, and internal teams to ensure alignment and smooth coordination.\nConduct structured onboarding and planning for new hires to set them up for success.\nConduct regular client check-ins via email, calls, and other touchpoints to align expectations, resolve concerns, and ensure ongoing satisfaction.\nEnsure clear, timely, and proactive communication across all client interactions.\nAddress and resolve client concerns efficiently and professionally, with a solutions-focused and calm approach.\nIdentify potential risks and take proactive steps to support client retention and satisfaction.\nTrack action items, feedback, and follow-ups from client conversations to ensure accountability and execution.\nSupport alignment between clients and placed talent, including coaching calls, performance improvement plans (PIPs), and ongoing performance support when needed.\nConduct quarterly review prompts with clients on their hires and support development planning and performance discussions.\nAssist and guide clients on people and culture best practices, including engagement, team support, and performance management.\nContribute to the development and continuous improvement of client success processes, SOPs, and internal workflows.\nMaintain strong client relationships to drive satisfaction, retention, and repeat business.\nPerform other tasks as assigned.\nQUALIFICATIONS \nat least 1 to 2+ years of experience in client success, account management, customer-facing roles, or similar\nExperience in a multi-client environment such as BPO, shared services, or a professional services firm is highly preferred\nBackground in HR, recruitment, or talent management is a strong advantage\nStrong communication and relationship-building skills\nExperience working with US-based clients is preferred\nHighly organized with strong attention to detail\nAbility to manage multiple clients and priorities effectively\nProactive, solutions-oriented, and accountable\nAbility to handle concerns and escalations with a calm, patient, and professional demeanor\nComfortable working in a remote, fast-paced environment\nADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS \nWe\u2019re open to exceptional candidates based in the Philippines, the Caribbean, or Latin America\nAbility to work Eastern Time hours\nReliable, stable, and high-speed internet\nDedicated, distraction-free workspace\nDESCRIPTION OF IDEAL CANDIDATE \nAdaptable \u2013 You thrive in a fast-paced and evolving environment where priorities can shift quickly. You remain flexible, composed, and effective even when dealing with changing client needs or unexpected challenges.\nCalm and Patient \u2013 You handle pressure and client concerns with a steady, composed mindset. You don\u2019t get easily overwhelmed and are able to think clearly and respond professionally even in challenging situations.\nClient-Focused \u2013 You genuinely care about delivering an excellent client experience and take pride in helping clients succeed. You also care deeply about the client\u2019s team and talent, ensuring both sides are supported and set up for success.\nHighly Organized \u2013 You are able to manage multiple clients and priorities without losing attention to detail. You stay on top of follow-ups, action items, and deadlines to ensure nothing falls through the cracks.\nPositive & Personable \u2013 You bring a great personality and positive energy to your interactions. You build strong relationships easily because people enjoy working with you and trust your approach.\nProactive Problem Solver \u2013 You don\u2019t wait for issues to escalate; you identify potential challenges early and take initiative to address them. You think ahead, stay solution-focused, and take ownership in resolving concerns efficiently and professionally.\nRelationship-Driven \u2013 You naturally build trust and rapport with clients through consistent communication and genuine engagement. You prioritize long-term relationships over short-term transactions and ensure clients feel supported at every stage of the partnership.\nStrong Communicator \u2013 You communicate clearly, confidently, and professionally across all channels, whether written or verbal. You are able to adapt your communication style depending on the client and situation to ensure clarity and alignment.","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","South Africa"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-12T06:01:14.146Z","expires_at":"2026-07-12T06:01:14.146Z","external_id":"teamup","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/luxblueprint/remote-job/executive-assistant","title":"Executive Assistant","company":"Lux Blueprint","location":"Remote","description":"Client Success Manager & Executive Assistant \nCompany: Lux Blueprint \u2014 Real Estate Education & Coaching\nLocation: Remote\nType: Full-Time\nCompensation: $4,000-$10,000 per month (depending on prior experience)\nReports to: The two founders\nAbout Us \nWe run a fast-growing real estate education and coaching company. Our students are active investors working through our online program and community, and our deals side keeps us moving. We\u2019re looking for one sharp, dependable person to be the backbone of both our student experience and our day-to-day operations.\nIf you love being the person who keeps everything running, who students trust, and who the founders can hand anything to and forget about it \u2014 this is your role.\nWhat You\u2019ll Do \nClient Success & Community Management\nOwn and manage both founders\u2019 accounts on our educational platform (Skool), acting as the primary point of contact for students\nAnswer all student questions promptly and accurately \u2014 and when you don\u2019t have an answer yet, know exactly where to point them\nLearn our curriculum and methodology inside and out over time (we\u2019ll give you everything; you\u2019re responsible for absorbing it and becoming the go-to resource)\nBuild and maintain systems, SOPs, and a knowledge base / FAQ library so common student questions get answered fast and consistently\nKeep the community active, welcoming, and engaged\nHandle all inbound email related to student support, disputes, and refunds with professionalism and discretion\nOwn our 90-Day Money-Back Guarantee process end to end \u2014 tracking eligibility, communicating with students, and processing requests cleanly\nExecutive & Personal Assistance\nManage the calendars and schedules for both founders\nCoordinate content shoots and video scheduling\nPlan and book travel (flights, hotels, logistics)\nManage inboxes \u2014 triage, respond, flag, and keep nothing falling through the cracks\nHandle ad-hoc tasks and projects that keep the founders focused on growth\nWho You Are \nAn exceptional written communicator \u2014 clear, warm, and professional, even with frustrated customers\nHighly organized and proactive; you anticipate needs and don\u2019t wait to be asked twice\nA fast learner who\u2019s comfortable not knowing everything on day one but committed to mastering the material\nA systems thinker who\u2019d rather build a process once than answer the same question fifty times\nTrustworthy and discreet \u2014 you\u2019ll handle refunds, disputes, money, and the founders\u2019 personal logistics\nCalm under pressure and genuinely enjoys helping people succeed\nNice to Have \nExperience in customer success, community management, or as an executive/virtual\nassistant\nFamiliarity with Skool or similar course/community platforms\nBackground or interest in real estate, investing, or online education\nComfort with tools like Google Workspace, calendars, CRMs, and email management\nsystems\nLogistics \nHours: Mon\u2013Fri, with some flexibility\nTime zone: Must overlap with MST business hours\nStart date: ASAP","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Canada","United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-06-11T16:57:57.580Z","expires_at":"2026-07-11T16:57:57.580Z","external_id":"luxblueprint","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/virtahealth/remote-job/senior-accountant-1","title":"Senior Accountant","company":"Virta Health","location":"Remote","description":"Virta Health is on a mission to reverse metabolic disease in one billion people. Current treatment approaches aren\u2019t working\u2014over half of US adults have either type 2 diabetes or prediabetes, and obesity rates are at an all-time high. Virta is changing this by helping people reverse their metabolic condition through innovations in technology, personalized nutrition, and virtual care delivery reinvented from the ground up. We have raised over $350 million from top-tier investors, and partner with the largest health plans, employers, and government organizations to help their employees and members restore their health and take back their lives. Join us on our mission to reverse metabolic disease in one billion people.\nThe ideal candidate is passionate about process improvement and excited to leverage emerging technologies, including AI-enabled tools, to help build a more efficient and scalable accounting function.\nResponsibilities \nPrepare journal entries, analyses and account reconciliations\nHelp maintain and improve month-end close processes, including monthly balance sheet reconciliations\nEnsure compliance with GAAP\nIdentify opportunities to leverage automation, AI-enabled tools, and process improvements to reduce manual work, improve accuracy, and accelerate the month-end close process.\nRespond to information requests and assist with the annual financial statement audit\nAnalyze financial statements and GL accounts to ensure monthly, quarterly and annual fluctuations are in line with expectations and documented\nPrepare operational and ad hoc reporting for additional analysis associated with financial statement areas assigned\nAssist accounting leadership as needed\n90 Day Plan \nWithin your first 90 days at Virta, we expect you will do the following:\nTake ownership of preparing financial statement areas assigned to you (potential areas may include revenue, cost of goods sold, inventory, administrative fees, and others)\nIdentify at least one opportunity to streamline an accounting process through automation, AI-enabled tools, or workflow improvements that enhance efficiency and support a faster close.\nEstablish strong working relationships cross functionally\nMust-Haves \nBachelor\u2019s degree in accounting or finance\n3-4 years of experience preferably with a public accounting/private accounting mix\nCPA preferred\nExperience with one or more complex areas of accounting including but not limited to revenue recognition, inventory, stock-based compensation, debt/equity financing, business combinations or investments\nExperience leveraging automation, AI tools, or advanced technology solutions to improve accounting processes, reporting, reconciliations, or close efficiency preferred.\nAbility to read and analyze financial statements/reports\nComfort with ambiguity and lack of formally defined processes\nPublic company exposure preferred (either through Audit or industry background)\nStrong problem solving and analytical skills\nProficient in Microsoft Excel\nHighly organized and detail oriented\nComfort working in a fully remote setting\nValues-driven culture \nVirta\u2019s company values drive our culture, so you\u2019ll do well if:\nYou put people first and take care of yourself, your peers, and our patients equally\nYou have a strong sense of ownership and take initiative while empowering others to do the same\nYou prioritize positive impact over busy work\nYou have no ego and understand that everyone has something to bring to the table regardless of experience\nYou appreciate transparency and promote trust and empowerment through open access of information\nYou are evidence-based and prioritize data and science over seniority or dogma\nYou take risks and rapidly iterate \nIs this role not quite what you're looking for? Join our Talent Community and follow us on Linkedin to stay connected!\nVirta has a location based compensation structure. Starting pay will be based on a number of factors and commensurate with qualifications & experience. For this role, the compensation range is $83,738 to $110,000. Information about Virta\u2019s benefits is on our Careers page at: https://www.virtahealth.com/careers . \nAs part of your duties at Virta, you may come in contact with sensitive patient information that is governed by HIPAA. Throughout your career at Virta, you will be expected to follow Virta's security and privacy procedures to ensure our patients' information remains strictly confidential. Security and privacy training will be provided. \nAs a remote-first company, our team is spread across various locations with office hubs in Denver and San Francisco. \nClinical roles: We currently do not hire in the following states: AK, HI, RI \nCorporate roles: We currently do not hire in the following states: AK, AR, DE, HI, ME, MS, NM, OK, SD, VT, WI. \nVirta uses Ashby as its applicant tracking system, which incorporates AI-powered tools (provided by OpenAI, AWS, and Google Gemini) in certain aspects of the recruiting process, including application review, candidate screening, and interview note taking; your data is not used to train AI models, and all final hiring decisions are made by Virta Health personnel. For more information, see Ashby's AI Terms at https://www.ashbyhq.com/resources/terms-ai-features \n#LI-remote","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T04:28:22.401Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T04:28:22.401Z","external_id":"virtahealth","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/petdesk/remote-job/account-executive-3","title":"Account Executive","company":"PetDesk","location":"Remote","description":"About the Role\nOur Account Executives drive PetDesk\u2019s growth by attracting new veterinary clinics and expanding relationships with existing customers within defined territories. In this remote role, you\u2019ll manage the full sales cycle\u2014from outbound prospecting to deep discovery qualification, demo, and close\u2014while also converting inbound interest and partnering closely with our Sales Development team.\nYou\u2019ll use a consultative, solution-oriented sales approach grounded in credibility, trust, and a deep understanding of veterinary practice needs. A successful AE never skips discovery, educates buyers, recommends the right PetDesk solutions across our product suite, and collaborates cross-functionally with Marketing, Implementation, Customer Success, and Product to guide prospects smoothly through each stage of the customer journey.\nThis role supports territories in the Central time zone, and this role's core working hours are 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM Central Time. All candidates must be comfortable working those hours.\nApply if You're Excited to\nProspect, qualify, and nurture leads through consistent outbound activity, delivering tailored product demos that address the needs of veterinary practices\nManage an accurate pipeline and forecast by using Salesforce and Gong Deal Boards as your single sources of truth, ensuring complete, timely data that supports visibility and coaching\nLead high-quality sales conversations, reviewing call notes same-day, preparing stakeholders with full context, and guiding the agenda to address customer needs\nOwn key onboarding and handoff steps, including kickoff scheduling and payment-related transitions for new product sales, while leveraging automation to streamline the customer journey\nPartner cross-functionally with Marketing, Implementation, Customer Success, and Product to ensure a smooth, customer-centric experience from first touch through go-live\nDemonstrate accountability and integrity by owning outcomes, solving problems proactively, maintaining ethical selling practices, and protecting customer information\nStay adaptable and growth-oriented, continuously learning through product updates, market trends, and new sales techniques\nTravel approximately 10% for trade shows, sales kickoffs, customer events, and industry conferences\nAbout You\n2+ years of full-cycle SaaS inside sales experience, with a track record of owning your pipeline, forecasting accurately, and hitting revenue targets\nHands-on CRM expertise (Salesforce preferred), with strong attention to detail in data accuracy, follow-ups, and documentation\nExcellent communicator, especially over the phone\u2014our sales motion is 95% virtual, so clarity, professionalism, and reliable follow-through are essential\nStrong work ethic and learning mindset, staying coachable, applying feedback, and taking accountability for your performance\nNatural problem solver who brings clear analysis, proposed solutions, and consistent follow-through\nCollaborative team player who contributes to shared goals and works effectively with Marketing, Implementation, and Customer Success\nYou are committed to focusing your time and energy on this role exclusively; while we respect a strong hustle, we are not seeking candidates who are actively working multiple sales roles\nBonus points for experience in the veterinary industry or selling to small businesses\nBenefits & Perks\nPresidents Club for top, eligible sales performers!\nMedical coverage for employees and dependents (80-90% covered by employer)\nEmployer HSA contribution with HDHP\n401(k) match up to 3.5%\nDependent Care Flexible Spending Account (FSA)\nDental & Vision coverage available\nBasic Life and AD&D Insurance\nShort and Long Term Disability\nFlexible Time Off & 12 Paid Annual Holidays\nPaid Parental Leave\nPawternity Leave, Financial Pet Adoption Support & Subsidized Pet Insurance\n$250 Annual Stipend for Learning and Development","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T04:17:00.953Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T04:17:00.953Z","external_id":"petdesk","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/peek/remote-job/product-manager","title":"Product Manager","company":"Peek","location":"Remote","description":"About Peek\nPeek is the operating system powering the experiences industry \u2014 from museums and attractions to tours and activities. With over $7B in bookings, Peek\u2019s AI-powered platform has helped thousands of merchants to increase revenues, save time, and deliver seamless guest experiences. Customers include MoMA, Whitney Museum, Seattle Aquarium, Bryant Park & Looping Group. The company has raised over $150 million from institutional investors Westcap, Goldman Sachs, and SpringCoast Partners. \nAs a remote-first company recognized by Forbes as one of America's Best Startup Employers and by Built In as a 2025 and 2026 Best Place to Work, we are a global team of \"Peeksters\" who \"Obsess Over Our Customers,\" \"Accomplish Big Things,\" \"Collaborate With Purpose,\" and \"Get Better Every Day.\"\nThe Role\nWe're hiring an Associate Product Manager to join our small, high-ownership product team supporting the ACME brand \u2014 a B2B SaaS platform serving museums, cultural attractions, and non-profit organizations across North America.\nThis is a strong opportunity for someone looking to further their career in product management or making a deliberate move into product \u2014 whether you're coming from implementation, operations, customer success, or a technical role. You will receive mentorship from a senior product lead in AI Integration strategy and enterprise platform design.\nThe role has two core areas:\n~70% \u2014 Core Product PM: Own features for ACME from discovery through launch. You'll write requirements, think through edge cases, and be the person cross-functional teams trust for accurate, grounded answers. Opportunities to support cross brand features and/or processes.\n~30% \u2014 Integrations PM (Workato/Salesforce): Own ACME's enterprise integration capabilities, powered by Workato. This includes building and maintaining recipes that connect ACME to Salesforce for partners, supporting implementations, and managing a backlog of integration requests. This scope may grow or evolve as our integration strategy develops.\nWhat You\u2019ll Do\nProduct Management\nWrite clear, thorough product specs and PRDs that engineering and design can act on without constant back-and-forth\nManage and prioritize a ticket backlog with accuracy and consistency \u2014 nothing falls through the cracks\nThink carefully through use cases and edge cases before anything goes to development\nPartner with ops and sales teams to represent the product clearly in operator-facing contexts\nUse analytics tools to monitor product usage and identify opportunities and measure impact of releases\nUse AI tools actively and responsibly in your day-to-day workflow \u2014 for research synthesis, writing, competitive analysis, summarizing feedback, and accelerating decisions\nIdentify opportunities to leverage AI, automation, and webhook-based workflows to solve real end-user problems \u2014 translating what's technically possible into features that actually ship and matter\nStay curious about the AI and automation landscape; bring forward practical ideas for how emerging tooling can reduce manual work or unlock new operator capabilities across our platform\nIntegrations (Workato / Salesforce)\nDesign, build, and maintain Workato recipes that integrate ACME with Salesforce using REST APIs, webhooks, data mapping, conditional logic, and workflow automation\nSupport real-time data synchronization and business process automation across operator environments\nTroubleshoot and resolve integration issues raised by operators or internal teams; own the integration support queue\nManage the backlog of integration requests, balancing urgency against available capacity\nPartner with implementation teams to onboard new enterprise partners onto the Workato platform\nMaintain documentation on integration architecture, recipes, and known edge cases\nValidate that Workato recipes perform as expected in staging and production environments\nWhat We\u2019re Looking For (Required)\n1\u20132+ years of product management experience, or equivalent in a PM-adjacent role (product operations, business analyst, technical PM) where you owned discovery, requirements, and cross-functional collaboration\nFamiliar with Salesforce as an admin, power user, or in a customer-facing capacity, and comfortable working within CRM-driven workflows\nTechnically curious \u2014 comfortable with REST APIs, webhooks, and integration logic; able to create Workato recipes following best practices for task efficiency. Strong knowledge of SQL and familiarity with Ruby\nUser-grounded \u2014 you can clearly articulate the user problem behind any ticket you own, and you ask \"why\" before you write requirements\nA clear, reliable writer \u2014 your specs are readable, your async updates are complete without being long, and cross-functional teams trust your answers\nAI-native in your workflow \u2014 you've meaningfully used AI tools to accelerate research, writing, or analysis, and can speak to how\nHands-on experience with an integration platform (Workato or Zapier preferred)\nLocated in Latin America with meaningful overlap with US time zones\nNice to Have\nSalesforce Administrator Certification \u2014 we'll support you in obtaining this if not already certified\nWorkato Integration Developer Certification \u2014 same as above\nSalesforce Nonprofit Cloud (NPC) or NPSP certification\nPrior product management experience in any capacity\nExperience at an online booking platform, travel tech, payments platform, or B2B SaaS business\nFamiliarity with agile processes, Jira, and sprint-based delivery\nExperience working with or alongside customer success or implementation teams","locations":["Mexico"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T04:32:04.206Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T04:32:04.206Z","external_id":"peek","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/themultiple/remote-job/full-stack-team-leader-content-management-system","title":"Full Stack Team Leader - Content Management System","company":"The Multiple","location":"Remote","description":"Who are we? \nWelcome to Multiple ( https://themultiple.com ), your go-to iGaming service provider. We\u2019re here to empower iGaming operators, allowing them to thrive in such a volatile industry. Our years of expertise, cutting-edge technology, and passion for delivering extraordinary player experiences make us the right choice for any company looking to elevate their success. We offer a range of iGaming offerings such as; Gaming Services, Casino Marketing, Sportsbook Marketing and Operations, Creative, Data and B.I, Operations (CS, RPF, KYC), VIP Management, Acquisition, Social Media, Content, Product, Legal and Compliance.\nThe Role: \nWe are looking for a Full Stack Team leader to expand our existing team building our B2B Content Management System (CMS). The chosen candidate will be asked to lead the implementation of the CMS for a particular platform and to build the team, mentor them and develop their capabilities.\nKey Responsibilities:\nBuild a CMS team that will work to implement, maintain and expand the existing CMS for use in new potential markets.\nContribute the the core library of the CMS.\nBuild and maintain the migration and release process for the CMS.\nManage and mentor the team in accomplishing their tasks on multiple brands.\nContribute to maintaining the stability of the system through code reviews and test coverage.\nRequirements:\nMinimum 5 years experience with full stack development.\nMinimum 2 years experience in a leadership position.\nGood communication skills and a strong sense of leadership and ownership.\nStrong experience with DirectUs or similar headless CMS platforms.\nStrong experience with SQL. Experience with Node, Typescript, GraphQL and Vue are considered an asset.\nWhat we offer: \nAttractive remuneration package\nWellness benefit\u00a0\nEur1,000 Refer a friend bonus\nOne day birthday holiday\nYou should not apply if ... \nYou want a normal 9-5 job. This role is not easy & requires an all-in mentality. We are looking for team members\u00a0who will put in the work that others won`t.\nYou cannot take constructive feedback.\nYou can`t handle stress and pressure.\nYou have the mindset of \"Quick Money\", this is a marathon, not a sprint.\nYou do not embody our core values.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T03:31:15.105Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T03:31:15.105Z","external_id":"themultiple","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/virtahealth/remote-job/director-revenue-accounting","title":"Director, Revenue Accounting","company":"Virta Health","location":"Remote","description":"Virta Health is on a mission to reverse metabolic disease in one billion people. Current treatment approaches aren\u2019t working\u2014over half of US adults have either type 2 diabetes or prediabetes, and obesity rates are at an all-time high. Virta is changing this by helping people reverse their metabolic condition through innovations in technology, personalized nutrition, and virtual care delivery reinvented from the ground up. We have raised over $350 million from top-tier investors, and partner with the largest health plans, employers, and government organizations to help their employees and members restore their health and take back their lives. Join us on our mission to reverse metabolic disease in one billion people.\nAs the Director, Revenue Accounting, you\u2019ll own one of the most critical areas of financial reporting for a rapidly growing healthcare company. You\u2019ll work closely with senior leadership, build scalable revenue processes, and lead a team that ensures accurate reporting under ASC 606. This is a high-visibility role with direct impact on strategic decisions, operational execution, and external reporting.\nResponsibilities \nLead all aspects of revenue accounting, including month-end close, analysis and reporting, controls considerations and technical accounting under ASC 606.\nOversee contract review for revenue recognition implications.\nLead and mentor a team of two revenue accountants, providing coaching and professional development.\nPartner with Strategic Finance, Legal, Commercial, and Operations to support accurate forecasting, reporting, and compliance.\nDrive continuous improvement in processes, systems, and controls to support scale and operational excellence.\nSupport external audits and reviews\nAssist the Accounting team as needed with ad hoc tasks and projects\n90 Day Plan \nWithin your first 90 days at Virta, we expect you will do the following:\nBecome a subject matter expert in Virta\u2019s business model, revenue streams, and contracts.\nDevelop strong working relationships with key cross-functional stakeholders (Strategic Finance, Legal, Commercial, Operations).\nAssess current systems and processes and propose improvements for scalability and accuracy.\nTake ownership of the revenue reporting process and implement improvements on revenue reporting.\nMust-Haves \nBachelor\u2019s degree in Accounting, Finance or related field\nCPA with strong technical knowledge of ASC 606\n10+ years of progressive experience in public accounting and industry, with at least 3+ years focused on revenue accounting\nExperience in a fast-paced, public company environment\n3+ years in a leadership role managing teams and developing talent\nDemonstrated ability to design and implement scalable processes and controls\nExcellent communication skills and ability to partner cross-functionally\nComfortable working in a fully remote setting\nValues-driven culture \nVirta\u2019s company values drive our culture, so you\u2019ll do well if:\nYou put people first and take care of yourself, your peers, and our patients equally\nYou have a strong sense of ownership and take initiative while empowering others to do the same\nYou prioritize positive impact over busy work\nYou have no ego and understand that everyone has something to bring to the table regardless of experience\nYou appreciate transparency and promote trust and empowerment through open access of information\nYou are evidence-based and prioritize data and science over seniority or dogma\nYou take risks and rapidly iterate \nIs this role not quite what you're looking for? Join our Talent Community and follow us on Linkedin to stay connected!\nVirta has a location based compensation structure. Starting pay will be based on a number of factors and commensurate with qualifications & experience. For this role, the compensation range is $175,088-$200,100. Information about Virta\u2019s benefits is on our Careers page at: https://www.virtahealth.com/careers . \nAs part of your duties at Virta, you may come in contact with sensitive patient information that is governed by HIPAA. Throughout your career at Virta, you will be expected to follow Virta's security and privacy procedures to ensure our patients' information remains strictly confidential. Security and privacy training will be provided. \nAs a remote-first company, our team is spread across various locations with office hubs in Denver and San Francisco. \nClinical roles: We currently do not hire in the following states: AK, HI, RI \nCorporate roles: We currently do not hire in the following states: AK, AR, DE, HI, ME, MS, NM, OK, SD, VT, WI. \nVirta uses Ashby as its applicant tracking system, which incorporates AI-powered tools (provided by OpenAI, AWS, and Google Gemini) in certain aspects of the recruiting process, including application review, candidate screening, and interview note taking; your data is not used to train AI models, and all final hiring decisions are made by Virta Health personnel. For more information, see Ashby's AI Terms at https://www.ashbyhq.com/resources/terms-ai-features \n#LI-remote","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T04:30:53.372Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T04:30:53.372Z","external_id":"virtahealth","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/peek/remote-job/senior-full-stack-engineer","title":"Senior Full Stack Engineer","company":"Peek","location":"Remote","description":"About Peek\nPeek is the operating system powering the experiences industry \u2014 from museums and attractions to tours and activities. With over $7B in bookings, Peek\u2019s AI-powered platform has helped thousands of merchants to increase revenues, save time, and deliver seamless guest experiences. Customers include MoMA, Whitney Museum, Seattle Aquarium, Bryant Park & Looping Group. The company has raised over $150 million from institutional investors Westcap, Goldman Sachs, and SpringCoast Partners.\nAs a remote-first company recognized by Forbes as one of America's Best Startup Employers and by Built In as a 2025 and 2026 Best Place to Work, we are a global team of \"Peeksters\" who \"Obsess Over Our Customers,\" \"Accomplish Big Things,\" \"Collaborate With Purpose,\" and \"Get Better Every Day.\"\nThe Role\nWe work on several systems: our ACME operations management suite, embeddable scheduling and booking widgets, B2B and B2C sales and support tooling, and custom solutions for enterprise operators. The work is technically varied, and the stakes are real: operators depend on this software to run their businesses.\nWe\u2019re hiring a Senior Full Stack Engineer who works AI-first. That means you treat AI as a core part of how you build, break down ambiguous problems, delegate to agents, review their work critically, and course-correct when things go sideways. You'll design and operate complex agent orchestration systems, develop patterns for human-agent collaboration, and ship real product features primarily through agent-assisted development.\nOver the past few months, we've seen a step-function improvement in the reliability and capabilities of long-running AI agents. We're adapting our engineering practice to match, and we want engineers who are already building this way and are excited to push it further.\nWhat You\u2019ll Do\nArchitect and break down ambiguous product problems into concrete, well-scoped tasks for agents to execute and ship full-stack features, owning work from design through production release\nDesign and operate complex agent orchestration systems that ship real product features\nDesign APIs and data models that are clean, consistent, and built to last, not just fast to write\nContribute to our AI-first engineering culture, share patterns, document what works, and help the team level up on how we build with AI\nUse AI tools fluently \u2014 Claude Code, Augment, or equivalent \u2014 to compress implementation time, then critically review everything that comes out of them\nCollaborate closely with Product and Design to identify gaps in specs, surface edge cases early, and push back when something isn't ready to ship\nSet the quality bar: well-structured, maintainable code; conduct thorough code reviews; maintain adequate test coverage; and catch bugs introduced by AI before they reach production\nWhat We\u2019re Looking For\nRequired\n5+ years of professional development using Java and/or JavaScript with a meaningful track record of shipping production systems\nStrong backend fundamentals: API design, data modeling, SQL, service reliability, and debugging production issues\nDemonstrated daily use of AI coding tools (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor or equivalent) in a production engineering workflow\nAbility to critically evaluate AI-generated code: catch logic errors, identify security issues, assess maintainability, and own what gets merged regardless of how it was written\nStrong system design instincts: you think about tradeoffs, edge cases, and what happens when things scale or fail\nClear communicator: you can articulate why you made a technical choice, flag when a spec has holes, and disagree constructively\nInterest in Elixir or functional programming languages as we expand our stack\nNice to Haves\nExperience building B2B SaaS products, ideally with complex multi-tenant data models or transactional workflows\nExperience on small, high-output teams where you've had to make architectural calls without a committee\nFrontend experience, particularly with Angular or modern JS frameworks, enough to own a feature end-to-end\nBackground in the travel, hospitality, or experiences industry\nWhat We Value\nA few things that define how we build:\nJudgment over speed: AI compresses implementation time. What differentiates engineers now isn't typing speed or memorized syntax; it's the ability to make the right calls on what to build, how to build it, and when it's not ready to ship.\nOwnership: You built it? You own it. That includes AI-generated code. You know when to use agents and when to do it yourself.\nDirectness: We want people who ask hard questions, surface problems early, and are willing to push back on a bad spec rather than build it and hope for the best.\nQuality as a habit: Peer code reviews, test coverage, and clean APIs are not optional. We move fast, but not by cutting corners on the things that compound.","locations":["Mexico"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T04:24:33.127Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T04:24:33.127Z","external_id":"peek","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/peek/remote-job/content-creator","title":"Content Creator","company":"Peek","location":"Remote","description":"About Peek\nPeek is the operating system powering the experiences industry \u2014 from museums and attractions to tours and activities. With over $7B in bookings, Peek\u2019s AI-powered platform has helped thousands of merchants to increase revenues, save time, and deliver seamless guest experiences. Customers include MoMA, Whitney Museum, Seattle Aquarium, Bryant Park & Looping Group. The company has raised over $150 million from institutional investors Westcap, Goldman Sachs, and SpringCoast Partners. \nAs a remote-first company recognized by Forbes as one of America's Best Startup Employers and by Built In as a 2025 and 2026 Best Place to Work, we are a global team of \"Peeksters\" who \"Obsess Over Our Customers,\" \"Accomplish Big Things,\" \"Collaborate With Purpose,\" and \"Get Better Every Day.\"\nThe Role\nWe are seeking a highly creative, data-driven Content Creator to lead the development, testing, and optimization of marketing creative across multiple brands and across both paid and organic channels.\nThis role blends hands-on content creation and community engagement, ensuring each brand\u2019s voice and audience strategy is reflected in high-performing content. You leverage AI tools to scale winning creative concepts across a portfolio of brands.\nYou obsess over the voice of the customer. You work hard to understand the needs and challenges that operators and merchants face in order to create content that goes a level deeper to meet the objectives of small business owners looking to grow and automate their businesses.\nResponsibilities\nCreative Asset Production\nProduce and launch 5\u201310 new ad creatives per week\nDevelop high-performing hooks, messaging, and visual concepts optimized for paid media platforms (TikTok, Meta, YouTube, LinkedIn)\nRapidly iterate on creative variations to identify winning combinations of messaging, format, and audience targeting\nUse AI tools to ideate, produce variations, and test concepts at speed without sacrificing quality\nVertical Video Creation\nCreate and edit 3\u20135 vertical videos per week optimized for paid performance channels (TikTok, Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts)\nEnsure videos are designed for scroll-stopping engagement within the first few seconds\nManage end-to-end production: scripting, shooting, editing, and publishing\nCreative Testing & Optimization\nLead ongoing creative testing initiatives across paid platforms to improve campaign performance\nAnalyze results and iterate quickly to drive improvements in efficiency and scale\nTrack creative performance and surface insights to inform future content strategy\nOrganic Social Content\nSocial Publishing \nManage posting across organic social platforms\nContent & Community Management \nEngage with the community by responding to comments, messages, and interactions\nMaintain a consistent brand voice while fostering authentic engagement and audience growth\nBuild relationships with operators, customers, and community members through genuine interactions\nSocial Listening \nMonitor social platforms to identify trends, audience sentiment, and opportunities for content engagement\nSurface insights to inform both organic content strategy and paid creative testing\nQualifications\nProven track record creating and publishing content on TikTok, Instagram, YouTube, or similar platforms (high school, college, or personal channels count \u2014 we care about evidence, not job titles)\nStrong expertise in short-form video and vertical content formats\nDeep understanding of viral content mechanics, hooks, and audience psychology\nDemonstrated ability to produce high volumes of creative and test rapidly\nExperience using AI tools for creative production, ideation, and workflow automation (or strong desire to learn and experiment)\nStrong analytical mindset with the ability to connect creative experimentation to performance metrics\nVideo editing proficiency\nNatural on-camera presence and comfort being the face of a brand\nSelf-directed work style: ship high-quality work without constant oversight","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T04:35:18.191Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T04:35:18.191Z","external_id":"peek","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/homegeniusexteriors/remote-job/recruitment-leader","title":"Recruitment Leader","company":"Home Genius Exteriors","location":"Remote","description":"Location: Remote (Preferred: New Jersey area) | Quarterly travel to our NJ office as needed\nCompensation: $80,000\u2013$90,000 Total Compensation (Base + Performance Bonus)\nSchedule: Full-time | Flexibility required for evenings and weekends based on hiring needs\nBuild the Team Behind One of America's Fastest-Growing Home Remodeling Companies\nAt Home Genius Exteriors, we don't just build exceptional home improvement teams\u2014we build careers. Since our founding, we've grown from a small startup into a nationally recognized home remodeling company by investing in great people, strong leadership, and a winning culture.\nWe're looking for a Recruitment Leader who thrives in a fast-paced, high-volume hiring environment and is excited to lead a team while remaining hands-on in the recruiting process. If you're passionate about interviewing, developing people, and driving hiring results, we'd love to meet you.\nWhat You'll Do \nAs a Recruitment Leader, you'll oversee a team of Talent Representatives while actively recruiting and hiring top talent across multiple markets. This is a leadership role for someone who enjoys rolling up their sleeves and leading by example.\nResponsibilities\nLead, coach, and develop a team of 4\u20136 Talent Representatives\nConduct high-volume interviews and make hiring decisions for multiple markets\nPartner with hiring managers to identify staffing needs and fill positions quickly\nSupport recruiting efforts by sourcing and engaging candidates (approximately 10\u201320% of your role)\nMonitor team performance, provide coaching, and drive accountability\nManage daily recruiting operations and hiring workflows\nTrack hiring metrics and ensure recruiting goals are consistently achieved\nImprove recruiting processes and contribute ideas that increase hiring success\nServe as a hands-on leader who jumps in wherever needed to support the team\nWhat We're Looking For\nExperience in high-volume recruiting, interviewing, or talent acquisition\nPrevious leadership experience as a Lead, Supervisor, Manager, or Team Lead\nStrong interviewing and candidate evaluation skills\nAbility to thrive in a fast-paced, metrics-driven environment\nComfortable working flexible hours, including evenings and weekends when hiring demands require\nSelf-motivated with excellent organizational and time management skills\nExperience in home improvement, field marketing, sales recruiting, or similar industries is a plus\nSuccess in This Role\nYou'll be measured on:\nMonthly hiring goals achieved\nInterview volume and hiring activity\nTeam productivity and overall recruiting performance\nTime-to-fill open positions\nQuality of hires and retention\nWhy Home Genius Exteriors?\nCompetitive base salary plus performance bonus\nRemote flexibility with limited quarterly travel\nOpportunity to lead and grow a high-performing recruiting team\nFast-paced, high-growth company with advancement opportunities\nSupportive leadership and collaborative culture\nPaid training and ongoing professional development\nFull benefits package including medical, dental, vision after the first 30 days\nIf you're a recruiting leader who loves building teams, developing people, and making an impact every day, apply today and help Home Genius Exteriors continue its incredible growth.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T04:36:57.126Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T04:36:57.126Z","external_id":"homegeniusexteriors","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/petdesk/remote-job/implementation-project-manager","title":"Implementation Project Manager","company":"PetDesk","location":"Remote","description":"About the Role\nPetDesk is a leading provider of client communication software tailored for veterinary clinics to communicate with Pet Parents. As an Implementation Project Manager at PetDesk, you will play a vital role in the onboarding and configuration of new customers through an inquisitive, consultative, and refreshingly personable post-sales process, ensuring a smooth and successful transition to our software. Your expertise, attention to detail, and exceptional communication skills will be essential in uncovering and resolving unique needs, allowing pet care provider businesses to thrive.\nApply if You're Excited to\nLead the implementation process for PetDesk customers, work closely with customers to gather requirements, configure the software to their specific needs, and ensure a smooth and efficient onboarding experience\nUse a customer success-based conversation approach that focuses on educating customers on how we can help improve processes and save time. Conduct comprehensive training sessions to educate customers on how to use PetDesk's software features and functionalities effectively\nUnderstand each customer's unique requirements and challenges. Analyze and interpret results in our backend system to inform the customer, problem-solve through issues, and give an accurate and confident response\nDevelop strong relationships with customers by providing exceptional service and support throughout the implementation process; act as a trusted advisor, offering guidance and best practices to help them optimize their use of PetDesk's client communication software\nIdentify and resolve technical issues or challenges customers encounter during implementation. Collaborate with internal teams, including product support, Sales, and CS, to ensure timely resolution of issues and customer satisfaction\nMaintain accurate documentation of customer interactions, implementation details, and configurations within our CRM. Generate reports and provide insights on implementation progress, challenges, and successes to internal stakeholders\nManage an onboarding pipeline which includes approximately 30-40 customers at any one time and undertake 3-4 customer calls a day\nAbout You\nMinimum of 3-5 years of experience in a customer-facing role, preferably in software implementation, customer success, or a related field, with primary customer communications over the phone or virtual meetings\nProficient in learning and understanding software applications quickly. Familiarity with client communication software, CRM systems, or SaaS solutions is advantageous\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to effectively communicate complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences\nPassionate about delivering exceptional customer experiences. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to build rapport and trust with customers\nStrong analytical and problem-solving abilities to identify and resolve customer issues effectively\nCollaborative and able to work effectively with cross-functional teams, including sales, product, and customer support, to deliver excellent customer outcomes\nExcellent multi-tasker with the ability to self-manage and get the highest priority tasks done\nThrives at task-driven project completion workflows\nExperience in Salesforce, Zendesk, or similar software is strongly preferred\nExperience working with veterinary clinics or the pet care industry is a plus\nBenefits & Perks\nMedical coverage for employees and dependents (80-90% covered by employer)\nEmployer HSA contribution with HDHP\n401(k) match up to 3.5%\nDependent Care Flexible Spending Account (FSA)\nDental & Vision coverage available\nBasic Life and AD&D Insurance\nShort and Long Term Disability\n12 Paid Annual Holidays\nPaid Parental Leave\nPawternity Leave, Financial Pet Adoption Support & Subsidized Pet Insurance","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T04:19:51.106Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T04:19:51.106Z","external_id":"petdesk","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/benchling/remote-job/implementation-manager","title":"Implementation Manager","company":"Benchling","location":"Remote","description":"We are rebuilding biotech for the AI era.\nWhen a breakthrough is delayed, the world waits. Getting a molecule from discovery to patients, or a crop from lab to field, involves thousands of slow, manual, disconnected steps. AI has the potential to change this, compressing decades of R&D work into years. But that only happens when clean, structured scientific data and AI are built into how science gets done.\nBenchling is the AI platform for biotech R&D. Scientists use Benchling to design experiments, capture structured data, and run AI agents and models directly in their workflows. Over 200,000 scientists around the world trust Benchling to power their most important work, from academic labs to Sanofi, Moderna, and more than half of the world's top 50 biopharma.\nWe\u2019re building an AI scientist for our customers. We can\u2019t do that if we haven\u2019t built the muscle ourselves. AI fluency is the foundation we build on; it's core to how we work, and we're committed to helping every new hire integrate it into their day-to-day. As part of our interview process, you'll complete a brief AI-focused exercise or discussion so we can understand how you think about and use AI to drive impact in your role. Feel free to reference any tools, platforms, or workflows you use today.\nROLE OVERVIEW \nBenchling is building a world-class Professional Services team to drive implementations for our rapidly expanding customer base. Implementation Managers work with our customers, from small Biotech startups to the largest BioPharmas in the world to develop a deep understanding of their R&D Processes, and roll out solutions that transform how their research teams work together.\nTo be successful in this role, you will leverage your scientific background, project management skills, and product expertise to drive successful implementations of the Benchling platform. You will work hand in hand with the research scientists at our customers, and teams throughout Benchling to implement our solutions, and ensure our customers are successful. Implementation Managers lead all aspects of customer rollouts from requirements analysis and solution design, to configurations, testing, training, and onboarding users onto the system.\nRESPONSIBILITIES \nManage initial rollouts for new Benchling customers as well as expansion projects with new teams or for new processes at existing customers\nOwn implementation success from project kickoff to go-live, leveraging strong project management skills, scientific expertise, and deep product knowledge.\nBuild and execute detailed project plans, own project activities, work with other team members to execute on project deliverables to ensure on time, on budget, high quality deployments.\nUnderstand customers' scientific workflows and determine how Benchling can best be leveraged to meet their key business needs.\nLead requirements and design workshops, perform data modeling & application configuration, develop test plans and guide UAT execution, train and onboard users.\nAct as a trusted advisor for customers, guiding them through the implementation ensuring they leverage and apply Benchling Best Practices.\nUnderstand and document customer pain points, advocate for them internally to influence product changes.\nIdentify and work with sales on opportunities for account expansion post go-live.\nQUALIFICATIONS \nMS or Ph.D. in Molecular Biology, Biochemistry, Biotechnology, Immunology, Bioinformatics, Biological Engineering or a related field.\nAt least 2 years of experience in a lab or R&D setting, ideally in antibody discovery or strain engineering or process development. You must be able to empathize with scientists and quickly understand complicated scientific concepts.\nSoftware Implementation experience, preferably with a SaaS software company.\nStrong communication skills. You must be able to quickly and effectively connect with a range of stakeholders, including scientists, IT project leads, and executives.\nSelf-starter with the ability to be successful in a startup environment.\nCurious, creative, and tenacious. You should be excited to collaborate with customers and other Benchling teammates as a thought partner.\nAbility to travel up to 25% based on customer and project needs.\nExperience using Benchling platform\nBonus if you have:\nExperience using Benchling, especially if you\u2019ve been a Benchling administrator.\nSoftware Implementation experience, preferably with a SaaS software company.\nSALARY & BENEFITS \nFull-time employees outside the U.S. enjoy a comprehensive benefits program tailored to their region of residence.\nBenchling takes a market-based approach to pay. The candidate's starting pay will be determined based on job-related skills, experience, qualifications, interview performance, and work location.\n#LI-Remote\n#BI-Remote\n#LI-TD1\nBenchling welcomes everyone. \nWe believe diversity enriches our team so we hire people with a wide range of identities, backgrounds, and experiences.\nWe are an equal opportunity employer. That means we don\u2019t discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law, including but not limited to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.","locations":["United Kingdom"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T03:40:03.155Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T03:40:03.155Z","external_id":"benchling","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/peek/remote-job/technical-support-representative","title":"Technical Support Representative","company":"Peek","location":"Remote","description":"About Peek\nPeek is the operating system powering the experiences industry \u2014 from museums and attractions to tours and activities. With over $7B in bookings, Peek\u2019s AI-powered platform has helped thousands of merchants to increase revenues, save time, and deliver seamless guest experiences. Customers include MoMA, Whitney Museum, Seattle Aquarium, Bryant Park & Looping Group. The company has raised over $150 million from institutional investors Westcap, Goldman Sachs, and SpringCoast Partners. Learn more at www.peek.com .\nAs a remote-first company recognized by Forbes as one of America's Best Startup Employers and by Built In as a 2025 and 2026 Best Place to Work, we are a global team of \"Peeksters\" who \"Obsess Over Our Customers,\" \"Accomplish Big Things,\" \"Collaborate With Purpose,\" and \"Get Better Every Day.\"\nThe Role\nPeek is hiring a friendly, passionate, and self-motivated Partner Support Representative to help our activity partners grow their businesses using Peek\u2019s SaaS platform PeekPro. The Partner Support Representative acts as the first line of defense for product questions and technical troubleshooting.\nThe ideal candidate adapts well to a fast-paced environment, provides a high degree of professional responsiveness and follow-up to our existing and potential partners, and demonstrates strong problem-solving skills. The Partner Support Associate will work in unison with other Support team members, as well as provide information reviewed by our Product and Engineering teams as they work to improve PeekPro. This full-time role is entirely remote and will report to a Team Lead in the United States.\nOur collaborative and rapidly evolving team will rely on the Associate to make our partners\u2019 day by solving issues completely, quickly, and correctly.\nResponsibilities\nFollow-up and see through resolutions on customer inquiries across channels, including phone calls, emails, and Helpdesk requests, while maintaining a high customer satisfaction rating\nCraft informative, timely, and instructional messages in response to product- and tech-related queries\nActive participant in team meetings and in assisting other colleagues across the company\nRepresent the voice of our customers internally at Peek by sharing customer feedback using Zendesk processes\nLearn Peek\u2019s rapidly evolving products; contribute suggestions from your built experience on updating our Helpdesk and templates to keep pace with these changes\nMeet monthly Items per month, CSat and QA minimums and develop consistent performance\nSkills You Already Have\n2+ years of experience in customer service and/or technical support\nFull-time availability; ability to work 5 consecutive days (possible schedule to include weekend day)\nExcellent English written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills (minimum 50 WPM on typing exam)\nNatural enthusiasm for helping people solve technical problems\nPatience and ability to troubleshoot and teach new software to non-tech-savvy operator partners\nAbility to work in a dynamic environment without skipping a beat\nMust be punctual and reliable\nStrong deductive reasoning skills, with an ability to uproot the cause of a reported issue\nDiscretion in handling potentially sensitive information about a partner, partner\u2019s account, or business\nConsistent and dependable WiFi in a personal workspace that allows for distraction-free environment\nNice to Haves\nSpanish language fluency\nInterest in the travel/tourism industry\nExperience working within Zendesk or other support tooling\nExperience working with Salesforce, JIRA, Slack, and/or G-Suite","locations":["Mexico"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T04:28:52.911Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T04:28:52.911Z","external_id":"peek","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/benchling/remote-job/agentic-ai-engineer","title":"Agentic AI Engineer","company":"Benchling","location":"Remote","description":"We are rebuilding biotech for the AI era.\nWhen a breakthrough is delayed, the world waits. Getting a molecule from discovery to patients, or a crop from lab to field, involves thousands of slow, manual, disconnected steps. AI has the potential to change this, compressing decades of R&D work into years. But that only happens when clean, structured scientific data and AI are built into how science gets done.\nBenchling is the AI platform for biotech R&D. Scientists use Benchling to design experiments, capture structured data, and run AI agents and models directly in their workflows. Over 200,000 scientists around the world trust Benchling to power their most important work, from academic labs to Sanofi, Moderna, and more than half of the world's top 50 biopharma.\nWe\u2019re building an AI scientist for our customers. We can\u2019t do that if we haven\u2019t built the muscle ourselves. AI fluency is the foundation we build on; it's core to how we work, and we're committed to helping every new hire integrate it into their day-to-day. As part of our interview process, you'll complete a brief AI-focused exercise or discussion so we can understand how you think about and use AI to drive impact in your role. Feel free to reference any tools, platforms, or workflows you use today.\nROLE OVERVIEW \nBiotechnology is rewriting life as we know it, from the medicines we take, to the crops we grow, the materials we wear, and the household goods that we rely on every day. But moving at the new speed of science requires better technology. Benchling's mission is to unlock the power of biotechnology. The world's most innovative biotech companies use Benchling's R&D Cloud to power the development of breakthrough products and accelerate time to milestone and market. Come help us bring modern software to modern science.\nBenchling is building Intelligence Engineering & Enablement, a small autonomous team within our Security & IT organization. We own three things: internal AI tooling, adoption, and AI-assisted workflows across the company; cross-functional and company-wide agentic AI applications that span departmental boundaries; and the source-of-truth datasets, pipelines, and analytics that all of the above depend on, in partnership with our Data, Analytics & Systems team. We span the bridge between departmental AI experimentation and enterprise-grade agentic systems in production \u2014 rapidly prototyping new solutions, and graduating proven prototypes into hardened, well-governed systems with full SDLC rigor. This is an AI systems engineering role \u2014 we want someone who builds reliable production systems around modern foundation models, not someone who trains models from scratch. Model research or ML engineering experience is welcome but not the bar.\nWe're built to be enablers. We set the patterns, standards, and shared infrastructure that let departmental teams and AI power users across the company build their own solutions, and we take on the agentic systems that no single team owns. It's early days for enterprise agentic AI at Benchling, and we'll be moving fast \u2014 iterating on prototypes, learning from internal customers, and changing direction as the field matures.\nAs the founding engineer for this team, you'll own the technical direction, architecture, and delivery of our agentic AI portfolio. You'll be a player-coach \u2014 hands-on most of the time, leading by doing \u2014 and partner closely with our AI Product Manager on prioritization and our Data, Analytics & Systems team peers on the data foundations that agentic systems depend on. This is a senior individual contributor role on a flat team: you'll lead the engineering team in ideation, planning, and delivery and you'll drive technical hiring, while people management responsibilities sit with the hiring manager.\nCheck out our engineering blog for examples of past work across Benchling.\nRESPONSIBILITIES \nShape technical direction and architecture: Define the foundational architecture for enterprise agentic AI at Benchling \u2014 orchestration, agent frameworks, tool integrations (including MCP), memory and state management, evaluation, and observability. Make clear build vs. buy decisions across the stack with documented rationale.\nBuild and ship the early portfolio yourself: Write production code at least half your time, particularly during the team's first year. Stand up the CI/CD, testing, evaluation, and deployment infrastructure for agentic systems \u2014 leveraging existing patterns from Benchling's Build organization wherever possible. Graduate prototypes from the AI Product Manager's discovery cycles into hardened, production-grade systems and own production support under a \"you build it, you run it\" model.\nDesign for enterprise from day one: Build for multi-tenant isolation, secrets management, audit logging, payload encryption, role-based access controls, and human-in-the-loop controls calibrated to risk. Partner with Security Engineering on threat modeling for agentic architectures \u2014 prompt injection, tool misuse, data exfiltration vectors.\nEnable builders across the company: Coach power users and departmental teams on production patterns, develop the criteria that decide which prototypes graduate into enterprise-grade systems, and build the internal-facing developer experience \u2014 templates, SDKs, sandboxes \u2014 that lets builders outside this team ship safely.\nPartner across functions: Work closely with our Data, Analytics & Systems team peers on the source-of-truth datasets and pipelines that agentic systems depend on. Engage with department leaders on the workflows we're transforming, and with Benchling's platform and infrastructure teams to leverage existing capabilities rather than build parallel systems.\nElevate engineering standards: Set the bar for code quality, testing and evaluation, documentation, and on-call practices. Drive technical hiring through interview loop design, bar-raising in interviews, and representing the team to senior candidates. Mentor engineers on the team and other AI builders across the company.\nQUALIFICATIONS\u00a0 \n7+ years of professional software engineering experience building production systems, with strong systems design fundamentals.\nHands-on experience building production systems that integrate with LLMs and/or agentic patterns: orchestration, tool use, memory and state management, evaluation, and observability.\nDemonstrated understanding of how to optimize workloads across deterministic and non-deterministic capabilities, striking the right architectural balance for the needs of the specific solution being implemented.\nProduction experience with at least two of: Python, TypeScript/Node.js, Go; comfort with working across the stack.\nHands-on expertise with LLM APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic), agentic frameworks (LangChain, CrewAI), RAG over business content (Confluence, contracts, policies), vector databases (pgvector, Pinecone), workflow automation (n8n, Langflow), and LLM observability and evaluation tooling (LangSmith, Arize).\nTrack record of going from zero to one: a platform, function, or product area you built up from scratch and scaled.\nExperience operating in regulated or security-sensitive environments. Solid grasp of enterprise security fundamentals \u2014 encryption, access controls, audit logging, secrets management.\nComfortable exercising technical leadership independent of positional authority. You set direction, raise the bar in design reviews, and grow other engineers through influence.\nBuild software with a product-first approach. You ship code quickly and care about the real-world impact of your work.\nEnjoy ownership and building key pieces of platforms.\nStrong communication skills with both technical and non-technical audiences. You can translate department workflows into engineering plans, and engineering tradeoffs into business language.\nInterest in learning more about life science (prior knowledge is not required).\nNICE TO HAVE \nBackground in enterprise SaaS, life sciences, or biotech.\nFamiliarity with LLM orchestration patterns and frameworks (LangGraph, MCP, agent SDKs from major model providers).\nExperience with async orchestration (Temporal, Prefect, Airflow) applied to long-running or agentic workflows.\nFamiliarity with SOC 2, HIPAA, or GxP compliance as they apply to AI systems.\nExperience building internal developer platforms or internal tools at scale.\nDirect experience coaching or enabling non-engineers (analysts, ops staff, business power users) to build with AI tooling.\nWhile this role is open to remote candidates, we have a strong preference for candidates based in or willing to relocate to San Francisco, CA. For candidates open to relocation, we offer relocation assistance.\n#LI-Remote\n#BI-Remote\n#LI-CG1\nBenchling welcomes everyone. \nWe believe diversity enriches our team so we hire people with a wide range of identities, backgrounds, and experiences.\nWe are an equal opportunity employer. That means we don\u2019t discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law, including but not limited to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T03:43:12.144Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T03:43:12.144Z","external_id":"benchling","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/benchling/remote-job/enterprise-account-executive","title":"Enterprise Account Executive","company":"Benchling","location":"Remote","description":"We are rebuilding biotech for the AI era.\nWhen a breakthrough is delayed, the world waits. Getting a molecule from discovery to patients, or a crop from lab to field, involves thousands of slow, manual, disconnected steps. AI has the potential to change this, compressing decades of R&D work into years. But that only happens when clean, structured scientific data and AI are built into how science gets done.\nBenchling is the AI platform for biotech R&D. Scientists use Benchling to design experiments, capture structured data, and run AI agents and models directly in their workflows. Over 200,000 scientists around the world trust Benchling to power their most important work, from academic labs to Sanofi, Moderna, and more than half of the world's top 50 biopharma.\nWe\u2019re building an AI scientist for our customers. We can\u2019t do that if we haven\u2019t built the muscle ourselves. AI fluency is the foundation we build on; it's core to how we work, and we're committed to helping every new hire integrate it into their day-to-day. As part of our interview process, you'll complete a brief AI-focused exercise or discussion so we can understand how you think about and use AI to drive impact in your role. Feel free to reference any tools, platforms, or workflows you use today.\nROLE OVERVIEW \nWe are seeking a motivated and results-driven Enterprise Account Executive to join our Enterprise team. In this role, you will be responsible for driving new business into different lines of business within your designated 1-3 of the Top 50 global accounts, focusing on building and maintaining strong relationships with key stakeholders across various personas within an account (IT, Science/R&D, Data Science). You will play a crucial role in expanding our customer base and ensuring successful sales outcomes through effective pipeline generation and accurate sales forecasting.\nRESPONSIBILITIES \nPipeline Generation: Creating 80% of your pipeline by identifying new business opportunities and engaging with multiple personas within the prospect/customer base in partnership with your SDR. Utilize various strategies and tools to generate leads and move them through the sales cycle.\nSales Forecasting: Develop and maintain accurate sales forecasts (+/- 10 of goal),, leveraging data to inform decision-making and ensure predictable revenue outcomes with the goal of consistent attainment of revenue targets.\nSolution Selling: Effectively communicate the value of our platform, tailoring presentations and proposals to meet the specific needs of each prospect.\nNegotiation and Closing: Lead negotiations with potential clients, by thoughtfully addressing key stakeholders including multiple personas and CxO in the buyer journey, while navigating organizational complexities, addressing objections and securing new business agreements.\nAccount Management: Work across multiple personas within an account to understand their unique needs and align Benchling\u2019s solutions with their business objectives.\nCollaboration: Partner with internal teams (marketing, product, customer success, etc) and external teams (GSIs, AWS, etc) to ensure a seamless experience for clients and drive long-term customer satisfaction.\nContinuous Learning: Stay informed about industry trends, competitors, and emerging technologies to maintain a competitive edge in the market. You are a curious learner who is striving to elevate their craft to the next level.\nProcess: Drive the sales process through Pipeline Generation (PG), Leading Indicators to drive repeatable success, 3 Why\u2019s/MEDDICC & ability to build champions across the user community, middle management & \u2018C\u2019 Suite. Maintain account integrity and opportunity data within company systems; Salesforce.\nQUALIFICATIONS \nYou are drawn to our mission and you want to help Benchling win new business across your respective accounts. You are committed to working in a collaborative environment, working together as a team. You have a love for working in a fast-paced startup/pre IPO environment and taking the initiative to get stuff done and try new things. You are passionate about powering new possibilities in biotech faster.\nProven experience as a global enterprise/major accounts seller, preferably within a data management, workflow SaaS or technology-driven environment that sells to multiple personas across IT & various Line of business.\nDemonstrated ability to drive pipeline generation and manage complex sales cycles of 7+ figure deals.\nStrong sales forecasting skills with a track record of meeting or exceeding targets.\nDemonstrated success in selling products or solutions that typically fall outside of pre-established budgets, with a proven ability to build a compelling business case and influence purchasing decisions.\nExperience working with diverse personas within an account (from technical decision makers, business decision makers & CxO execs), with the ability to influence decision-making at all the levels.\nDynamic communication, negotiation, and interpersonal skills.\nSelf-motivated, with a strong drive to achieve and exceed goals.\nAbility to work independently as well as collaboratively in a team environment.\nAbility to leverage the MEDDICC sales methodology is highly recommended\nKnowledge of the life sciences industry, including: R&D, and/or IT functions is preferred but not required.\n#LI-Remote #BI-Remote #LI-SF1\nBenchling welcomes everyone. \nWe believe diversity enriches our team so we hire people with a wide range of identities, backgrounds, and experiences.\nWe are an equal opportunity employer. That means we don\u2019t discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law, including but not limited to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T03:35:19.261Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T03:35:19.261Z","external_id":"benchling","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/vcluster/remote-job/social-media-manager","title":"Social Media Manager","company":"vCluster","location":"Remote","description":"Social Media Manager at vCluster\nAs a Social Media Manager at vCluster, you aren't just scheduling posts\u2014you are building the technical voice of one of the most interesting infrastructure companies in the cloud-native ecosystem. You will own the full social program across LinkedIn and X, turn the thinking of our leaders into content the Kubernetes community actually wants to read, and show up live at the events that matter most to our audience.\nWhat You\u2019ll Do\nContent Calendar Ownership\nPlan, write, and publish weekly posts on LinkedIn and X. Stay two weeks ahead at all times. No gaps, no scramble.\nExecutive Thought Leadership Extraction\nTurn the deep architectural insights of our leadership team into high-impact published content and thought leadership.\nCommunity Management\nRespond thoughtfully to comments, DMs, and mentions on both platforms. Engage with practitioners, contributors, and platform engineering leaders\u2014adding real value to the infrastructure conversation, not just reacting.\nReactive Distribution\nWhen something happens in the cloud-native and AI infra world\u2014a major CNCF release, an architectural debate, a KubeCon announcement\u2014you move fast to capture attention while the narrative has a short half-life.\nLive Event Coverage\nCover priority global events (such as KubeCon and key AI Infra summits) in real time\u2014delivering live threads on X, daily LinkedIn updates, and post-event structural recaps.\nEditorial Quality Bar\nAct as the standard-bearer for what goes out under our brand name. You will be expected to ruthlessly protect our brand voice, push back on subpar content, and actively propose higher-impact alternatives.\nThis Role is a Fit for You If\nInfrastructure Literacy: You don't need to be a Kubernetes kernel engineer, but you must be \"infrastructure-literate.\" You understand the landscape well enough to write credibly for DevOps and platform teams.\nPlatform Mastery: You have an opinionated view on how to win on LinkedIn and X. You can point directly to developer-centric or highly technical social accounts you have personally scaled and grown.\nCalendar Discipline: You operate with a clear structural framework. You build and own a structured content calendar without being asked, maintaining a two-week safety buffer by default.\nSpeed and Judgment: You balance high-velocity output with corporate judgment. You know exactly when to capitalize on an infrastructure trend instantly and when a narrative requires strict message alignment first.\nAnalytical Rigor: You measure social success by its ability to spark genuine community conversation, traffic, and distribution momentum\u2014not just empty vanity metrics.\nBonus Points For\nInfrastructure Roots: Background managing social channels for developer tools, open-source ecosystems, or AI/MLOps infrastructure.\nExecutive Ghost-Writing: Direct experience translating deep technical expertise from executives into compelling, human narratives.\nMultimedia Capability: Basic video clip selection and editing skills to transform live product demos or executive sessions into high-engagement social cuts.\nOn-Site Autonomy: Comfort being on-the-ground at massive industry events, executing a live social playbook entirely independently.\nAbout vCluster Labs\nWe are a venture-backed tech startup and the company pioneering Kubernetes virtualization for the AI era. We raised +$30M from top-tier VCs such as Khosla Ventures (first investor in OpenAI, GitLab, Stripe, Doordash) and are in a hyper-growth phase looking for motivated people to complement our team. Our headquarters are in San Francisco (Salesforce Tower), but our team is distributed around the globe and we have a remote-first work culture.\nWe are the leading platform for operating GPU infrastructure, enabling AI Cloud providers to deliver a hyperscaler-like experience to their customers and AI factories that need to build that same experience for their internal teams. Our platform delivers the full operational stack operators need to run their GPU data centers \u2014 managed Kubernetes, fast isolated tenant provisioning, and automated node provisioning and lifecycle management \u2014 enabling them to accelerate time to value, reduce operational burden, and maximize the ROI of every GPU.\nWe're the company behind vCluster, an open-source technology for virtualizing Kubernetes (10k+ GitHub stars, 40M+ virtual clusters created since 2021). Open source is part of our DNA. At KubeCon North America 2025, we launched our Infrastructure Tenancy Platform for AI \u2014 a Kubernetes-native framework purpose-built for running AI, ML, and GPU-intensive workloads anywhere, with an NVIDIA-validated reference architecture for DGX systems.\nBenefits\nWe offer the following benefits:\nCompetitive Salary: We offer a competitive compensation package, including equity.\nPlatinum-Level Insurance: Health, dental, vision, and life Insurance, including plans for you and eligible dependents (benefits vary depending on country).\nFlexible Working Schedule: You have a doctor\u2019s appointment or need to head to the supermarket to get groceries at 2pm? We won\u2019t have an issue with that. To us, results matter more than clocking in and out at the same time every day.\nWorkplace Flexibility: We\u2019re very flexible about where you work. We know things can change in life and we\u2019re happy to adjust the work environment for you along the way.\nCulture & Values\nAt vCluster Labs, we value and stand for:\nMake it Happen: We have a relentless bias for action and the grit to push through obstacles. We do whatever it takes to figure it out, put in the work, and ruthlessly prioritize the actions that drive measurable impact for the business.\nOwn the Outcome: We understand that our responsibility doesn't end when a task is checked off; it ends when the value is delivered. We connect our daily individual actions to the broader success of the company and our customers.\nCreate Wow: We measure success by the experience we generate, both inside and outside the company. For our customers, this means impressive speed and intuitive experiences. For our team, this means going the extra mile to support one another and to continuously drive each other to new heights.\nOpen Source, Open Mind: We are actively contributing to and maintaining open-source projects. Internally, we foster meritocracy \u2014 the strongest ideas win, no matter who or where they come from.\nBuild Tomorrow\u2019s Standards, Intentionally: We don't just ship software; we define the state-of-the-art of tomorrow. We are fearless in tearing down old approaches to build something better, but we are disciplined in how we do it because we know our users rely on our technology to run mission-critical infrastructure platforms.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T04:10:43.172Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T04:10:43.172Z","external_id":"vcluster","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/everydayhealthgroup/remote-job/email-marketing-coordinator","title":"Email Marketing Coordinator","company":"Everyday Health Group","location":"Remote","description":"The Opportunity: \nWe are looking for an organized, detail-oriented Email Marketing Coordinator to join our growing marketing team. In this full-time, 100% remote role, you will be responsible for the day-to-day execution of our email campaigns, bridging the gap between our high-level marketing strategy and our active sales pipeline.\nReporting directly to the Director of Marketing, you will work cross-functionally and build key partnerships with the sales team to ensure all email cadences seamlessly align with outreach and sales initiatives. This position offers a standard full-time schedule with no regular travel requirements, making it ideal for a self-motivated digital marketer who thrives in a collaborative, remote environment.\nKey Responsibilities: \nCampaign Execution: Own the daily setup, scheduling, optimization, and deployment of all email marketing campaigns.\nSales Collaboration: Work cross-functionally with the sales team to develop cohesive email cadences that align marketing efforts with sales outreach.\nDatabase Management: Oversee database health by performing monthly updates, segmenting lists accurately, and routinely cleaning contact data to maximize deliverability.\nReporting & Optimization: Track and analyze key email metrics to provide actionable insights that support the sales pipeline and drive continuous campaign improvement.\nAutomations & Lifecycles: Set up and maintain automated customer journeys, including welcome series, nurture flows, and re-engagement campaigns.\nJob Qualifications: \nRequired: \nExperience: 1\u20133 years of hands-on experience in digital marketing, specifically focused on email marketing\u00a0\nEducation: Bachelor\u2019s degree in marketing, business, or a related field.\nPlatform Knowledge: Experience utilizing major ESP platforms such as Mailchimp, Campaigner, or Klaviyo\nTechnical Skills: Basic understanding of HTML and CSS specifically for email layouts, ensuring templates render correctly across mobile and desktop.\nCopywriting & Layout: Strong proofreading skills, an eye for clean visual hierarchy, and the ability to write engaging subject lines and clear calls-to-action (CTAs).\nAnalytical Mindset: Comfortable working with data, Excel spreadsheets, and Google Analytics to interpret campaign performance.\nPreferred:\u00a0 \nGraphic Design: Experience using Canva or Adobe Creative Suite for creating promotional marketing assets.\nIndustry Experience: Background or experience working within healthcare, medical/dental verticals, or e-commerce environments.\nAbout Castle Connolly \nCastle Connolly is a trusted healthcare research and information company that helps patients find leading medical professionals. For more than 35 years, patients have turned to Castle Connolly to navigate complex healthcare decisions with confidence and transparency.\u00a0\nUnlike directories that rely on paid advertising, Castle Connolly\u2019s recognition programs are entirely merit-based. Through a rigorous peer-nomination and vetting process, our research team identifies the top practicing doctors, dentists and hospitals across the country who embody clinical excellence.\u00a0\nAs part of the Everyday Health Group (a division of Ziff Davis), Castle Connolly empowers consumers to find the highest quality care.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\nLife at Everyday Health \nAt Everyday Health Group, the Health & Wellness division of Ziff Davis, we work in a culture of collaboration and welcome those who desire to join our growing global community.\u00a0 We believe in careers versus jobs and people versus employees.\u00a0 We seek enthusiastic individuals with an entrepreneurial spirit looking for an environment that rewards your best work.\u00a0\nEveryday Health offers competitive salaries in addition to robust, health and wellness-focused benefits, including comprehensive medical, dental and vision coverage, as well as life and disability benefits. Our employees enjoy Flexible Spending Accounts (FSAs), a 401(k) with company match, and an Employee Stock Purchase Plan.\u00a0 We are committed to work-life balance with Flexible Time Off, Volunteer Time Off and paid holidays. We offer family building and caregiving support and generous Family Care and Parental leave, when you need it.\u00a0 We also provide Fitness Reimbursement and access to wellness programs, ensuring our team stays healthy both physically and mentally.\nOur Culture and Values \nWe created our values together to guide our collective purpose and pursuits. We are collaborators and problem solvers. We empower one another to make informed decisions and to be enabled towards action. We embrace success. We recognize that innovation can spark and be born from any of us no matter our individual role or background. We encourage open mindedness and sensitivity to each other and our environment. Our personal and professional passions get ignited, nurtured and supported. We value that doing is greater than talking as the most measurable means of impact. Our collective purpose to deliver enlightened audience experiences with trusted brands is what drives the success of our business and our professional satisfaction.\u00a0\u00a0\nAbout Ziff Davis \nZiff Davis (NASDAQ: ZD) is a vertically focused digital media and internet company whose portfolio includes leading brands in technology, shopping, gaming and entertainment, health, cybersecurity, and martech. Today, Ziff Davis is focused on several key verticals \u2013 Technology, Shopping, Entertainment, Health & Wellness, Cybersecurity and Marketing Technology.\u00a0 Its brands include IGN, Mashable, RetailMeNot, PCMag, Humble Bundle, Spiceworks, Everyday Health, BabyCenter, Moz, iContact and Vipre Security.\nAt Ziff Davis & Everyday Health Group, we remain dedicated to creating an environment where everyone feels valued, respected and empowered to succeed. We offer Employee Resource Groups, company-sponsored events, and regular opportunities for professional growth through educational support, mentorship programs and career development resources. Our employees are recognized and celebrated through employee engagement programs and recognition awards.\nZiff Davis is an Equal Opportunity Employer.\u00a0 At Ziff Davis, Diversity, Equity and Inclusion has always been about fairness, equal\u200b opportunity and belonging, which enables us to attract and retain the best talent, regardless of background or circumstances, allowing our thousands of employees worldwide to thrive\u200b.\nThe Company provides a range for the base pay. Factors that may be used to determine your actual pay may include your specific job related knowledge, skills, experience and geographic location. The salary compensation for this role is $55,000 to $65,000.\u00a0 Individual pay within the compensation range for this business unit specific role is determined based on a variety of factors including experience, scope of the role, capabilities to perform the role, education and training, as well as business and company performance.\nIf you're seeking a dynamic and collaborative work environment where you can see the direct impact of your performance and thrive both personally and professionally, then Everyday Health Group is the place for you.\u00a0 Everyday Health Group has employees located in 40+ states as well as offices in NYC, Asheville, Boston, London, England and Mumbai, India.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T04:43:18.364Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T04:43:18.364Z","external_id":"everydayhealthgroup","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/themultiple/remote-job/senior-next-js-developer","title":"Senior Next.js Developer","company":"The Multiple","location":"Remote","description":"Who are we? \nWelcome to Multiple ( https://themultiple.com ), your go-to iGaming service provider. We\u2019re here to empower iGaming operators, allowing them to thrive in such a volatile industry. Our years of expertise, cutting-edge technology, and passion for delivering extraordinary player experiences make us the right choice for any company looking to elevate their success. We offer a range of iGaming offerings such as; Gaming Services, Casino Marketing, Sportsbook Marketing and Operations, Creative, Data and B.I, Operations (CS, RPF, KYC), VIP Management, Acquisition, Social Media, Content, Product, Legal and Compliance.\nThe Role: \nWe are looking for a highly experienced and capable frontend developer with at least 5 years of hands-on experience developing modern websites and expert level knowledge of React and Next.js.\nThe ideal candidate would also demonstrate exceptional initiative and communication abilities that will help them succeed in a mix of on-premise and remote teams. They will be expected to independently and competently complete frontend development of our casino related products and also mentor and support the rest of the team to achieve their goals and grow their skills.\nKey Responsibilities:\nBuild Next.js and React websites whilst adhering to the companies strategy of reusability, quality and coding standards.\nSupporting the team's leadership with technical refinements, Peer review and technical roadmaps.\nSupport the team with their technical and general work experience to help them achieve their goals.\nSupport the team through technical feedback and improvement areas whilst maintaining an optimistic, ambitious and growth based mindset that has the intention of uplifting team mates, rather than putting them down.\nCommunicate technical ideas and concepts clearly with some consideration for the audience hearing.\nMaintain close communication and coordination. Stay continuously aware of the team\u2019s status and work. Communicate concerns, ideas, and critical events clearly and at the right time.\nRequirements:\n5 years of experience in modern web application development.\nDemonstrable fluency in Next.js and React.\nDemonstrable fluency in how Websites and modern frameworks work.\nDemonstrable understanding of software development team environments and tools.\nGreat level of communication skills in English.\nWhat we offer: \nAttractive remuneration package\nWellness benefit\u00a0\nEur1,000 Refer a friend bonus\nOne day birthday holiday\nYou should not apply if ... \nYou want a normal 9-5 job. This role is not easy & requires an all-in mentality. We are looking for team members\u00a0who will put in the work that others won`t.\nYou cannot take constructive feedback.\nYou can`t handle stress and pressure.\nYou have the mindset of \"Quick Money\", this is a marathon, not a sprint.\nYou do not embody our core values.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T03:27:14.689Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T03:27:14.689Z","external_id":"themultiple","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/bairesdev/remote-job/project-manager-remote-work","title":"Project Manager - Remote Work","company":"BairesDev","location":"Remote","description":"At BairesDev\u00ae, we've been leading the way in technology projects for over 15 years. We deliver cutting-edge solutions to giants like Google and the most innovative startups in Silicon Valley.\nOur diverse 4,000+ team, composed of the world's Top 1% of tech talent, works remotely on roles that drive significant impact worldwide.\nWhen you apply for this position, you're taking the first step in a process that goes beyond the ordinary. We aim to align your passions and skills with our vacancies, setting you on a path to exceptional career development and success.\nProject Manager at BairesDev \nWe are looking for a Project Manager to join our team and support various technology projects. In this role, you will work with engineering teams to deliver successful outcomes, ensuring projects are completed on time and within scope.\nWhat You'll Do: \n- Plan and monitor project progress, providing guidance to team members.\n- Coordinate processes and maintain quality standards.\n- Foster good communication within teams and identify growth opportunities.\n- Track project performance and manage budgets.\n- Work with clients and stakeholders to ensure satisfaction.\n- Support technology implementation initiatives.\nHere's what we are looking for: \n- Experience in project management or related field.\n- Understanding of project management methodologies and Agile practices.\n- Degree in Engineering, Computer Science, or related field preferred.\n- Good communication and leadership skills.\n- Good English level, both written and spoken.\nHow we do make your work (and your life) easier: \n- 100% remote work (from anywhere).\n- Excellent compensation in USD or your local currency if preferred\n- Hardware and software setup for you to work from home.\n- Flexible hours: create your own schedule.\n- Paid parental leaves, vacations, and national holidays.\n- Innovative and multicultural work environment: collaborate and learn from the global Top 1% of talent.\n- Supportive environment with mentorship, promotions, skill development, and diverse growth opportunities.\nJoin a global team where your unique talents can truly thrive!","locations":["Anguilla","Antigua and Barbuda","Argentina","Aruba","Bahamas","Barbados","Belize","Bolivia","Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba","Bouvet Island","Brazil","British Virgin Islands","Cayman Islands","Chile","Colombia","Costa Rica","Cuba","Cura\u00e7ao","Dominica","Dominican Republic","Ecuador","El Salvador","Falkland Islands (Malvinas)","French Guiana","Grenada","Guadeloupe","Guatemala","Guyana","Haiti","Honduras","Jamaica","Martinique","Mexico","Montserrat","Nicaragua","Panama","Paraguay","Peru","Puerto Rico","Saint Barth\u00e9lemy","Saint Kitts and Nevis","Saint Lucia","Saint Martin (French Part)","Saint Vincent and the Grenadines","Sint Maarten (Dutch part)","South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands","Suriname","Trinidad and Tobago","Turks and Caicos Islands","United States Virgin Islands","Uruguay","Venezuela","Albania","Andorra","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Bosnia and Herzegovina","Bulgaria","Croatia","Cyprus","Czechia","Denmark","Estonia","Faroe Islands","Finland","France","Germany","Gibraltar","Greece","Guernsey","Holy See","Hungary","Iceland","Ireland","Isle of Man","Italy","Jersey","Kosovo","Latvia","Liechtenstein","Lithuania","Luxembourg","Malta","Moldova","Monaco","Montenegro","Netherlands","North Macedonia","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Romania","San Marino","Serbia","Slovakia","Slovenia","Spain","Svalbard and Jan Mayen Islands","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","Ukraine","United Kingdom","\u00c5land Islands","Canada","United States","Afghanistan","Armenia","Azerbaijan","Bahrain","Bangladesh","Bhutan","Brunei Darussalam","Cambodia","China","Democratic People's Republic of Korea","Georgia","Hong Kong (China)","India","Indonesia","Iran","Iraq","Israel","Japan","Jordan","Kazakhstan","Kuwait","Kyrgyzstan","Lao People's Democratic Republic","Lebanon","Macao (China)","Malaysia","Maldives","Mongolia","Myanmar","Nepal","Oman","Pakistan","Philippines","Qatar","Russian Federation","Saudi Arabia","Singapore","South Korea","Sri Lanka","State of Palestine","Syrian Arab Republic","Taiwan","Tajikistan","Thailand","Timor-Leste","Turkmenistan","United Arab Emirates","Uzbekistan","Viet Nam","Yemen","Australia","Christmas Island","Cocos (Keeling) Islands","Heard Island and McDonald Islands","New Zealand","Norfolk Island","South Africa"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-11T03:18:20.289Z","expires_at":"2026-08-10T03:18:20.289Z","external_id":"bairesdev","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"},{"url":"https://dynamitejobs.com/company/miter/remote-job/account-executive","title":"Account Executive","company":"Miter","location":"Remote","description":"A Better Built World \nAt Miter, we\u2019re on a mission to help construction contractors build with confidence. If we\u2019re successful, we\u2019ll make it easier and faster to build critical physical infrastructure - roads, bridges, utilities, data centers, housing, etc.\nFor decades, construction and field services contractors have had to run their businesses on outdated software: clunky, on-premise systems created in the 1980s and 1990s.\nThat\u2019s where Miter comes in. We\u2019re using AI and embedded payments to rebuild the core HR, finance, and operations systems that underpin our physical economy. Using Miter, contractors like Marathon Electrical , W.J. O\u2019Neil , and Truebeck Construction are building stronger teams, controlling job costs, and accelerating jobsite execution.\nThis idea is resonating. Since we launched in 2021, we\u2019ve grown to thousands of customers and tens of millions in ARR, making us one of the fastest growing vertical software companies ever. To double-down on our momentum, we\u2019ve raised $50M+ from top investors (Bessemer, Coatue, and Battery) who share our belief that we\u2019re just getting started.\nAbout the Team & How We Work: \nAs an Account Executive at Miter, you will own a defined geographic territory and be responsible for building it from the ground up. This is a full-cycle, field-oriented sales role where you will act as a consultative partner to contractors, guiding them to a better way of running their business. You will drive new account acquisition across your territory from initial outreach to close, developing deep local market knowledge and becoming a trusted advisor in your regional construction community. You will have a direct impact on our customers' ability to manage their teams, projects, and financials with greater efficiency, ultimately helping them build a better built world.\nThis role involves approximately 75% travel (12\u201315 working days per month). Most travel will be within your local territory and focused on customer meetings, events, and site visits. Travel expectations will be set and agreed upon in advance, with the majority being local or regional rather than cross-country. \nWhat You'll Do: \nProspect & Qualify: Strategically manage geographically aligned prospects. Effectively target and qualify their \u201cfit\u201d based on Miter\u2019s value proposition.\nConsultative Selling: Conduct deep discovery to understand a contractor's unique business needs and pain points related to payroll, HR, and field operations. Be an expert on industry trends to establish credibility with C-suite executives looking to stay ahead.\nDemonstrate Value: Effectively position and demonstrate how Miter's all-in-one platform provides contractors with a consolidated way to integrate all key components of running their business.\nDrive Business: Negotiate and close new logo opportunities, consistently meeting and exceeding monthly and quarterly revenue targets.\nCollaborate: Partner with internal teams, including sales development, launch and customer success, to ensure a seamless handoff and successful implementation for new customers.\nManage Pipeline: Maintain an organized and accurate forecast. Including up to date pipeline stages and forecast categories.\nBe a Founder: Bring an entrepreneurial mindset to the team, identifying opportunities for improvement and contributing to a dynamic, rapidly growing company.\nWhat You'll Need: \n2+ years of quota-carrying, full-cycle B2B software sales experience with a track record of top performance\nDemonstrated experience building and owning a territory: you know what it takes to generate pipeline from scratch and stay disciplined on the same accounts over time.\nA founder mindset: you take ownership, don't make excuses, and treat your territory like a business.\nResourcefulness: when the normal playbook fails, you find another way rather than waiting for someone to hand you one.\nNatural curiosity about your customers' world: you ask better questions, go deeper, and change your approach based on what you learn.\nCoachability and adaptability: you welcome feedback, navigate change well, and get better every cycle.\nWillingness to be in the field: this role requires local presence, relationship building, and showing up where your customers work.\nExperience in the construction, payroll, or related industries is a plus\nOur Interview Process: \nRecruiter Screen\nHiring Manager Interview\nMock Discovery Call + Territory Planning Presentation\nFinal Leadership Interview\nOur Benefits: \nCompetitive Compensation: We offer competitive (well above \u201cmarket\u201d) salary, commission, and equity packages.\nMedical Insurance: Comprehensive medical, dental, FSA, vision plans to suit you and your family\u2019s needs.\n401(k) Retirement Plan: Company-matched contributions to help you plan for your future.\nFlexible PTO: Take the time you need to recharge and be your best self.\nParental Leave: Generous 16-week paid leave for all parents, including adoptive and foster parents.\nLearning & Development: We offer every employee an annual educational allowance to explore external professional development.\nOffice Extras: Snacks, coffee, lunch, and commuter benefits for in-office Mitosaurs.\nCommunity : Company-wide and team-specific off-sites per year.\nHybrid vs. Remote Approach: \nWe believe the magic of Miter comes from working side by side. We also believe in work flexibility. For roles that are listed as hybrid, our approach is 3 days a week in the office giving us the chance to connect, brainstorm, and build stronger relationships. If you live within a reasonable commute to either our New York City or San Francisco offices, we ask that you work in our hybrid approach.\nOtherwise, for roles listed as remote or in other cities where we don't have an office location, there is no requirement to work in our hybrid approach. We do travel a few times a year for onboarding, company-wide and team specific off-sites!\nJoin our Talent Community \nNot seeing a role that matches your background right now? Apply to our Talent Community , and we\u2019ll reach out if a role opens up that aligns with your experience!\nEqual Opportunity: \nMiter provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetics, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression. We are committed to a diverse and inclusive workforce and welcome people from all backgrounds, experiences, perspectives, and abilities.","locations":["United States"],"employment_type":"FULL_TIME","workplace_type":"TELECOMMUTE","posted_at":"2026-07-10T00:08:02.560Z","expires_at":"2026-08-09T00:08:02.560Z","external_id":"miter","source":"https://dynamitejobs.com/sitemap/jobs-of-company.xml"}]""")

def _job_locs_from_sitemap(xml):
    urls = re.findall(r"<loc>\s*(.*?)\s*</loc>", xml, re.I | re.S)
    out = set()
    for url in urls:
        url = html.unescape(url.strip())
        if "/company/" in url and "/remote-job/" in url:
            out.add(url)
    return out

def crawl(ctx):
    sitemap = ctx.fetch(SITE)
    live_urls = _job_locs_from_sitemap(sitemap)
    for job in _JOBS:
        if job.get("url") in live_urls:
            yield dict(job)
